PVD("afghanistan_ndp_2008-2013",{"docs":["","AFG NDS 2008 2013"],"s":{"1":[[1,"38","4","Municipal Urban Development Capacity Strengthening","strengthened municipal capacity to manage urban development and deliver services",""],[1,"38","4","Urban Coordination and Monitoring System","improved institutional coordination and moni- toring of key urban indicators",""],[1,"38","5","Urban Governance Decentralization and Urban Development Strategy","More is now being done under the ANDS to devolve authority to municipalities.",""],[1,"128","10","Urban Service and Infrastructure Improvement","The management of urban areas will be improved through the devolution of authority and responsibility to municipalities in ways that improve urban infrastructure and services, reduce urban poverty and allow urban residents to live safe, healthy and productive lives and cities to grow and prosper.",""],[1,"128","10","Private Investment Promotion for Urban Development","The ANDS strategic vision and goal for urban development sector is to ensure increased access to improved services, and affordable shelter while promoting sustainable economic development as part of efforts to reduce urban poverty through encouragement of private investment.",""],[1,"128","10","Urban Employment and Livelihoods Support","Improving the urban environment, the supply of urban services, providing employment opportunities, utilizing the potential resources and improving the livelihoods of the population will lead to improvements in security.",""],[1,"129","1","Municipal Capacity Strengthening for Urban Development and Service Delivery","Municipal Governments will have strengthened capacity to manage urban development and to ensure that municipal services are delivered effectively, efficiently and transparently;",""],[1,"129","9","Dehsabz City Development Authority","The Dehsabz City Development Authority has been established to facilitate the development of new city housing for up to 3 million people north of Kabul.",""],[1,"129","11","Regional and City Development Planning","strategic development plans are being prepared for 7 regional cities, while a city development plan for three major cities (Mazar, Jalalabad, Kabul) and existing-Kabul plan is due for completion by mid 2008.",""],[1,"129","12","National Urban Program","Urban policy: initiatives include a comprehensive National Urban Program (NUP)",""],[1,"129","13","Institutional Reform and Capacity Strengthening in Urban Development Institutions","Institutional reforms within MoUD, KM & IDLG (established in 2007) continue, along with investments in strengthening institutional capacity.","MoUD | KM | IDLG"],[1,"130","15","National Urban Policy Reform","The key to the urban sector development strategy is a national urban policy that decentralizes decision making to the local level, encourages participatory processes based on urban community councils or other neighborhood organizations, adopts a market based approach that encourages private sector activity and that establishes a regulatory framework focused narrowly on environmental protection and the rationalization of land use.",""],[1,"130","16","Urban Governance Restructuring and City Planning Initiative","The Ministry and Municipalities will be restructured and jointly work to prepare city action strategies and structure plans for Kabul and the 34 major urban areas, with special attention to local area plans for selected, fast growing areas, strengthen urban and municipal governance, finance and management.","The Ministry and Municipalities"],[1,"130","16","Participatory Municipal Governance Mechanism","This involves establishing an enabling environment where stakeholders participate in municipal elections and residents can have a say in policy formulation and the design of implementation activities.",""],[1,"130","17","Revenue Generation Capacity and Budget Management Reform","Steps will be taken to increase revenue generation capacity and improve management by upgrading accounting and budgetary practices and linking the capital budget to the planning process.",""],[1,"130","17","Revenue Base Review and Revenue Improvement Action Plans","Review existing revenue base and assets and develop action plans for revenue improvement plans to include widening revenue base, improved collection rates, user charges, co-",""],[1,"131","1","Local Revenue Mobilization for Urban Services","Develop mechanisms to increase local revenues to finance part of the costs of improved urban service.",""],[1,"131","1","Public-Private and NGO Partnerships for Urban Service Delivery","Promote public partnerships with the private sector and NGOs to more efficiently provide urban services or meet urban needs.",""],[1,"131","1","Public Finance and Expenditure Management Law Enactment","The draft Public Finance and Ex- penditure Management Law will be enacted.",""],[1,"131","2","National Spatial Development Plan","The Government will prepare a national spatial development plan.",""],[1,"244","3","Legislative Review for Regularization and Basic Infrastructure Investment Program","Review of relevant legislation to facilitate regularization, followed by program of investments in basic infrastructure and public facilities with drawing from best practices in the region",""],[1,"244","6","Administrative Process Reform and Urban Development Monitoring and Evaluation System","Institutional reform and enforcement of administrative processes; introduction of effective systems of monitoring and evaluation for the implementation phase for transparent urban development processes",""],[1,"244","16","Land and Housing Development Investment and Housing Finance Systems","Investments by public and private sector in land and housing development, coupled with development of systems of housing finance",""],[1,"244","21","Land Tenure Regularization for Informal Settlements","Provide land tenure to the inhabitants in informal settlements",""],[1,"244","23","Dehsabz New City Development and Kabul Business Hub Initiative","Establish Dehsabz New City and turn Kabul into a business hub of the surrounding regions",""],[1,"244","25","Policy, Regulation, and Implementation Plan Review and Update","Review and update policies, regulations and implementation plans that will consider crosscutting issues gender, environment, ant-corruption and counter narcotics.",""],[1,"244","30","HRM and Finance Computerization","Computerize HRM/Finance and program activities to strengthen Human Re-",""],[1,"245","7","Urban Data Collection Unit","Establish Uni- urban Data collection unit (encourage disaggregated data col- lection)",""],[1,"245","9","Monitoring, Evaluation, and Re-planning Capacity Building","Training and capacity building of the key staff in the process of monitoring and evaluation and re-planning",""],[1,"245","16","National Settlement and Regional Strategic Planning Framework","Develop national settlement and regional strategic plans and through them provide a framework for balanced urbanization and greater regional coher- ence, from which the border cities of Afghanistan and neighboring countries shall benefit.",""],[1,"275","24","Municipal Capacity Strengthening for Urban Service Delivery","By March 2011, Municipal Governments will have strengthened capacity to manage urban development and to ensure that municipal services are delivered effectively, efficiently and transparently;",""],[1,"276","14","Mortgage System Implementation","The process is underway to implement mort- gage system",""],[1,"276","19","Municipal Governance and Urban Service Delivery Reform","Municipalities will be operating under updated laws and polices and effectively and transparently delivering urban services, with better customer service system",""]],"2":[[1,"98","8","Electronic Government Applications Rollout","By Jaddi 1387 (end-2008), cross-cutting electronic govern- ment applications will be launched to reduce corruption and increase effi- ciency.",""],[1,"98","8","Public Complaints Mechanism","By Jaddi 1387 (end-2008), the Government will establish and imple- ment a public complaints mechanism.",""],[1,"98","8","Right to Information Legal Framework","By Jaddi 1389 (end-2010), the legal frame- work required for exercising this right provided under the constitution will be put in place, distributed to all judicial and legislative institutions, and made available to the public and, imple- mented.",""],[1,"98","8","Anti-Corruption and Drug-Trafficking Enforcement","By Jaddi 1389 (end-2010), the Govern- ment will increase the number of arrests and prosecutions of traffickers and cor- rupt officials, and improve its informa- tion base concerning those involved in the drugs trade, with a view to enhanc- ing the selection system for national and sub-national public appointments.",""],[1,"98","8","Asset Declaration Requirement for Senior Public Officials","Pub- lic officials elected and appointed to high positions will be required to declare their asset before taking charge of their",""],[1,"98","10","Asset Declaration Requirement for Senior Public Officials","Public officials elected and appointed to high positions will be required to declare their assets before taking office and on a periodical basis during their tenure in public office.",""],[1,"98","10","Counter-Narcotics Unit Support in Key Ministries","The Government will establish and support the existing Counter Narcotics units in key ministries and will establish coordination mechanisms for a coor- dinated Government response.",""],[1,"98","12","Training and Study Tours for Sub-National Governance Officials","The Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG) will collaborate with the LOGOTRI with a view to organizing training and study tours of Afghan sub-national governance policy makers and Afghan officials at LOGOTRI member-institutions in Asia and the Pacific.","Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG)"],[1,"98","13","National Assembly CN Training Programme","The National Assembly will organize trainings for its members on CN issues, in particular the CN Law.",""],[1,"99","1","Anti-Corruption Leadership and Monitoring Mechanism","The Government will establish a single leadership and monitoring within government and parliament on anticorruption process and implementation of UNCAC.",""],[1,"99","1","Anti-Corruption Institutional Rationalization and Strengthening","Institutional arrangements within the Government to fight corruption will be rationalized and strengthened.",""],[1,"99","1","Anti-Corruption Road Map Implementation","The actions contained in the Anti Corruption Road Map will remain priority actions for the Government in 2008 and beyond.",""],[1,"99","1","Implementation of Inter-Institutional Commission Recommendations","The Government will take steps contained in the report of Inter-Institutional Commission.",""],[1,"99","2","Youth Group Counter-Narcotics Awareness Integration","Awareness of CN issues will be incorporated into the programs developed for youth groups.",""],[1,"99","2","Provincial Counter-Narcotics Initiative","Provincial level counter narcotic initiatives will be implemented with the cooperation of the Governors and the Provincial Council Members",""],[1,"99","4","Civil Servant Training and Development Policy","The aim of T & D policy shall be to: Provide job-related education, training, and development opportunities for all Civil Servants so that they may perform their jobs competently and happily.",""],[1,"257","13","Anti-Corruption Mainstreaming in Administrative Reform Programs","To mainstream into all administrative reform programs measures required to address the systems and incentives promoting anti-corruption within the public administration system and Development Activities.",""],[1,"259","5","Line Ministry Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen line ministries capacities at national and sub-national levels",""],[1,"266","11","Public Management Capacity Strengthening and Anti-Corruption Measures","Strengthened public management capacity to develop policy and negotiate agreements and strengthen ant-corruption measures",""],[1,"269","12","Public Sector Workforce Training Policy","By Jaddi 1392 (end-2013), a training policy for the entire public sector work- force shall be developed and implemented.",""],[1,"269","15","Civil Service Merit-Based Appointment and Performance Review Reform","By March 2011, in furtherance of the work of the Civil Service Commission, merit-based appointments, vetting procedures and performance-based re- views will be undertaken for civil service positions at all levels of govern- ment",""]],"3":[[1,"11","2","Continuous Monitoring and Evaluation for ANDS","Sustained fiscal support and continuous evaluation and monitoring are essential now to meet the challenges ahead related to ANDS implementation.",""],[1,"11","2","Decisive Government Action for ANDS Goals","The Afghan Government with support from the international community must act decisively, strategically, and with an absolute commit- ment to the ANDS goals and vision.",""],[1,"33","1","National Development Strategy Implementation, Monitoring, and Evaluation Framework","The ANDS establishes the Government's strategy and defines the policies, pro- grams and projects that will be implemented over the next five years and the means for ef- fectively implementing, monitoring and evalu- ating these actions.",""],[1,"33","1","Adaptive Living Strategy Framework","While focus of the ANDS is on the next five years, it will continue to adjust to changing cir- cumstances - it is intended to be a 'living document'.",""],[1,"35","1","Inter-Ministerial Coordination Committees","Considerable attention has therefore been given to developing better coordination between ministries through Inter-Ministerial Committees.",""],[1,"89","2","Public Administration Reform Acceleration","The main priorities for the governance sector are (i) to increase the pace and quality of public administration reform;",""],[1,"91","2","Public Administration Pay and Grading Reform","Public administration reform will focus on pay and grading reforms to increase competitive recruitment, hiring of a trained and capable public sector workforce, strengthening merit based appointments, conducting performance-based reviews.",""],[1,"91","9","Single National Identity Document Issuance","To enhance public accountability and trans- parency a single national identity docu- ment will be issued.",""],[1,"91","13","Sub-national Public Administration Reform","Public administration will be reformed at the sub-national level and the capacity of the public sector workforce at sub-national level strengthened.","Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG)"],[1,"91","14","Government Office Facilities Review and Upgrade","Review and assessment of the facilities in all government offices will be undertaken and appropriate facilities provided.",""],[1,"91","15","Government Information Flow Enhancement","There will be enhanced flow of information between all government entities related to national policy, strategy and national budget procedures.",""],[1,"93","14","Administrative Capacity Enhancement","enhancing admin- istrative capacity;",""],[1,"98","7","Sub-national Administration Service Delivery Reform","By end-1389 (20 March 2011), the Government will build institutional and administrative capabilities in provincial, district and, municipal administrations to manage basic service delivery through reforming organizational structures, stream- lining management processes, de- veloping essential skills and knowl- edge of civil servants.",""],[1,"98","7","Public Sector Training Policy","A training policy for entire public sector workforce will be developed and implemented.",""],[1,"98","7","Public Sector Workforce Training Arrangements","Institutional arrangements shall be put in place to ensure that each member of the workforce gets trained at least once in two years in organization specific and job specific training along with",""],[1,"170","9","Administrative Simplification and Anti-Corruption Reform","Removal of nuisance procedures, licenses and taxes will reduce corruption.",""],[1,"170","9","Predictable Public Administration Reform","Making administration more predictable so that laws are followed and administrative discretion is reduced will also help.",""],[1,"175","2","Mainstreaming Process for Public Administration, Financial Management, and Legal Reform","The mainstreaming process will be driven pri- marily by the three complementary and inter- dependent areas of public administration, fi- nancial management and legal reform:",""],[1,"175","3","Public Sector Management Improvement","Improving Public Sector Management: aimed at the creation and consolidation of a motivated, knowledgeable, skilled, effi- cient and effective public service.",""],[1,"221","14","Public Sector Workforce Training and Capacity Building","Oversee/Implement/Monitor Training and Capacity Building of Public Sector Workforce",""],[1,"221","16","Merit-Based Civil Service Recruitment","Appoint civil servants based on Merit",""],[1,"221","26","E-Government Applications Launch","Launch E-Government Applications",""],[1,"222","45","Civil Registry and Single National Identity Document System","Establish civil registry with a single national identity document",""],[1,"223","17","Sub-National Governance Policy Development","Develop Sub National Governance Policy",""],[1,"223","37","Provincial Planning and Provincial Budgeting Institutionalization","Instutionalize Provincial Planning and Provincial Budgeting",""],[1,"238","8","Anti-Corruption Mainstreaming in Administrative Reform Programs","To mainstream into all administrative reform programs measures required to address the systems and incentives promoting anti-corruption within the public administration system and Development Activities.",""],[1,"242","2","External Scrutiny System Establishment","Establishing an effective external scrutiny system;",""],[1,"242","2","Anti-Corruption Training for Responsible Agencies","Targeted anti corruption training for the responsible anti-corruption agencies to effectively investigate and report on corruption;",""],[1,"242","2","Code of Conduct and Enforcement Mechanism Development","Developing code of conducts and enforcement mechanisms",""],[1,"242","2","Civil Service Wage Increase","Increasing wages of the civil service",""],[1,"242","21","Public Sector Salary Increase Linked to Capacity Growth","Increase public sector salaries in tandem with increases in capacity",""],[1,"249","7","Chief Information Officer Culture Development in Government","Develop CIO (Chief Information Officer) culture in government organizations",""],[1,"249","12","Government Service ICT Streamlining and Automation Reform","Reduce corruption by reviewing all government services and making recommendations for the adoption of ICT to streamline and automate (for example, customs processing, procurement and licensing",""],[1,"250","2","National Data Centre","The electronic data of the government will be securely hosted and will be available to all entities upon request and level of access",""],[1,"250","3","National Data Centre for Cross-Cutting Issues","The National Data Centre will have information on crosscutting issues like anti-corruption, counter narcotics, and environment.",""],[1,"250","8","HRD Unit Strengthening and HRM Computerization","Strengthen HRD unit to oversee the HR and R&D issues, Computerize all HRM activities to strengthen Human resource management",""],[1,"250","11","Policy and Planning Support Unit Strengthening","Strengthen policy and planning support unit in the Ministry","the Ministry"],[1,"250","15","Anti-Corruption Mainstreaming in Administrative Reform Programs","To mainstream into all administrative reform programs measures required to address the systems and incentives promoting anti-corruption within the public administration system and Development Activities.",""],[1,"252","3","Sustainable Transparent and Accountable Financial Management System","Create a sustainable, transparent and accountable financial management system at central, provincial and district level",""],[1,"252","4","Computerized Human Resource Management System","Create a computerized HRM system to strengthen human resource manage- ment",""],[1,"252","6","Sector Administrative Unit Compliance Monitoring","Monitor the activities of sector administrative units to confirm adherence to ethical standards, professional service and staff integrity, based upon relevant laws, codes of conduct and standardized procedures and protocols",""],[1,"252","8","Public Administration Position Regularization and Pay Grading","Implement PRR and Pay and Grading of all approved positions within the min- istry including teaching staff",""],[1,"253","19","Computerized Human Resource Management System","Create a computerized HRM system to strengthen human resource manage- ment",""],[1,"253","21","Monitoring of Sector Administrative Units for Ethical Compliance","Monitor the activities of sector administrative units to confirm adherence to ethical standards, professional service and staff integrity, based upon relevant laws, codes of conduct and standardized procedures and protocols",""]],"4":[[1,"168","17","Counter-Narcotics Strategic Actions","Strategic actions related to counter- narcotics include the: implementation",""],[1,"173","2","National Drug Control Strategy Implementation Acceleration","the Government is moving immediately to accelerate and improve strategy implementa- tion through:",""],[1,"173","4","Counter-Narcotics Trust Fund Restructuring and Reform","Restructure and reform of the Counter- Narcotics Trust Fund (CNTF)",""],[1,"173","9","Mainstreaming CN into Government Policies","Mainstreaming CN into all government policies.",""],[1,"173","10","Cross-Sector Counter Narcotics Responsibility Framework","Counter Narcotics is a core crosscutting issue in the ANDS and will be the responsibility of all sectors; while the MCN will take the leadership","MCN"],[1,"173","11","Narcotics Elimination and Drug Control Strategy","The goal is to ensure a rapid and sustain- able decrease in cultivation, production, traf- ficking and consumption of illicit drugs with a view to complete and sustainable elimination of narcotics by providing a conducive devel- opment environment and opportunities while taking requisite direct action.",""],[1,"173","12","Provincial Counter-Narcotics Planning and Coordination Framework","The implementation of the strategy will rely on a provincial based approach to counter- narcotics, which will provide the provinces requisite responsibility for developing counter narcotics action-plans aligned with the Provin- cial Development Plans (PDPs).",""],[1,"173","12","Local Counter-Narcotics Implementation Planning Process","Governors will be consulted in developing local CN im- plementation plans ultimately consolidated and prioritized into a national implementation plan.",""],[1,"173","12","National Counter-Narcotics Priority Identification and Provincial Plan Support","At the national level the Minis- try of Counter Narcotics, in conjunction with provincial Governors, line ministries, the IDLG, and ANDS must help identify provincial CN priorities and support the design of compre- hensive provincial counter narcotics plans in line with Provincial Development Plans (PDPs) within the framework of the national budget.","Ministry of Counter Narcotics"],[1,"174","4","Adequate Financing for CNTF and Alternative Development Program Alignment","Adequate financing of CNTF and adjust alternative development programs to the priorities of PDPs, subject to reform and improved functioning;",""],[1,"174","10","Counter-Narcotics Intelligence Sharing Improvement","Improve intelligence sharing on counter- narcotics activities;",""]],"5":[[1,"11","1","Inclusive National and Sub-national Consultation Process","To embrace 'Afghanization\" and ownership, the OSC facilitated inclusive and extensive consultations both at national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"27","4","Afghanistan National Development Strategy","the Government developed the Afghanistan National Development Strategy (ANDS) to clarify existing conditions, establish objectives and define the policies, programs and projects needed to achieve those objections.",""],[1,"27","4","Renewed and Upgraded UN Assistance Mission for Afghanistan Coordination","The international community made new pledges of financial and security assistance and set out to improve its coordination by renewing and upgrading the UN Assistance Mission for Afghanistan (UNAMA), headed by a Special Representative of the Secretary General with enhanced powers for coordination.",""],[1,"28","2","Priority-Setting Institutional Mechanisms","the ANDS aims to establish institutional mechanisms that will include the Afghan people, the Government, civil society and the international community in identifying priorities in an evolving environment.",""],[1,"43","3","National Budget Alignment with ANDS Sector Strategies","The National Budget is the central tool for implementing the ANDS.",""],[1,"43","3","Ministry Programme and Project Alignment Process","all line ministries will first develop or align their programs and projects with the ANDS Sector Strategies; sector program and projects will then be costed and re-prioritized against the medium-term budget ceilings.",""],[1,"43","3","ANDS Public Investment Program Preparation","the ANDS Public Investment Program (PIP) will be prepared to enable the full integration of the ANDS into the medium term budget in accordance with the MoF's on- going activities to introduce program budget- ing.",""],[1,"43","5","ANDS Oversight and Coordination Mechanism","The ANDS Oversight Committee (OSC), composed of senior ministers, will oversee and coordinate the overall ANDS implementation process.",""],[1,"43","5","Budget Integration and Costing of Line Ministry Programs","The MoF will play an important role by making sure that the program and projects of the line ministries are costed, prioritized and integrated into the National Budget.","MoF"],[1,"43","5","Operational Coordination of Line Ministries","Moreover, the Ministry of Economy will strengthen this mechanism by coordinating the work of the line ministries at the operational level.","Ministry of Economy"],[1,"43","5","Joint Government-Donor Coordination and Monitoring Board","The Joint Coordination and Monitoring Board will remain the highest Government-donor mechanism in charge of coordination and monitoring, which will cover not only the Afghanistan Compact but the entire ANDS.",""],[1,"46","26","Policy, Planning, and Budget Formulation Strengthening","Valu- able outcomes and lessons have been learned as part of this process, which are being used to strengthen the policy, planning and budget formulation.",""],[1,"47","13","Presidential Oversight Committee for ANDS Implementation","The Oversight Committee (OSC) was formed to oversee the economic, policy and strategic direction for the implementation and development of the ANDS.",""],[1,"47","13","Ministry and Agency Strategy Development under the Sector-Wide Approach","Within the frame- work of the various Consultative and Technical Working Groups, each Ministry and Agency developed its individual strat- egy, coordinated within the sector wide approach underpinning the ANDS.",""],[1,"47","14","Joint Coordination and Monitoring Board Coordination Mechanism","The Joint Coordination and Monitoring Board (JCMB) coordinates the efforts of all partners in the process, and reports the results to the President, the National Assembly, and the UN Secretary General as well as to the international community and the public.",""],[1,"49","10","Priority Project Mapping into the National Budget Process","These are being mapped into the national budget process.",""],[1,"50","1","Prioritized Project Alignment and Monitoring Mechanism","Prioritized projects will be aligned with ministries' national programs.",""],[1,"50","2","Priority Action Prioritization Process","The prioritization process will assist ministries with effective resource allocation and provincial projects highlighted as the most urgent should be seen as priority action by the ministries.",""],[1,"53","4","Integration of Lessons Learned into Policy, Planning, and Budgeting","Lessons learned have been formally integrated into the policy, planning and budgeting processes, including ongoing concerns about regional cooperation, conflict management, counter-narcotics, anti-corruption, gender, the environment and capacity building.",""],[1,"67","6","Fiscal Policy Alignment with Development Strategy Priorities","Fiscal policies will remain a central policy tool for macroeconomic stability, public resource allocation, and implementation of the development strategy - all of which are important ingredients for sustained robust economic growth.",""],[1,"78","5","ANDS-Based Medium-Term Fiscal Framework and Budget Prioritization","From 1387 (2008/09) onward the MTFF and the budget will be based on the prioritization established in the ANDS and the utilization of resources for the implementation of ANDS through the budget.",""],[1,"79","6","Medium-Term Fiscal Framework and Program-Based Budgeting","These are being built into the MTFF and the Ministry of Finance's program-based budgeting system focused on achieving the country's development needs.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"200","2","Inter-Ministerial Committees for ANDS Sector Strategy Oversight","17 Inter-Ministerial Committees (IMCs) will be established, each responsible for overseeing the implementation of an ANDS sector strategies.",""],[1,"200","4","Legislative Enabling Environment for National Development","The National Assembly will be responsible for legislating an enabling environment for security, economic growth and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"200","6","ANDS Oversight Committee Implementation Oversight Mechanism","The ANDS Oversight Committee as high level body comprised of senior ministers will over- see the implementation of the ANDS and re- port about the progress directly to the Presi- dent and the Cabinet.",""],[1,"200","10","Local Governance Coordination Mechanism","The Independent Department for Local Gov- ernance (IDLG), under the President's Office, will be responsible for the overall coordination of local governance and all provincial gover- nors will report to it on the progress of the im- plementation of the ANDS.","Independent Department for Local Governance (IDLG) | President's Office"],[1,"200","12","Joint Coordination and Monitoring Board","The Government and the international community have established the Joint Coordination and Monitoring Board (JCMB), with responsibility for overall strategic coordination and monitoring of the implementation of the Afghanistan Compact.",""],[1,"200","13","Joint Coordination and Monitoring Board Implementation Mechanism","This mechanism will be a very important implementation mechanism for ANDS because of its past experience, criticality and positioning.",""],[1,"201","1","Consultative Groups Aid Coordination Mechanism","Consultative Groups (CGs) will continue to play important role in coordinating the efforts of the Government and donors in implementa- tion of the development programs and projects.",""],[1,"201","2","Sector Working Groups Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","Working Groups (WGs) have been established for each sector, and where necessary are supported by sub-working groups.",""],[1,"201","2","Sector Program Development, Alignment, and Monitoring Forum","They will remain to be the key forum through which line ministries and international partners can develop programs, align efforts and monitor results.",""],[1,"201","3","Policy Action Group Coordination Mechanism","The Policy Action Group (PAG) will provide overall direction to key Afghan and interna- tional actors to ensure that the interdependence of security, governance and development ob- jectives guide operations and programs in or- der to achieve the conditions for basic service delivery, development programs and private sector-led growth, especially in conflict affected areas.",""],[1,"201","4","Provincial Development Committee Coordination Mechanism","At the sub-national level, the Provincial Development Committees (PDCs), chaired by the Governors, will ensure coordination within the provincial administration and with the donors, PRTs and civil society.",""],[1,"201","8","Integrated Approach Coordination and Capacity Strengthening","Implementation of the ANDS under the Inte- grated Approach will require synchronization of budgetary, cabinet, legislative, program and stabilization cycles.","Office of Administrative Affairs | Ministry of Parliamentary Affairs | Ministry of Finance | IARCSC | IDLG | NSC"]],"6":[[1,"56","1","National Risk and Vulnerability Assessment Survey","Ongoing data collection includes the planned 2007/08 NRVA survey (predominantly funded by the EC).",""],[1,"62","2","Poverty Data Collection and Analysis Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity for data collection and poverty analysis: institutional capacity for data collection and poverty analysis will need to improve in order to better inform policies for poverty reduction.",""],[1,"62","4","Mainstreaming Poverty Reduction Policy Implementation and Monitoring through Sector Strategies","Implementation and monitoring of the ANDS poverty reduction policies will be main- streamed through the sector strategies.",""],[1,"62","4","Separate Evaluation of ANDS Sector Poverty Reduction Policies","the evaluation of the overall ANDS sector policies for poverty reduction will be evaluated separately to inform policy makers about their effectiveness.",""],[1,"62","4","National Poverty Data Collection through NRVA","The NRVA will remain the main tool for data collection on matters of poverty.",""],[1,"62","4","Household Budget Survey Introduction and Poverty Data System Strengthening","the introduction of the household budget survey and strengthening of the CPI and national income data will also contribute to this understanding.",""],[1,"62","4","Census Survey for Poverty Analysis","The forthcoming Census Survey will play an important role in enhanc- ing the understanding of poverty.",""],[1,"62","4","Strengthening CSO Capacity for Poverty and Development Data Collection","The capacity of the CSO's for data collection of key poverty and development indicators will need to be strengthened.",""],[1,"62","4","Government Capacity Building for Poverty Analysis","the Government will continue to improve its own capacity to under- take poverty analysis within the CSO and other Government agencies.",""],[1,"91","10","National Census Completion and Publication","The national census will be completed and the results published.",""],[1,"91","10","National Economic and Poverty Baseline Establishment","National economic and poverty baselines will be established.",""],[1,"91","11","Village and Gozar Boundary Verification and Mapping Programme","Village and Gozar boundaries will be verified and mapping exercises will be undertaken.",""],[1,"205","3","National Statistical System Strengthening","The capacity of the CSO will be strengthened so that a meaningful statistical system be put in place for providing useful data on various macro-economic processes and important sectors.",""],[1,"205","3","Sectoral Operational Data Collection Strengthening","It is necessary for this purpose to strengthen the collection of operational data in various sectors through respective agencies.",""],[1,"205","3","Inter-Ministerial Data Collection Coordination","The CSO will coordinate data collection systems in various ministries and organizations.",""],[1,"205","5","Expansion of Multi-Purpose Household Surveys","The role of these surveys will be further expanded so that they can meet the immediate data needs of the other sectors.",""],[1,"205","5","Poverty and Social Outcome Monitoring System","To monitor the impact on poverty, the NRVA and the future household budget surveys will serve as the key source for monitoring for critical poverty and social outcome indicators and completion of the reports on poverty situation (see appendix III).",""],[1,"205","6","Sector Spending Monitoring and National Program Coordination Mechanism","Line departments will continue to collect sector relevant information to monitor the output and sectoral outcome of national spending through the ANDS.",""],[1,"205","7","Strengthening Provincial Offices for Disaggregated Monitoring and Reporting","The line ministries will strengthen their provincial offices to collect disaggregated data on all indicators to monitor progress on individual projects at provincial, district and village level.","line ministries"],[1,"205","7","Sub-national Monitoring, Support, and Reporting Mechanisms","The provincial offices and institutions of sub-national governance will utilize monitoring, support and reporting mechanisms to feed data to the line ministries which will assist in provincial budgeting, planning and monitoring of the overall implementation of the ANDS.","line ministries"],[1,"205","7","Provincial Council Reporting on ANDS Implementation","The Governor will report to the Provincial Councils on the progress of implementation of the sub-national ANDS priorities and other parts of the PDPs.",""],[1,"206","2","International Partner Support for Policy Analysis and Aid Dialogue","The Government will continue to request support from international partners in (a) developing analysis of the main obstacles to more rapid growth and poverty reduction; (b) discussing the quality, coverage and timeliness of key data, including possible final and intermediate indicators; (c) assessing the main policy issues confronting the Government in the macroeconomic, structural, and social areas, given the core objectives of promoting growth and reducing poverty; (d) assessing the current 'resource envelope' and, within this, the possible scale of expenditures for poverty reduction; and (e) discussing current levels and nature of external assistance, and prospects for increased aid over the medium-term.",""],[1,"206","9","Poverty and Vulnerability Survey and Monitoring System","The Government has developed poverty and vulnerability surveys largely based on income and consumption data, disaggregated by province, household, agro-economic zone, gender and household size, among other factors.",""],[1,"206","9","New Poverty Line Development","Against these a new poverty line has been developed.",""],[1,"206","9","Poverty Monitoring and Strategy Design Process","Figure 11.2 outlines the overall poverty monitoring and strategy design process undertaken in formulating and implementing the ANDS.",""],[1,"206","9","CMRS Decision-Support Information System","The CMRS will play a pivotal role in providing information to decision-makers as part of this process.",""]],"7":[[1,"102","2","Regional Cooperation on Trade, Transit, Power, and Labor Mobility","Afghanistan and its neighbors will achieve lower transit times through Afghanistan by means of cooperative border management and other multilateral or bilateral trade and transit agreements; Afghanistan will increase the amount of electricity available through bi-lateral power purchases; and Afghanistan, its neighbors and countries in the region will reach agreements to enable Afghanistan to import skilled labor, and to enable Afghans to seek work in the region and send remittances home.",""]],"8":[[1,"42","4","National Action Plan for Women","The National Action Plan for Women focuses on three main outcomes: (i) government entities embracing 'gender equality' in their employment, promotion, policy making and budgetary allocations;",""],[1,"90","7","National Action Plan for Women of Afghanistan","The National Action Plan for Women of Afghanistan is being implemented to establishing greater gender equality by eliminating discrimination, building of women's human capital and promoting their participation and leadership.",""],[1,"91","5","National Action Plan for Women's Rights Implementation","Fulfillment of the national action plan for women's rights will be implemented",""],[1,"91","5","Affirmative Action Programs for Women","affirmative action programs made available to women",""],[1,"98","3","Implementation of the National Action Plan for Women in Afghanistan","The Government will fully implement the National Action Plan for Women in Afghanistan",""],[1,"175","14","Gender Equity Cross-Cutting Strategy","The Gender Equity Cross Cutting Strategy is the basis for the ANDS to address and reverse women's historical disadvantage.",""],[1,"176","1","Gender Mainstreaming Capacity Development for Ministries and Government Agencies","Three immediate goals have been prioritized, namely: (iii) to develop basic institutional capacities of ministries and government agencies on gender mainstreaming.",""],[1,"176","6","Strengthening of the Ministry of Women's Affairs as Lead Ministry for Women's Advancement","MoWA's status as lead ministry for women's advancement will be maintained and strengthened.","MoWA"],[1,"176","6","Gender Equity Measures in Government Entities","All government entities will: (i) foster a work environment that supports egalitarian relationships between women and men; (ii) establish internal enabling mechanisms for gender equity; and (iii) support women's shuras.",""],[1,"176","6","Gender Mainstreaming Capacity Support for ANDS Working Groups","ANDS consultative and working groups will be provided with capacity to pursue gender mainstreaming.",""],[1,"176","6","Gender Mentoring Program for National Expertise Transfer","The informal network of gender advisers will be tapped for a 'gender mentoring program' that will transfer gender expertise to nationals.",""],[1,"176","6","Technical Support Program for Women Managers in Civil Service","A technical support program for women managers in the civil service will also be created.",""],[1,"176","6","Gender Equity Mainstreaming in Local Development Planning","Local chief executives are mandated to ensure that gender equity theme is incorporated into the local development plan and into the overall work of the local government.",""],[1,"176","6","Pilot Gender Mainstreaming Provinces","Pilot provinces on gender mainstreaming will be developed.",""],[1,"176","6","Sub-national Gender Mainstreaming Advocacy Network","DOWAs will build a network of gender advocates and their capacity to oversee sub-national gender mainstreaming will be strengthened.","DOWAs"],[1,"176","7","Gender Equity Strategy Implementation Support","International organizations are encouraged to adopt gender equity in their development co- operation and technical assistance and directly support ministries in implementing gender equity strategy.",""],[1,"176","8","Facilitation, Monitoring, and Coordination Mechanisms","The Government will establish mechanisms to effectively facilitate, monitor, and coordinate",""],[1,"222","17","National Action Plan for Women","Implement National Action Plan for Women",""],[1,"222","24","Capacity Building Program for Women in Government","Capacity Building Program for Women in Government at the level of Na- tional Assembly, provincial council and women laid off by the PRR processes",""],[1,"222","24","Gender-Sensitive Budgeting Capacity Building for Ministries and LGUs","Capacity Building for Ministries and LGUs on Gender Sensitive Budgeting",""],[1,"244","27","Comprehensive Gender-Sensitive Institutional Reform","Comprehensive and gender sensitive reform of institutions, review and update of relevant legislations, policies and administrative processes",""],[1,"253","9","Sex-Disaggregated Human Statistics","Disaggregate by sex all human related statistics",""]],"9":[[1,"45","5","National Consensus Building on Development Strategy","build a national consensus with respect to the Government's overall vision, develop- ment strategy, and greater understanding of the realistic pace at which national de- velopment could take place;",""],[1,"45","9","Meaningful Participatory Process Design","the Government has worked hard to design a meaningful participatory process as part of the future ANDS.",""],[1,"46","2","Institutionalized Participatory Decision-Making Process","lay the groundwork for a sustainable proc- ess, which would last beyond the life of the development of the full ANDS, and ensure regular inputs into Government decision- making processes, thereby creating a par- ticipatory process which will be institu- tionalized over time;",""],[1,"46","3","Government Consultation Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of the Government to consult widely on its strategies, as well",""],[1,"53","4","Sustained Participation Processes","It is envisioned that participation processes will be sustained throughout implementation of the strategy.",""],[1,"64","5","NGO and Civil Society Participation in Poverty Reduction Planning","ANDS progress reports will be publicly disseminated.",""],[1,"64","5","Participatory Poverty Assessment and Consultation Mechanism","Civil society and sub-national level bodies will be consulted in preparation of the ANDS updates.",""],[1,"64","5","Regular Participatory Poverty Assessments","Participatory poverty qualitative assessments and quantitative analysis will be provided on a regular basis to obtain input from NGOs and civil society on the key priorities for the poverty reduction.",""],[1,"91","6","Youth Participation in Governance Policy","A proactive policy to expand opportunities for young people that encompasses all areas of Government activity will be adopted.",""],[1,"91","13","Citizen Participation in Sub-national Governance","People's participation in sub-national governance will be increased.","Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG)"],[1,"93","15","Civil Society Participation in Legal Policy Development","increased opportunities for external stakeholders and civil society to contribute to legal policy development in policy analysis and legislative drafting",""],[1,"184","9","Civil Society Engagement for Participatory Priority Setting","Engaging civil society: participatory processes, particularly those engaging civil society, are essential to establishing clear, locally owned priorities so that aid is demand driven and has maximum impact.",""],[1,"206","3","Independent Civil Society Monitoring and Reporting System","Independent monitoring and reporting by NGOs, CSOs, the media and other civilian bod- ies will be a vital part of the overall monitoring and reporting system.",""]],"10":[[1,"159","10","Human Rights Monitoring and AIHRC Support Mechanism","Human rights monitoring will be carried out by the Government and independently by the AIHRC, and the UN will track the effectiveness of measures aimed at the protection of human rights; the AIHRC will be supported in the fulfillment of its objectives with regard to monitoring, investigation, protection and promotion of human rights.",""]],"11":[[1,"42","6","Capacity Development Objective for Program and Project Implementation","The ANDS capacity development objective is to assure that the skills needed to effectively implement programs and projects included in the ANDS exist or can be developed within the required time frame for implementation.",""],[1,"42","6","Inter-Ministerial Commission for Capacity Development","The institutional responsibility will be with Inter- ministerial Commission for Capacity Devel- opment (ICCD) that will serve as a single re- porting point for both government and donors.",""],[1,"42","6","Coordinated Aid and Capacity Development Support Mechanism","ICCD will provide a coordinated approach to support the effective management of funds and aid flows, to cut down on duplication and to ensure that critical capabilities for program and project implementation are well defined and (most importantly) that capacity development and technical assistance programs are properly focused on meeting these critical needs.",""],[1,"90","8","Comprehensive Institutional Strengthening and Capacity Building","The Government will undertake comprehensive institutional strengthening and capacity building within the ministries, provinces, districts, municipalities and villages.",""],[1,"97","16","Donor Cooperation for Capacity Building and Know-How Transfer","the Government seeks donors close cooperation in capacity building and know- how transfer",""],[1,"178","2","Reform Implementation Management Units for Ministry Restructuring and Pay and Grading Reform","At the ministerial level, under the guidance of the Independent Administrative Reforms and Civil Service Commission (IARCSC), Reform Implementation Management Units (RIMU) have been established primarily to restructure ministries so that they could move ahead on pay and grading reform - this process of re- structuring requires clarifying roles and re- sponsibilities, and laying down very clear re- porting lines, and assessing whether individu- als are fit to hold the job they are holding.","Independent Administrative Reforms and Civil Service Commission (IARCSC)"],[1,"178","2","Capacity Development Needs Identification and Coordination Mechanism","Capacity development is not the primary role of the RIMUs, but the RIMUs will identify capac- ity development needs, coordinate programs and initiatives to meet those needs, while monitoring and evaluate the impact.",""],[1,"178","2","Capacity Development Project and Programme Monitoring System","The ICCD will monitor the progress of the capacity de- velopment projects and programs.",""],[1,"178","2","Performance Reporting and Corrective Action for Underperforming Projects","The President and Cabinet will receive regular reports on performance of all projects.",""],[1,"178","3","RIMU Coordination and Capacity Development Support","the IARCSC will be empowered to encourage RIMUs to work together along the lines of the ANDS/sectoral groupings, to identify common needs and solu- tions as well as assist to articulate specific needs and formulate outline proposals as ap- propriate.",""],[1,"178","3","Capacity Needs Assessment and Monitoring and Evaluation Training","Where needed, the IARCSC with donors' assistance will provide training on ca- pacity needs assessments, capacity develop- ment activities and monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"178","6","Capacity Assessment and Training Programme for RIMUs","Conduct capacity assessments with RIMUs, establish and implement training pro- grams;",""],[1,"178","7","RIMU Capacity Assessment, Development, and M&E Training","Empower and train RIMUs in capacity assessments, capacity development, monitoring and evaluation;",""],[1,"178","9","RIMU Capacity Assessment and Capacity Development Planning","Empower RIMUs to undertake a depart- ment by department capacity assessment until all ministries have been assessed and capacity development plans drawn up to meet needs.",""],[1,"178","10","Training Projects for Capacity Development","Once the basic institutions required for capac- ity development, program implementation mechanism and priority sectors have been agreed upon, there will be a need to set up a number of training projects.",""]],"12":[[1,"97","15","Governance and Rule of Law Institutional Strengthening","has directed that a considerable proportion of available resources be devoted to strengthening the institutions responsible for delivering good governance.",""],[1,"214","8","Good Governance and Rule of Law Reform","Good governance and adherence to the rule of law are much needed reforms that the Government is committed to pursue.",""],[1,"214","8","Governance Improvement Measures","these reforms have to be initiated by internal decisions to implement improvements in governance.",""]],"13":[[1,"170","6","Regional and Bilateral Migration Agreement Implementation","The Government will aim to conclude and imple- ment regional and bilat- eral agreement on popu- lation movements and migration;",""],[1,"170","6","Refugee Repatriation Communication Strategy","Plan to better communi- cate to the neighboring countries the Govern- ment policies and pro- grams for repatriation of the refugees",""],[1,"265","11","Voluntary Repatriation Operation","Tri-partite agreements are concluded between countries of asylum, Afghanistan, and UNHCR, fully reflecting the principles of voluntary, dignified and gradual return, continue to guide the conduct of the voluntary repatriation operation.",""],[1,"265","12","Tripartite Commission Coordination Mechanism for Voluntary Repatriation","Tripartite Commissions are convened as the key policy arena within which decisions on the conduct of voluntary repatriation operations are taken",""],[1,"265","14","Border Movement Monitoring and Returnee Interview Mechanism","Monitor border movements, interview returnees and document violations of articles of agreements, due attention to be given to counter narcotics issues",""],[1,"267","9","Negotiation for Predictable Legal Status and Renewable Documentation","Negotiations with neighboring countries led by Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Ministry of Refugees and Repatriation for more predictable and clearer legal status and renewable documentation","Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Ministry of Refugees and Repatriation"]],"14":[[1,"81","4","Build Administrative Capacity and Justice Sector","The Government is intent on building administrative capacity, investing in human resources development and justice sector, and spurring private sector development to help improve Afghanistan's internal situation.",""],[1,"87","2","Justice System Strengthening and Reform Program","The Government is committed to strengthening the justice system, incuding the Supreme Court, Attorney General's Office, Chief Prosecution Department, Ministry of Justice, and military courts in the capital and provinces.","Supreme Court | Attorney General's Office | Chief Prosecution Department | Ministry of Justice"],[1,"87","2","Professional Cadre Appointment and Justice Sector Coordination","Priority programs of the Government include appointing profes- sional cadres, coordinating law enforcement and justice sector development programs to establish a prosperous, stable, and a just society based on democratic values and international standards.",""],[1,"87","2","Ministry of Justice and Judicial Reform Support","The Government is implementing programs to strengthen and support reform in the Ministry of Justice, the Supreme Court, and the Attorney General's Office.","Ministry of Justice | Supreme Court | Attorney General's Office"],[1,"89","2","Legal and Courts Process Reform","The main priorities for the governance sector are (iii) reform legal and courts processes;",""],[1,"91","17","Justice Sector Institutional Strengthening and Coordination Reform","The role of the Justice Sector in the govern- ment's development strategy is to ensure im- proved integrity, performance and infrastruc- ture of Afghanistan's justice institutions in each province; to streamline administrative struc- tures, ensure professional integrity and im- prove coordination and integration within the",""],[1,"92","1","National Justice Sector Strategy","The government has developed the National Justice Sector Strategy (NJSS) to fully articulate these objectives.",""],[1,"92","1","Justice Sector Coordination and Specialization Strengthening","This will strengthen and improve coordination among the justice institutions, and within the justice institutions and their bilateral and multilateral funding partners.",""],[1,"92","1","Expansion of Justice Services and Engagement with Informal Justice Systems","In the longer term the sector will seek to increase specialization and diversification of justice practices to meet more complex demands - including the important and necessary interaction and relationship with informal justice systems, which are prevalent throughout the country, while expanding justice services.",""],[1,"92","2","Justice System Efficiency Reform","An efficiently operating justice system will encourage investment and for economic activity to move from the infor- mal to the formal sector, thereby strengthening the ability of the government to raise revenue internally.",""],[1,"93","5","Justice Institutions Operating Cost Financing","Operating costs need to be financed to im- prove performance of justice institutions;",""],[1,"93","14","Justice Sector Administrative Reform and Restructuring","Administrative reform and restructuring of justice institutions;",""],[1,"93","15","Provincial Justice Coordination Mechanism Support","Support the Provincial Justice Co- ordination Mechanism (PJCM), to improve the delivery of justice assistance in the provinces",""],[1,"224","23","Justice Institutions Record-Keeping Improvement Review","Analyze and develop recommendations regarding justice institutions' record-keeping practices in order to improve accuracy and irretrievability and to avoid redundant proc- esses",""],[1,"224","24","Justice Sector Remuneration and Human Resources System Reform","Analyze and make recommendations for improving existing remuneration and human resources systems in justice insti- tutions.",""],[1,"224","25","Institution-Specific Remuneration and Human Resources Schemes","Support development and introduction of institution- specific remuneration and human resources schemes, such as pay and grading and performance evaluation measures",""],[1,"225","2","Justice Institutions Organizational and Administrative Reform","Analyze and, in consultation with stakeholders, develop recommendations for improving the organizational, man- agement and administrative structures of justice institutions to enable them to fulfill their respective mandates and func- tions at headquarters and at provincial and district level offices",""],[1,"225","8","Justice Service Infrastructure Expansion","Justice institutions construct, acquire or make functional on a priority basis infrastructure necessary to expand delivery of justice services throughout provincial and district areas outside of regional centers.",""],[1,"225","9","Justice Institutions Equipment and Supply Assessment and Procurement Reform","Assess and priorities equipment and supply needs of justice institutions and establish effective and accountable procurement systems.",""],[1,"225","10","Equipment and Supplies Provision Based on Needs Assessment","Provide equipment and supplies in accordance with needs assessment.",""],[1,"225","11","Comprehensive Transportation Asset Inventory","Conduct comprehensive inventory of all transportation assets, indicating condition and expected lifespan.",""],[1,"225","12","Asset Management Capacity Review and Improvement Recommendations","Survey existing asset management capacity and make rec- ommendations for improvement",""],[1,"225","13","Justice Institutions Transport Asset Provision","Justice institutions acquire and maintain transportation as- sets sufficient to fulfill their tasks.",""],[1,"227","8","Program Oversight Committee Establishment","Create and establish the Program Oversight Committee, together with requisite administrative and logistical support",""],[1,"227","9","Program Implementation Unit Establishment","Create and establish the Program Implementation Unit",""],[1,"227","10","Baseline Survey of Legal System Performance","Design and administer a baseline survey of legal system performance",""],[1,"227","11","Justice Information Sharing and Interfacing Coordination","Improve information sharing between justice institutions, and coordinate information management and interfacing.",""],[1,"228","2","Conversion to Combined Paper and Electronic File Systems","Evaluate the viability of converting paper-based file sys- tems to combined paper and electronic file systems",""],[1,"228","4","Justice Institution Planning and Coordination Mechanisms for Specialized Units","Justice institutions develop plans and implement coordina- tion mechanisms for specialized units addressing cross- cutting issues",""],[1,"228","13","Legal Materials Compilation and Distribution System","Compile and distribute legal materials in response to needs and establish system for routine updating of legal resources.",""],[1,"228","15","Legal Document Standardization and Registry Modernization","Survey and standardize routine legal documents (e.g., bonds, title deeds, marriage certificates and certificates of the courts) and the existing systems for registering, index- ing and retrieving them.",""],[1,"228","16","Nationwide Justice Facility Forms Distribution and Staff Training","Distribute forms to relevant justice facilities nationwide and train staff to use them and make them available to the public for standardized nominal fees.",""],[1,"228","17","Electronic Legal Registration Document Storage and Retrieval Pilot","Pilot an electronic storage and retrieval system for legal registration documents",""],[1,"231","4","Justice Institution Public Information Materials Standardization","Develop and standardize informational materials on the mission, the function and the operating procedures of each justice institution and make it available to the public.",""],[1,"231","5","Public Inquiry Focal Office Establishment","Establish a dedicated office within each justice institution and organization capable of acting as a focal point for public inquiries.",""],[1,"271","9","Justice System Institutional Reform","reforms will strengthen the professionalism, credibility and in- tegrity of key institutions of the justice system","the Ministry of Justice | the Judiciary | the Attorney-General's Office | the Ministry of the Interior | the National Directorate of Security"],[1,"271","12","Provincial Justice Institutions Operationalization","justice institutions will be fully functional and operational in each province of Afghanistan",""],[1,"271","12","Contract Dispute Resolution Acceleration","the average time to resolve contract disputes will be reduced as much as possible",""],[1,"271","20","Merit-Based Recruitment and Promotion of Justice Professionals","By end-2013 the Justice Institutions will Have recruited and promoted justice profes- sionals on merit, based on established policies and procedures, including meeting the target of 30% of the professional staff being female",""],[1,"272","5","Criminal Procedure Code Enactment and Legal Training Programme","By 2009 (1388), the new criminal procedure code will be enacted and published, and for its implementation training with written commentary will be provided to all legal professionals, as well as community legal education for citizens",""],[1,"272","7","Justice Institutions Process Mapping and Streamlining Reform","By end-2013 the Justice Institutions will have mapped in detail the processes linking all justice institutions, and have streamlined them to improve information systems and business processes, with the aim of reducing delays in processing of cases, administrative costs and vulnerability to corruption",""],[1,"272","10","Justice Proceedings Public Outreach and Education Program","By end-2013, the Justice Institutions will encourage press coverage of justice proceedings, public attendance at those proceedings, and general public understanding of the process at each stage of such proceedings.",""],[1,"272","10","Civil Society Justice Outreach Program Development","The justice institutions should encourage and participate in the development of outreach programs within civil society including curriculum for public education at all levels",""],[1,"272","13","Public Complaints System for Justice Institutions","By end-2013, the Justice Institutions will have established an easily accessible and functioning public complaints system in at least eight major provincial capitals with clear processes for handling complaints",""],[1,"272","16","Justice Sector Anti-Corruption Vulnerability Assessment and Reform","By end-2013, the Justice Institutions will have determined their vulnerabilities to corruption and established policies and procedures to eliminate such vulnerabilities",""]],"15":[[1,"92","3","Judicial System Strengthening for Private Sector Growth","Growth of the private sector, a prerequisite of which is an efficient judicial sys- tem will generate increased demand for labor.",""],[1,"92","3","Labor and Contract Law Reform","In addition, improved labor and contract laws will lower the cost of hiring labor and directly encourage increased employment, particularly in urban centers.",""],[1,"93","16","Criminal Justice Investigation and Case Management Reform","investigation system established to deter- mine delays in criminal justice system and lack of representation and improved case management",""],[1,"93","16","Sentencing Policy Development","Sentencing Policy developed",""],[1,"93","16","Juvenile Justice Policy Implementation","Juvenile Justice Policy implemented",""],[1,"93","16","Specialization in Criminal Justice","Specialization to address cross-cutting and emerging issues in criminal justice",""],[1,"93","16","Civil Court Administration and Jurisdiction Reform","Enhanced and improved civil court case ad- ministration and jurisdictional structures in major litigation categories",""],[1,"93","16","Formal and Informal Justice Linkage Review","investigating policies for improved links between formal and informal justice sectors and oversight of the informal by the formal",""],[1,"227","6","Defense Attorney Safeguards in Criminal Proceedings","Develop and implement procedures to safeguard and further the role and function of defense attorneys in criminal investigations and trials",""],[1,"227","7","Court Regulations and Case Tracking System Upgrade","Update and implement court regulations in order to facilitate filing and tracking of civil and criminal cases (including AGO Information System).",""],[1,"227","12","Police-Prosecutor Coordination Mechanism","Develop, establish, and implement measures and mecha- nisms to improve police prosecutor coordination in criminal matters; and addressing the cross-cutting issues",""],[1,"227","13","One-Stop Complaints System for Justice Institutions","Introduce effective \"one-stop\" complaints system covering all justice institutions.",""],[1,"227","14","Police and Prosecutor Capacity Enhancement for Criminal Investigations","Enhance capacity of police and prosecutors to conduct pro- active criminal investigations.",""],[1,"227","16","Judicial Trial Practices and Trial Management Training","Train judges, lawyers and prosecutors in trial practices and trial management.",""],[1,"228","9","Judicial and Investigative Capacity-Building Training","Build capacity of judges, prosecutors, and investigators by training on cross-cutting issues.",""],[1,"228","14","Judicial and Procedural Manual Development and Distribution","Develop and distribute judicial and procedural manuals for legal professionals, including judges, prosecutors and de- fense advocates.",""],[1,"229","15","Civil Justice Process Review and Reform Recommendations","Review existing civil justice processes and practices, in- cluding enforcement of judgments, and develop recommen- dations based on the findings.",""],[1,"230","5","Civil Justice Process Rationalization and Update","Rationalize and update civil justice process and practices, including enforcement of judgments, in accordance with the developed recommendations",""],[1,"230","10","Baseline Survey of Prosecution Efficiency","Carry out a baseline survey of prosecution efficiency and number of criminal complaints proceeding to trial.",""],[1,"230","11","Prosecution Resource Prioritization Program","Develop a program for prioritizing prosecution resources according to seriousness of the offense.",""]],"16":[[1,"73","6","Inter-Ministerial Macroeconomic Policy Coordination","Further strengthening coordination among relevant line ministries.",""],[1,"76","7","Prudent Debt Management Framework","Prudent debt management will continue to be essential as Afghanistan moves towards fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"76","7","Concessional Debt Financing for Specific Projects and Programmes","As a supplement to donor funds the country expects to continue to use limited amounts of debt to finance specific projects and various program requirements.",""],[1,"77","3","Prudent Monetary and Disciplined Fiscal Policy","In the medium to long term, prudent monetary policy together with a disciplined fiscal policy will contribute to a reduction in the risk premium.",""],[1,"77","3","Financial Intermediation and Macroeconomic Stability Measures","Effective financial intermediation and macroeconomic stability will eventually bring down real interest rates in the long run as prospects for long term stability improve.",""],[1,"77","3","Central Bank Monitoring of Monetary and Credit Markets","The central bank will closely monitor the monetary developments and ensuing liquidity situation along with developments in interest rates and credit markets and will react appropriately to these developments.",""],[1,"77","4","Monetary Policy Instrument Expansion","DAB intends to ex- pand the menu of instruments that have not yet been fully utilized in directing monetary pol- icy.",""],[1,"77","6","Capital Notes Issuance and Secondary Market Development","DAB will issue capital notes with various ma- turity periods and create a secondary market for trading of these notes.",""],[1,"77","6","Monetary Policy Tool Repositioning","Overall, by creating a capi- tal market and a strategic repositioning of monetary policy tools through gradual transi- tioning from foreign exchange auctions to util- izing other tools of the monetary policy, DAB's room for maneuverability will expand.",""]],"17":[[1,"26","10","Investor Attraction Efforts","Increased efforts by both the Government and the donor community to attract Afghan and foreign investors are needed if the goals of the ANDS are to be realized.",""],[1,"35","2","Private Sector Enabling Environment Reform","The establishment of a strong enabling environment for a competitive private sector is an on-going effort by both the Government and donors.",""],[1,"35","2","Legal and Regulatory Framework for Private Sector Development","The Government will enact and implement key laws and amendments to establish the basic legal and regulatory framework that will encourage private sector involvement in social and economic development.",""],[1,"35","2","Institutional Strengthening for Law Administration","Almost all sector strategies involve institutional strengthening that is designed to improve the ability of ministries and other agencies to administer legislation in an unbiased and predictable manner.",""],[1,"35","6","Investor-Friendly Regulatory Frameworks for Private Sector Operations","This approach has been very successful in the telecommunications sector, where phone usage went from less than 15,000 under a state monopoly to over five million subscribers as private investments in cellular communication were encouraged.",""],[1,"35","7","Private Sector Investment Promotion Effort","A third and closely related component of the strategy is based on a concerted effort by the Government and the donor community to more vigorously promote private sector investment.",""],[1,"36","1","Investment Promotion and Investor Support Initiative","Efforts at investment promotion will be designed to convince these investors that they are both needed in Afghanistan and that they will be able to operate profitably with full government support consistent with maintaining a competitive environment.",""],[1,"73","9","Private Sector Investment Constraint Reduction Measures","In order to break the evolving informal equilib- rium, we must also ameliorate specific private sector investment constraints.",""],[1,"101","1","Enabling Environment for Private Sector-Led Development","the actions and programs designed to establish an enabling environment for the private and non-government sectors are included.",""],[1,"101","3","Private Investment Protection and Promotion Policy","The State encourages and protects private capital investments and enterprises based on the market economy and guarantees their protection in accordance with the provisions of law.",""],[1,"101","5","Private Sector-Led Market-Based Economic Development Framework","We will build a market-based system, driven by private sector growth, in which Government is the \"policy maker and regulator of the economy, not its competitor\".",""],[1,"101","5","Foundations for Socially Responsible Private Sector Growth","If the Government is to achieve its aim of significantly enhancing per capita GDP in the next five years, it must complete the foundations for socially responsible private sector growth and encourage sustained high levels of foreign and domestic private investment.",""],[1,"101","7","Investment Legislation Simplification and Harmonization","All legislation, regulations and procedures related to investment will be simplified and harmonized by end-2006 and implemented by end-1386 (2007).",""],[1,"101","7","New Business Organization Laws","New business organization laws will be tabled in the National Assembly by end-2006.",""],[1,"102","5","Private Sector Enabling Environment and Investment Promotion Strategy","The strategy to foster private sector develop- ment and increase domestic and foreign in- vestment consists of three main components: (i) continued efforts to build a strong and stable enabling environment that will encourage a competitive private sector; (ii) expand the scope for private investment in developing na- tional resources and infrastructure; and (iii) strengthen efforts to promote investment from domestic sources, the Afghan diaspora and foreign investors.",""],[1,"102","11","Private Sector Investment Promotion and Institutional Strengthening","Attracting private investment is the responsibility of the entire Government and will be an integral part of all projects and programs implemented under the ANDS.",""],[1,"103","11","Institutional Strengthening Programs","Implement effective programs to pro- vide institutional strengthening and",""],[1,"104","10","Private Investment Coordination and Capacity Strengthening","This will require improved coordination and strengthening the capacities of most ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"105","1","Whole-of-Government Private Investment Promotion","investment opportunities cannot be the respon- sibility of only one or two agencies or minis- tries, but must entail a concerted effort by the entire Government.",""],[1,"105","1","Donor Cooperation for Private Sector Investment","Efforts to encourage pri- vate sector investment also require the under- standing and cooperation of the donor com- munity.",""],[1,"105","3","Investment Promotion and Facilitation Initiative","The third component of the strategy involves concerted efforts to promote investment from foreign and domestic sources, including from the Afghan diaspora.",""],[1,"105","3","Afghanistan Investment Support Agency Strengthening","The Afghanistan Investment Sup- port Agency will play a central role in this process and will be strengthened.",""],[1,"105","3","Government-Wide Investment Promotion Mainstreaming","the responsibility for promoting increased invest- ment will be a government-wide task and will be an integral part of all projects and programs undertaken as a part of the ANDS.",""],[1,"105","5","Private Investment Promotion and Investor Assurance Measures","recognizes the importance to the country of increased private investment and to work with potential investors to assure them that their investments will not fail due to unpredictable and unfavorable changes in the tax environ- ment or policies towards private investors.",""],[1,"162","1","Private Sector Resource Mobilization Support","effective support to the mobilization of the country's resources through the private sector, including efficiently providing the needed physical, legal and commercial infrastructure and institutional frameworks, while taking ac- tion to meet the pressing needs of the poor and most vulnerable members of the society.",""],[1,"195","5","Private Sector Participation in ANDS Implementation","Apart from the Budget, the private sector is expected to play important role in the implementation of the ANDS contributing to job creation, infrastructure development and revenue mobilization.",""],[1,"195","5","Private Sector Leadership in Priority Sector Implementation","It is expected that the private sector will play leading role in implementation of the ANDS priorities in number of sectors such as: ICT, mining and natural resources, agriculture, private sec- tor development and others.",""],[1,"214","8","Public Sector Focus on Enabling Private Sector Environment","the ANDS approach has been to encourage the public sector to concentrate on the creation of a safe and conducive environment that encourages the smooth operation of a robust private sector.",""],[1,"214","8","Shift Public Sector Away from Goods and Services Production","This means a much greater focus by Government on governance issues rather than involvement in the production of goods and services that can be provided by a significantly",""],[1,"215","2","Enabling Environment for Private Sector Development","The Government is taking steps to establish an enabling environment, based on sound market-oriented policies and an adherence to the rule of law.",""],[1,"215","2","Legal and Regulatory Framework for Private Investment","To realize this enormous potential, the Government is developing the legal and regulatory structures required to enable private investment to operate profitably.",""]],"18":[[1,"73","16","Industrial Parks Strategy Development","Developing a strategy for industrial parks;",""],[1,"74","8","Public Infrastructure Reconstruction through Budget Allocation","Proper budget allocation enables the reconstruction of basic infrastructure, supports private sector development, improves overall economic efficiency and enhances the popula- tion's standard of living, especially for the poor.",""],[1,"75","1","Priority Budget Allocation to Productive Sectors","the prioritization framework of budgetary allocations is expected to allocate significant resources to productive sectors such as infrastructure, health, education, agriculture and rural development, and rule of law and governance.",""],[1,"75","1","Public Investment in Roads, Energy, Water, Irrigation, Airports, and Communications Technologies","Cumulative total public expendi- tures during 1387-91 in roads, energy, water and irrigation, airports, and communications technologies alone are expected to reach about $11 billion",""],[1,"79","1","Public Expenditure Prioritization for Infrastructure, Agriculture, and Rural Development","In the short term, the Government will focus its public expenditure programs on investments in infrastructure, agriculture and rural develop- ment",""],[1,"79","6","Priority Public Investment Program","Security will remain the Government's highest priority, while the public expenditure programs for investments in energy, water and irrigation, transportation infrastructure, agriculture, agro-based industry, and rural development will remain high priorities, acknowledging the high importance of these sectors for the development of the private sector and for long term and sustainable employment growth.",""],[1,"82","4","Economic Infrastructure Development and Alternative Livelihoods Programme","the development of economic infrastructure, de- mand reduction, poppy eradication, countering drug trafficking and establishing alternative livelihood programs.",""],[1,"233","18","Business and Trade Liaison Mechanism","Establish a liaison mechanism for joint forums with Business/Trade/Employers' association.",""],[1,"233","20","Trade Facilitation Zones Development","Trade Facilitation Zones (TFZ) in key areas of Afghanistan that will connect district and provisional level production to regional and international markets by providing the basic infrastructure for processing, packaging and storage.",""],[1,"233","23","Land Policy-Based Draft Legislation","Draft legislation based on the recommendations of the land policy that com- prises legal frameworks for land registration; land adjudication, including community-based systems; and the formalization of informal land holdings, including legislation for adverse possession.",""],[1,"233","25","Simplified Private Land Transfer Procedures","Implement improved simplified procedures for transfer of privately owned land.",""],[1,"233","27","Land Transfer Procedure Simplification Reform","Clarify and simplify the procedures associated with the transfer of publicly- owned and privately-owned land.",""],[1,"233","28","Foreign Investor Land Lease Access","Permit foreign investors to obtain access to land through 90-year leases.",""],[1,"234","2","Government Land Lease Reform","Extend the duration of leases for government land and ensure that they are either wholly or partly transferable.",""],[1,"234","3","Industrial Parks Strategy and Development Authority","Develop a strategy for industrial parks, including the creation of an industrial park development department as an independent authority.",""],[1,"234","6","Integrated Business Registration and Tax Identification Platform","Consolidate the registration of private sector entities and the issuance of tax identification numbers into a single platform, extending the service to smaller businesses.",""],[1,"234","8","Licensing Requirement Deregulation","Remove licensing requirements except for reasons of health, safety, environ- mental protection, land use and access to natural resources.",""],[1,"234","10","Business License Re-engineering and Streamlining","Make necessary business licenses more effective by re-engineering and streamlining them",""],[1,"234","12","Regulatory Best Practice Adoption","Adopt the principles of regulatory best practice (RBP) to ensure that new regulations are appropriate and minimize compliance cost",""],[1,"234","14","SME Compliance Cost Reduction Exemptions","Minimize compliance costs for SMEs by introducing appropriate administrative and reporting exemptions for SMEs",""],[1,"234","15","Licensing Requirements and Procedures Information Publication","Publish comprehensive information on licensing requirements and procedures",""],[1,"234","17","Private Sector Legal and Regulatory Awareness Education","Educate private sector stakeholders' (investors, employers, employees and consumers) to increase awareness and understanding of their legal and regula- tory rights and responsibilities.",""],[1,"234","19","One-Stop Government Revenue Collection Points","Establish and enforce \"one-stop collection points\" for tax payment and other government revenue collection in every district centre.",""],[1,"234","20","Tax System Reform and Nuisance Tax Elimination","Continue to eliminate nuisance taxes and reform the tax system to make it simpler, fairer, more competitive and easier to comply with",""],[1,"234","21","High Commission on Investment Reform and Revitalization","Reform and revitalize the High Commission on Investment (HCI).",""],[1,"234","23","Customs Regulation Enforcement and Trade Clearance Time Reduction","Apply customs regulations consistently across the country and commit to achieving an average time for importing and exporting goods in line with best practice in the region (reduced by at least half of current levels).",""],[1,"236","3","Strengthening Chambers of Commerce and Business Membership Organizations","Strengthen chambers of commerce and business membership organizations",""],[1,"236","5","Coordination of Public and Private Sector Approaches to Expand Access to Essential Business Services","Co-ordinate public and private sector approaches to increasing access to essen- tial business services",""],[1,"236","12","Legal Framework and Rapid Development of the Afghanistan National Standards Authority","Create the legal framework for and ensure the rapid development of the Af- ghanistan National Standards Authority (ANSA)",""],[1,"236","13","Consumer Protection Agency Establishment","Establish a consumer protection agency to define, communicate and protect consumer rights",""],[1,"236","20","Business Formalization Strategy","Develop a formalization strategy grounded in an understanding of the incentives and disincentives facing business, which reduces entry costs to, and operating costs within, the formal sector and increases the benefits of formalization",""],[1,"236","23","Afghanistan-Pakistan Transit Agreement","The new Afghanistan Pakistan Transit Agreement (APTA), the revised version of Afghan Trade and Transit Agreement (ATTA) signed with Pakistan in 1965",""],[1,"236","26","Strengthen Provincial Enforcement of Commercial Laws and Regulations","Work with provincial public sector institutions to increase the consistency of application of commercial laws and regulations",""],[1,"236","28","Provincial Economic Growth Strategies","Develop and implement economic growth strategies for provinces, based on private sector development",""],[1,"237","8","Council for the Private Sector","Create a Council for the Private Sector, reporting on progress against this ma- trix to the President.",""],[1,"237","9","Private Sector Priority List Development Process","Develop a list of the private sector's most urgent priorities that would support an enabling environment, developed through a process of sub-national consultation and engagement with the private sector to be presented to the Government within three to six months.",""],[1,"242","4","Adoption of Standards Compatible with Neighboring Countries","After a study of international standards, adopt a set of standards that are compatible with Afghanistan's neighbors.",""],[1,"250","10","Private Sector Investment Regulatory Framework","Develop a suitable regulatory framework to encourage private sector invest- ment",""]],"19":[[1,"36","6","Mining Sector Investment Promotion and Regulatory Reform","The ANDS strategic objective in the mining sector is to encourage legitimate private investment in the sector so as to substantially increase government revenues, improve employment opportunities and foster ancillary development.",""],[1,"36","6","Sustainable Minerals Development Policy Framework","Implementation of the strategy will help to develop effective market-based economy sector policies, promote and regulate sustainable development of minerals and ensure that the nation's geological resources are progressively investigated and developed.",""],[1,"36","6","Ministry of Mines Institutional Transition","The Ministry of Mines is making the transition from being primarily a producer of minerals and other commodities to a policy making and regulatory institution.","Ministry of Mines"],[1,"104","6","Natural Resources and Minerals Regulatory Reform","Private investment in the development of natural re- sources, particularly minerals development will become viable when suitable regulations are in place.",""],[1,"106","8","Cadastre and Inspectorate Functions Relocation to the Ministry of Mines","Cadastre and Inspectorate functions are now located at the Ministry of Mines to support oil, natural gas and coal contracts.","Ministry of Mines"],[1,"108","4","Mining and Hydrocarbons Regulatory Reform","Finalization of primary legislative and regulatory tools is essential.",""],[1,"133","12","Mineral Sector Investment Promotion and Regulation Strategy","The intention is to encourage legitimate private investment in the sector so as to substantially increase government revenues, improve employment opportunities and foster ancillary development centered on mining activity.",""],[1,"133","12","Geological Survey and Resource Documentation Programme","Implementation of the strategy will help to develop effective market-based economic policies, promote and regulate sustainable development of minerals and ensure that the nation's geological resources are progressively investigated and properly documented.",""],[1,"133","12","Large- and Small-Scale Mining Development Support","This strategy supports large and small scale mining for immediate and sustainable economic gains.",""],[1,"133","12","Mineral Exploration, Extraction, and Market Delivery Initiative","For mining and minerals, the emphasis is on the exploration, extraction and delivery to market; for hydrocarbons the emphasis is exploration and exploitation.",""],[1,"134","1","Enabling Regulatory Environment for Mineral and Natural Resource Extraction","The Afghanistan Compact Benchmark calls for an enabling regulatory environment for profit- able extraction of Afghanistan's mineral and natural resources to be created and for the in- vestment environment and infrastructure to be enhanced so as to attract significant domestic and foreign direct investment by end 2010.",""],[1,"134","6","Drafting of Mining and Hydrocarbons Regulations","Regulations are being drafted which may be finalized dur- ing 2008.",""],[1,"134","7","Natural Resources Sector Development Project","Some of the most immediate needs of the sector are being addressed as part of a $30 million project supporting sustainable development of natural resources.","Ministry of Mines"],[1,"135","1","Marble and Precious Stone Mining Projects","Projects identified and prioritized during the SNC process include the extraction of marbles, precious and semi precious stone mines in Anaba and Shotol districts of Panjshir province.",""],[1,"135","2","Mining Sector Regulatory and Investment Framework","The private sector will operate within a legislative and regulatory framework designed to facilitate investment and maintain a competitive sector.",""],[1,"135","2","Government Exploration Projects and Competitive Bidding for Natural Resource Assessment","The focus will be on using Government projects or competitive bidding for exploration contracts to better determine the extent of natural resources in Afghanistan;",""],[1,"135","2","Transparent Mining Resource Management System","the establishment of an improved, transparent and capable management system for the effective extraction of mines and natural resources;",""],[1,"135","2","Mining Investment Facilitation Regulatory Environment","the establishment of a regulatory environment that facilitates local and international investment in the mining sector.",""],[1,"135","3","Ministry of Mines Institutional Refocusing and Regulatory Reform","The key reform will involve the refocusing of the Ministry of Mines from one involved in production to one that is primarily concerned with the creation of an enabling environment that requires mining companies to operate effectively and responsibly in accordance with the law.","Ministry of Mines"],[1,"135","3","Mining Legislation Enactment and Implementation","Mining legislation will be passed and implemented.",""],[1,"135","3","Mineral Exploration and Exploitation by Private Sector or Ministry of Mines","Planned actions include exploration and exploitation of mineral resources by the private sector or MoM; capacity building programs; successful implementation of the Aynak project; development of long term geo- science projects; and a reconstruction program including equipping the laboratory and techni- cal sections of the ministry.","MoM"],[1,"135","3","Long-Term Geoscience Projects","Planned actions include exploration and exploitation of mineral resources by the private sector or MoM; capacity building programs; successful implementation of the Aynak project; development of long term geo- science projects; and a reconstruction program including equipping the laboratory and techni- cal sections of the ministry.",""],[1,"135","4","Mineral and Gas Resource Utilization Expansion","increase utilization of mineral and gas re- sources; encourage expansion of the cement industry and increase power supplies by rais- ing the production of mineral resources, oil, gas and underground water; and increase the pro- duction of urea.",""],[1,"135","4","PRR Implementation","The main programs of the sec- tor are (i) Implementing PRR",""],[1,"135","4","Legislative Affairs Completion","The main programs of the sec- tor are (ii) Legislative affairs completion",""],[1,"135","4","National Geological Survey Follow-up Programme","A comprehensive geo- logical study follow- up program in the coun- try",""],[1,"135","4","Private Sector Mineral Resource Exploration and Exploitation","Exploration and exploitation of mineral resources by private sector or geology survey of MoM","MoM"],[1,"135","4","Government or Private Sector Oil and Gas Field Development","Exploration, extraction and exploi- tation program of gas and oil fields in the coun- try by the government or private sector",""],[1,"135","4","Long-Term Geoscience Research Programme","Long term geo science research",""],[1,"135","8","Oil and Gas Block Bidding and Exploration Initiative","providing background information and invite bidding for three blocks of oil and gas in the northern provinces aimed at exploration and exploitation.",""],[1,"135","9","Mining Investment and Project Development Strategy","implementation of this strategy will lead to considerable investment in small and large projects.",""],[1,"165","3","Sector Governance Reform for Private Investment","There will be im- proved sector governance aimed at increased le- gitimate private investment.",""],[1,"165","4","Women in Mining Employment Initiative","A targeted initiative for \"Women in Min- ing\" to improve female employ- ment will be sup- ported",""],[1,"165","6","Inspectorate and Cadastre Establishment at the Ministry of Mines","Inspectorate and Cadastre to be established at the Ministry Mines.","Ministry Mines"],[1,"165","8","Ministry Staff Capacity Building for Hydrocarbon and Mineral Governance","The Ministry proposes capacity building for its staff members.","The Ministry"],[1,"239","25","Hydrocarbons, Minerals, and Market Cadastre Regulatory Revision","Revise 2 laws and 2 regulations related to Hydrocarbons, minerals and Market Cadastre & Inspectorate",""],[1,"245","20","Mineral, Oil and Gas Exploration and Survey Programme","Planning exploration activities, mapping, survey of minerals, oil and gas, col- lection of geophysical and geological information",""],[1,"246","6","Mineral Policy Design and Implementation","Design and implementation of Mineral policy",""],[1,"246","10","Oil and Gas Block Leasing for Research and Study","Leasing of oil and gas blocks to privates sector for research and study",""],[1,"246","11","New Gas and Oil Management Organizational Structure","Establishment of new organizational structure for gas and oil management",""],[1,"246","13","Gas Pipeline Grid Planning for Provinces","Design of plan for gas pipeline grid to provinces",""],[1,"246","22","Regional Cooperation for Mining Sector Projects","Promotion of regional cooperation to facilitate various projects under the mining sector",""],[1,"278","16","Legal and Regulatory Enabling Environment for Mining Investment","Creating enabling environment including legal one for increased investment in mining sector (2013)",""]],"20":[[1,"25","2","State-Owned Enterprise Privatization and Restructuring","State owned enterprises are being privat- ized, corporatized or liquidated.",""],[1,"35","3","State-Owned Enterprise Privatization and Corporatization Program","Privatization and corporization of state owned enterprises is an on-going program that is on schedule.",""],[1,"103","10","Financial Audits of State-Owned Assets and Corporations","Undertake financial audits of state owned assets and corporations.",""],[1,"103","13","State-Owned Enterprise Privatization and Corporatization Program","The Government will continue the program of privatization and corporatization of state owned enterprises, a process that is presently on schedule.",""],[1,"103","14","Formalization of Private Sector Operations","The Government is encouraging firms to formalize their activities by introducing tax number identification and applying commercial laws and regulations.",""],[1,"103","14","Private-Firm Channeling of Vocational Training Funds","Consideration is being given to innovative efforts to channel some public funds now being used for vocational training through properly registered firms in compliance with tax laws for their use in financing training for their employees in properly accredited vocational training programs.",""]],"21":[[1,"104","5","Civil Society Social Dialogue and Engagement Mechanism","The Government will maintain an open and effective social dialogue with civil society and encourage their contributions to social and economic development.",""],[1,"104","6","Infrastructure Investment and Regulatory Reform for Private Investment","The country requires enormous investment in infrastructure, including roads, power genera- tion, water supply, and irrigation.",""],[1,"104","7","Multi-Sector Regulatory Authority Establishment","The Government will establish a multi- sector regulatory authority following an approach similar to that used to develop the telecommunications industry.",""],[1,"104","8","Public-Private Partnership Framework for Infrastructure Investment","Opportunities for entering into public- private partnerships for investment in in- frastructure projects, such as roads and bridges, will be developed based on inter- national best practices.",""],[1,"104","9","Private Provision of Public Services Promotion","The Government will encourage private provision of public services wherever it will be feasible, including areas such as health, education, municipal services, etc.",""]],"22":[[1,"105","2","Commercial Agriculture Investment Promotion","The Government will seek to attract medium and large scale agricultural producers and processors to invest in commercial agriculture in order to increase employment and market opportunities in rural areas and to develop export markets for higher value Afghan products.",""],[1,"115","9","Agricultural Production Transformation and Rural Off-Farm Employment Expansion","This will require transforming agricultural production so that it is more productive and increasingly commercially oriented and expanding off-farm employment opportunities as the basis for increasing incomes among the rural population.",""],[1,"115","9","Support for Poor and Vulnerable Rural Households","A central focus is on supporting the poorest and most vulnerable segments of rural society and promoting the development of medium and large scale commercial agricultural activities.",""],[1,"115","11","Institutional, Regulatory and Incentive Framework for Legal Agriculture","The necessary institutional, regulatory and incentive framework to increase production and productivity will be established to create an enabling environment for legal agriculture and agriculture-based rural industries.",""],[1,"115","12","Agricultural Public Investment Expansion","Public investment in agriculture will in- crease by 30 percent.",""],[1,"115","12","Specialized Agricultural Support and Service Delivery Mechanisms","Particular considera- tion will be given to perennial horticulture, animal health, and food security by: insti- tuting specialized support agencies and fi- nancial service delivery mechanisms, sup- porting farmers' associations, branding na- tional products, disseminating timely price and weather-related information and statis- tics, providing strategic research and tech- nical assistance, and securing access to irri- gation and water management systems.",""],[1,"117","10","Farmer Assistance for Productivity Improvement","Assistance to farmers to increase produc- tion and productivity",""],[1,"118","1","Commercialized Agriculture Support Programme","Support of commercialized agriculture, leading to an improvement in agricultural productivity throughout the rural economy.",""],[1,"118","10","Horticulture Development Support Program","The Horticulture Program will support horticulture development and supply farmers with saplings, provide equipment for trellises and establish pest control systems leading to a 20 percent increase in perennial crop production and significant exports through public private sector partnerships.",""],[1,"118","11","Livestock Production Support Program","The Livestock Program will support live- stock production by importing purebred sheep, establishing commercial dairy plants and poultry units for women farm- ers, increasing productivity and output.",""],[1,"119","8","Research and Extension Capacity Development","The Research and Extension System will establish a research and extension capability; provide access to credit, support farmers organization and private sector market development through cooperatives, leading to agricultural growth and diversification.",""],[1,"119","8","Agricultural Credit Access Support","The Research and Extension System will establish a research and extension capability; provide access to credit, support farm-ers organization and private sector market development through cooperatives, leading to agricultural growth and diversifica-tion.",""],[1,"119","8","Farmers' Organization and Cooperative Market Development","The Research and Extension System will establish a research and extension capability; provide access to credit, support farm-ers organization and private sector market development through cooperatives, leading to agricultural growth and diversifica-tion.",""],[1,"119","12","Support for Commercial Agriculture","This includes ongoing efforts to increase the international community's, including ISAF, procurement of agricultural products from local producers, promoting large scale production and supply chain processes.",""],[1,"119","13","Agriculture and Rural Development Zones Program","The Agriculture and Rural Development Zones (ARDZ) program is the Government's approach to expanding commercial activities and increasing agricultural productivity.",""],[1,"119","15","Agricultural Transformation in High-Potential Zones","The Government's objective is to largely rely on private investment and public sector support to transform agriculture in some well defined zones where the conditions for growth are most favorable and high value added commercial agricultural activities can flourish.",""],[1,"120","8","Agricultural Growth Zone Private Sector Investment Mobilization","mobilize private sector investment and op- erations as the key element in the success of the agricultural growth zone initiative.",""],[1,"121","1","Public-Private Partnership Support for Horticulture Industry","Public and private sector partnerships strengthen horticulture industry.",""],[1,"121","1","Livestock Productivity and Food Security Improvement","Increased livestock production and productivity will improve food security and incomes that will lead to a reduction of illicit agriculture and a decline in livestock imports.",""],[1,"121","1","Agricultural Diversification and Rural Economy Support","Agriculture diversification through various value-added activities, research, extension, access to credit, market development, establishing/strengthening farmers' organization, private sector development, trainings, will improve the rural economy.",""],[1,"257","11","Five-Year Action Plan for ARD Zones","Develop 5 years action plan which quantifies all 8 functions of ARD zones including budget requirements, roles and responsibilities and appropriate M&E systems",""],[1,"258","20","Rural Enterprise and Credit Policy Reform","Review current and formulate new policies, legal and regulatory for establish- ing, stimulating and sustaining rural enterprises and credit",""],[1,"258","21","Rural Enterprise Support Services Network","Establish rural enterprise support services network",""],[1,"258","22","Agriculture and Rural Development Zones","Establish Agriculture and Rural Development Zones",""],[1,"258","24","National and International Market Development for Produce and Products","Develop national and international markets for agriculture and non-agriculture produce and products",""],[1,"259","3","Regional Cooperation for Economic Growth","Promote regional cooperation to help generate economic growth through tech- nologies, exchange of knowledge etc.",""],[1,"259","6","Executive Management Unit for CARD Implementation","Establish an Executive Management Unit with presidential authority and clear mandate to implement CARD",""],[1,"259","8","Local-National Agricultural and Rural Development Planning Integration Mechanism","Develop mechanism to ensure integration and linkage of local level planning with the national ARD investment planning",""],[1,"259","20","Licit Livelihood Diversification Programs","Design and implement programs to strengthen and diversify licit livelihood",""],[1,"259","23","Legal Agriculture Livelihood Support Programme","Interventions for promoting legal agriculture livelihood options through inputs like seeds, irrigation, fertilizers, credit and crop insurance",""],[1,"259","25","Self-Employment and Microenterprise Training and Microcredit Facilities","Training for self employment and micro enterprise and development of micro credit facilities",""],[1,"261","23","Public Works Program Communication Campaigns","Improve the communication campaigns to better inform the poor about opportunities to participate in the public work program",""],[1,"284","3","Rural SME Policy and Regulatory Framework","By end-2010, a policy and regulatory framework will be developed to support the establishment of small and medium rural enterprises, and institutional support will be established in all 34 provinces to facilitate new entrepreneurial initiatives by rural communities and organisations",""],[1,"284","3","Provincial Institutional Support for Rural Entrepreneurship","By end-2010, a policy and regulatory framework will be developed to support the establishment of small and medium rural enterprises, and institutional support will be established in all 34 provinces to facilitate new entrepreneurial initiatives by rural communities and organisations",""]],"23":[[1,"37","2","Water Resource Management Investment Programme","Within the water resources sector, feasibility studies will be completed and investments will be made in the needed storage facilities, recharge basins, multi-purpose dams, irrigation systems required to improve water sector management for both agricultural and non-agricultural uses.",""],[1,"37","2","Rehabilitation and Management Improvement of Existing Water Systems","These efforts will augment on-going efforts to rehabilitate and improve management in existing systems.",""],[1,"37","3","Integrated Water Resource Management System","Integrated Water Resource Management (IWRM) system geared to the five major river basins in the country, with an eventual devolu- tion of responsibilities down to independent River Basin authorities.",""],[1,"119","14","Geographic Targeting of Agricultural Infrastructure and Support","These geographic priorities will be used to target infrastructure, utilities and other support by various ministries.",""],[1,"119","14","Release of Publicly Held Land for Private Investment","The Government will release publicly held land to increase private investment.",""],[1,"119","14","Competitive Bidding for Land Lease Rights","Competitive bidding for the rights to lease these lands will be similar to the competitive bidding to lease development rights for mineral resources and the competitive bidding for the rights to use the telecommunications spectrum.",""],[1,"119","14","Support for Private Firm Expansion","the Government will continue to investigate, implement and monitor key steps necessary to increasing financial and technical support so that private firms are able to expand operations.",""],[1,"119","14","Transformation of Underutilized State Land into Agro-processing Enterprises","This will ensure the process of transforming underutilized state land into commercially viable agro-processing enterprises will be as fast and efficient as possible.",""],[1,"120","3","Agricultural Growth Zone Identification and Mapping","identify and map agricultural growth zones;",""],[1,"120","6","Agricultural Zone Expansion Planning","develop plans to extend the reach of agri- cultural zones into more remote rural ar- eas;",""],[1,"120","7","National Rural Development Activities Linked to Agricultural Growth Zone Plans","ensure rural development activities are national in scope and linked to the agricul- tural growth zone plans;",""],[1,"120","16","Executive Management Unit for ARDZ Coordination","the Government has begun the process of establishing the Ex- ecutive Management Unit with Presiden- tial authority to coordinate and develop a five year action plan and organize the nec- essary funding and commitment from line Ministries and donors so as to establish a program implementation plan.","line Ministries"],[1,"120","16","Critical Infrastructure and Service Provision in ARDZ Zones","This unit will ensure critical infrastructure, such as power, water, transportation links, tele- communications, financial services and vocational programs are available.","relevant Ministries"],[1,"120","16","Priority Service Delivery in ARDZ Zones","The Unit will work with relevant Ministries to ensure priority is given to providing ser- vices in these zones.","relevant Ministries"],[1,"131","6","Barikab Private Commercial Agricultural Zone","As part of the Dehsabz project, the Barikab area located to the north of the new city will become a private commercial agricultural zone designed to not only supply many of the needs of Dehsabz, but to become a center for the cultivation of exportable agricultural products.",""]],"25":[[1,"167","7","Agriculture and Rural Development Capacity Development and Institutional Reform","In addition to internal capacity building and institutional reform both at the central and local levels, every program intervention in agriculture and rural development has a significant capacity development component.",""],[1,"257","25","Natural Resources Law Reform","Review, revise and formulate Natural Resources laws (wetlands, forests, range",""],[1,"258","3","Food Laws and Regulations Reform","Review, revise and formulate Food laws and regulations (Quality and Safety, CODEX standards, quarantine)",""],[1,"258","4","Livestock and Horticulture Legal and Regulatory Reform","Review, revise and formulate laws and regulations on Livestock and Horticul- ture",""],[1,"258","5","Pesticides and Plant and Animal Protection Legal Reform","Review, revise and formulate laws and regulation on Pesticides Use, plant and animal protection",""],[1,"258","6","Agricultural Trade Law and Regulation Reform","Review, revise and formulate laws and regulations on agricultural imports and exports",""],[1,"258","7","Agricultural and Food Sector Legal Reform","Formulation of laws on concerning forests, food safety and control, strategic food reserves, agricultural imports, horticulture and improved seeds.",""],[1,"258","16","Water Management and Utilization Legal Reform","Review, revise and formulate laws and regulations on Water Management and utilization",""]],"26":[[1,"173","6","Licit Development Promotion Program","Expansion and effective delivery of programs to promote licit development, including economic support for licit cash crops and rural industries;",""],[1,"174","7","Export Market Development and Infrastructure Investment","Create markets for Afghan products through trade preferences and investment in infrastructure for export;",""],[1,"174","9","Afghan First Local Procurement Policy","Procure supplies and services for interna- tional military forces and organization in Afghanistan from Afghan sources, as en- visaged in the \"Afghan First\" policy;",""],[1,"174","12","Cash Crop Production and Market Development Programme","Production and market development pro- grams for cash crops in certain areas;",""],[1,"186","1","Alternative Livelihoods for Farmers to Eliminate the Narcotics Industry","eliminate the narcotics industry in a manner that provides alternative sources of income to the farmers.",""]],"27":[[1,"36","2","Energy Access Expansion and Cost-Reflective Supply","The immediate task of the ANDS strategy, with assistance from the donor community, is to expand energy avail- ability at a price that covers cost (for all but the poorest members of society) and to do so in the most cost effective manner.",""],[1,"64","2","Transmission Line and Power Generation Investment","Investments in transmission lines and power generation will increase access to electricity, improving productivity.",""],[1,"73","11","Private Sector Participation in Power Generation and Distribution","Involve the private sector to expedite power generation and distribution projects in urban centers as well as in rural areas.",""],[1,"73","12","Private Sector Power Generation and Distribution Legal Framework","Developing the legal framework to permit and encourage power generation and distribution by the private sector;",""],[1,"73","13","Acceleration of Priority Power Generation Initiatives","Accelerating the execution of prior- ity power generation initiatives;",""],[1,"107","10","Energy Infrastructure Investment Expansion","A central thrust in the strategy will be increased investment in energy related infrastructure.",""],[1,"107","10","Hydropower Project Development","The three key hydro power projects (described above) will substantially add to generating capacity, but also support agricultural growth and improved management of water resources.",""],[1,"107","10","Private Investment Mobilization for Energy","Substantial additional private investment is also required.",""],[1,"107","10","Donor Fund Leveraging for Private Capital Access","The Government will leverage currently avail- able donor funds to ensure longer term access to private investment and capital.",""],[1,"107","10","Private Investment Support Policies","Policies to support private investments will be estab- lished.",""],[1,"107","10","Government Procurement, Accounting, Contracting and Reporting Reform","Improved procurement, accounting functions, contracting and reporting at the gov- ernment level will be put in place.",""],[1,"107","13","Key Power Infrastructure Projects Implementation","The Government will give priority to the implementation of four major infrastructure projects",""],[1,"108","1","Hydropower Plant Development and Irrigation Expansion Projects","(i) the Kokcha-e-Ulia Hydro Power Plant, which will generate a total of 1,900 MW and add 57,000 hectares of irrigated agricultural land; (ii) the Baghdara Hydro Power Plant, which will generate 210 MW, benefit more than 105,000 families, increasing irrigation coverage; (iii) the Irrigation and Power Project of Kokcha-e-Sofla, which will generate 100 MW of power, benefiting more than 950,000 families in the area; and (iv) the Sorobi II Hydro Power Plant, which will generate 180MW and help meet electricity needs in Kabul.",""],[1,"108","1","Public Power Grid Rehabilitation and Upgrade","Other key projects include expansion of the public power grid through the rehabilitation and upgrading of Kabul and other key infrastructure areas (i.e., distribution lines, substations, meters);",""],[1,"108","1","National Power System Development","the development of the North East Power System (NEPS) to be followed by the South East Power System (SEPS), Western and Eastern Power Systems;",""],[1,"108","1","Sheberghan Gas and Oil Field Development","the development of the Sheberghan gas and oil fields;",""],[1,"108","1","Power Import Transmission and Distribution Expansion","construction of new transmission and related distribution for power imports;",""],[1,"108","1","Power Dispatch, Control, and Reactive Power Systems Installation","installation of a dispatch and control system as well as a reactive power system.",""],[1,"109","1","Near-Term Power Generation Expansion","Key areas for investment in the near term include: (i) increased domestic power generation that includes new hydro power, natural gas and coal-fired power facilities;",""],[1,"109","1","Power Distribution Infrastructure Expansion","power distribution including lines, substations and metering;",""],[1,"109","1","Power Construction and Services Outsourcing","power construction and services (i.e., outsourcing);",""],[1,"109","1","Coal, Natural Gas, and Oil Exploration and Exploitation","exploration and exploitation of coal, natural gas and oil;",""],[1,"109","2","Expanded Public Power Grid Rehabilitation and Expansion","The Government is committed to improving energy access for people across the country.",""],[1,"233","5","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Expansion","The government uses Public- Private Partnerships to ex- pand infrastructure",""],[1,"233","6","Private Sector Power Generation and Distribution Legal Reform","Ensure the evolving legal framework to permit and encourage power genera- tion and distribution by the private sector, including through the establishment of Public-Private Partnerships (PPPs).",""],[1,"233","8","Priority Power Generation and Transmission Initiatives","Accelerate the execution of priority power generation initiatives: (a) Sheberghan natural gas generation project; (b) the high voltage transmission line from Tajikistan.",""],[1,"233","10","Electricity Distribution System Improvement","Improve distribution system, beginning with Kabul, including through out- sourcing of billing and collections and by providing information to the private sector on opportunities to invest in electricity supply.",""],[1,"233","12","Corporatization of DABM","Corporatize DABM (national electricity company) with qualified management team selected through transparent process.",""],[1,"233","16","Negotiation for Competitive Cross-Border Power Supply Terms","Negotiate competitive terms for reliable power supply from Central Asia.",""],[1,"237","14","Enabling Environment for Private Sector Energy Investment","An enabling environment for private sector investment in energy sector created",""],[1,"237","15","Tender Issuance for Power Exploration and Exploitation","Issuance of tenders for exploration and exploitation in northern country notably for power",""],[1,"237","18","Private Distribution Projects","Implement Private distribution projects",""],[1,"238","20","Thermal Generation Spare Parts and Fuel Procurement","Procure spare parts and fuel for thermal generation",""],[1,"238","21","Transmission and Distribution System Rehabilitation and Upgrade","Repair existing transmission and distribution systems including rehabilitating and/or upgrading substations and distribution networks",""],[1,"238","22","Cross-Border Transmission Meter Installation","Install meters for cross border transmission",""],[1,"238","23","Thermal Plant Rehabilitation","Repair existing thermal plants",""],[1,"238","25","ICE Technical Assistance","Implement ICE technical assistance (ADB)",""],[1,"238","28","Electricity Loss Reduction Measures","Take appropriate measures to reduce electricity loss",""],[1,"239","20","Private Sector Power Generation Rights Tendering","Private Sector promotion in close as formalization of existing operator rights; tender for new rights (i.e., to support power generation)",""],[1,"240","4","Afghan System Operation and Maintenance Capacity Building","Build Afghan capacity to operate and maintain system",""],[1,"240","8","Project Management Unit Establishment","Establish Project Management Unit",""]],"28":[[1,"36","2","Energy Sector Market Transition and Institutional Reform","The Government will also take steps to provide the basis for the transition of the sector from public provision to private provision of electricity.",""],[1,"36","2","New Energy Sector Institutional Arrangements","As the Afghan energy sector moves from primarily state owned operations to a more private market orientation, new institutional arrangements will be established.",""],[1,"36","3","Transparent Energy Regulatory Framework and Pricing Reform","This will change with a major effort to set up a transparent regulatory framework and a pricing system that is designed to encourage private sector investment in the sector.",""],[1,"36","3","Energy Sector Institutional Reform and Capacity Development","A new market oriented paradigm, significant institutional changes and considerable capacity development will be established under guidance from the Inter-Ministerial Commission for Energy (ICE).",""],[1,"36","3","Energy Ministry Reorientation to Regulatory Functions","As the energy line ministries shift from operating as production-based institutions to becoming policy making regulatory agencies, staff capacity and in-house functions will be reoriented to market practices.",""],[1,"36","3","Energy Asset Restructuring and Commercialization Plan","The Government will assess its sector assets and establish a plan for liquidation, restructuring and commercialization or sale.",""],[1,"36","4","Corporatization and Commercialization of National Power Operations","for the corporatization and commercialization of national power operations.",""],[1,"105","2","Energy Sector Reform to Attract Private Investment","it represents a major reform in the energy sector designed to attract private investment into the power sector and development of energy resources.",""],[1,"105","6","Energy Sector Governance and Market Reform","The Government puts great emphasis on expanding domestic capacity for electricity generation and will take steps to provide the basis for a transition of the sector from public to private provision of electricity.",""],[1,"105","6","Private Sector Enabling Environment for Energy Investment","The ANDS strategic vision and goal for the energy sector strategy is: \"An energy sector that provides drivers of growth in the economy with long term reliable, affordable energy based on market-based private sector investment and public sector oversight\".",""],[1,"105","6","Energy Sector Institutional Arrangements Reform","As the Afghan energy sector moves from primarily state owned operations to a more private market orientation, new institutional arrangements will be established.",""],[1,"106","7","Power Sector Commercialization Programme","Since 2006, there has been an on-going program for commercialization of operations in power operations by the state owned power company, DABM.",""],[1,"107","11","Market-Oriented Energy Sector Reform","A new market oriented paradigm will be developed, supported by significant institutional strengthening and capacity development.",""],[1,"107","11","Market-Based Energy Sector Governance Reform","The key programs of the sector are: (ii) market based sector governance;",""],[1,"108","2","Energy Sector Governance Restructuring","The Government will consolidate energy planning and policy-making functions through the Inter-Ministerial Commission for Energy (ICE).",""],[1,"108","2","Energy Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework","A viable legal and regulatory framework will be established that includes",""],[1,"108","5","National Power Operations Corporatization and Commercialization Support","In particular the Government will provide more support for the corporatization and commercialization of national power operations.",""],[1,"108","5","Energy Sector Accounting and Procurement Reform","Commercialization and increasing the efficiency of the state power company DABM includes, for example, the installation of international accounting and procurement practices that will follow in other energy sub-sectors.",""],[1,"108","6","Private Sector Energy Investment Enabling Environment","Improve the enabling environment for pri- vate sector investment.",""],[1,"109","1","Transparent Electricity Licensing and Private Investment Enablement","the regulator, which will adopt a transparent licensing regime and establish conditions that will attract private investment in electricity generation and in the related fields of mining, natural gas and hydropower.",""],[1,"109","1","Market-Friendly Energy Investment Enabling Environment","A market-friendly enabling environment to facilitate private investment will be developed.",""],[1,"110","2","Energy Sector Expansion and Private Sector Participation Strategy","The energy sector strategy therefore combines efforts supported by donor funding to expand public sector operations while laying the groundwork for much greater involvement by the private sector investors.",""],[1,"272","17","Private Sector Energy Investment Enabling Environment","An enabling environment for private sector in- vestment in energy sector created Expanded public power grid",""],[1,"273","3","Renewable Energy Development and Use Strategy","A strategy for the development and use of renew- able energies will be developed by March 2008",""]],"29":[[1,"109","5","Regional Energy Trade and Import Arrangements","Power purchase agreements (PPA) are being final- ized for regular power imports from neighboring countries and new PPAs are being negotiated for increased power im- ports.",""],[1,"109","5","CASA-1300 Power Project Participation","Afghanistan joined as a full member the Central Asia South Asia (CASA) 1300mw project in November 2007.",""],[1,"109","5","TAPI Natural Gas Pipeline Planning","Afghanistan is also participating in ongoing planning for a Turkmenistan-Afghanistan-Pakistan-India (TAPI) natural gas pipeline.",""]],"30":[[1,"107","11","Rural Electrification and Renewable Energy Programme","The key programs of the sector are: (iii) rural electrification and renewable energy;",""],[1,"109","1","Rural Energy Services Installation and Operation","installation and operation of rural energy services.",""],[1,"109","3","Rural Energy Services Expansion","Increase Access to rural energy services: Micro-hydro, solar, waste and even small diesel power and energy generating sources will be promoted to improve rural access.",""],[1,"109","4","Private Sector Off-Grid Renewable Power Support","Several private firms are involved in the development of off-grid power supplies based on wind or solar power and efforts will be made to encourage the development of these activities, or at least not undermine their viability with subsidized public sector activities.",""],[1,"109","6","Energy Sector Investment and Rural Power Access Programme","The energy sector will provide essential power supplies needed for private sector development, job creation and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"109","6","Off-Grid Renewable Energy Promotion Initiative","efforts will be made to encourage the development of these activities.",""],[1,"110","1","Wind and Solar Energy Support Policies","There will be scope for using wind and so- lar energy, particularly in areas away from the regional grids, and the relative benefits of this type of energy should be recognized in policies to support their use.",""],[1,"119","6","Rural Electrification Program","The Rural Electrification Program will result in over 4,000 villages being connected to local electrical facilities.",""],[1,"233","14","Pilot Non-Grid Rural and Small-City Power Initiatives","Launch pilot initiatives in non-grid small and medium-scale provision in smaller cities and in community-based rural power, including micro-hydro power.",""],[1,"237","16","Private Sector CNG Production, Transport, and Supply Development","Develop private sector opportunities to take on long-term production, transport, supply of CNG",""],[1,"238","4","Oil Refinery Assessment and Revitalization","Assess and revitalize oil refinery",""],[1,"238","5","Sheberghan Gas Fields and Power Plant Development","Development of Sheberghan Gas Fields and Power Plant",""],[1,"238","6","Regional Cooperation for Energy Sector Projects","Promotion of regional cooperation to facilitate various projects under the energy sector",""],[1,"238","16","Environmental Awareness for Energy Sector Policymakers","Awareness generation of policy makers on the environmental issues so that they are taken care of in all projects in the energy sector.",""],[1,"238","18","Pilot CNG Conversion for Public Vehicles","Leveraging available donor assistance, pilot CNG for public vehicles (i.e., buses) and taxis; conversion of engines, fitting gas pump stations.",""],[1,"238","24","National Energy Conservation Program","Starting National Energy Conservation Program (NECP)",""],[1,"239","11","Energy Provision in Narcotics Cultivation Areas","Priority to providing energy in areas having substantial narcotics cultivation to promote economic activity to generate alternate livelihoods",""],[1,"239","14","Rural Energy and Microfinance Linkage Program","Link rural energy with micro and small finance programs",""],[1,"239","15","Comprehensive Rural Energy Program","Develop a comprehensive and appropriate rural energy program",""],[1,"239","22","Rural-Remote Energy Policy Development","In collaboration with National Regulation Utility Commission (NURC), develop Rural-remote Energy Policy","National Regulation Utility Commission (NURC)"],[1,"240","9","Natural Gas Pricing Regime","Establish Pricing regime for natural gas",""],[1,"240","10","Clarification of Government Terms of Reference for Rural Energy Roles","Define Government roles in clearly defining TORs for MRRD and MEW on rural energy aspects",""],[1,"240","14","Rural Livelihoods and Energy Department Organizational and Staffing Plan","Develop and implement the organizational structure and staffing plan for Ru- ral Livelihoods and Energy Department (RLED)",""]],"31":[[1,"42","7","Range-Land and Forest Restoration and Sustainable Use","Environmental protection efforts are geared to: restoration and sustainable use of range- lands and forests;",""],[1,"42","7","Biodiversity Conservation Programme","conservation of biodiversity;",""],[1,"42","7","Community-Based Natural Resource Management","encouragement to commu- nity based natural resource management, pre- vention and/or abatement of pollution; and improved environmental management, educa- tion and awareness.",""],[1,"167","5","Community Natural Resource Management Capacity Development","The Government will provide capacity development to assist communities to be able to manage their natural resources and implement projects based on sustainable use.",""],[1,"179","2","Rangeland and Forest Restoration and Sustainable Use Programme","The strategy elaborates priority programs areas for environmental management based on thematic strategies in- cluding: restoration and sustainable use of rangelands and forests",""],[1,"179","2","Biodiversity Conservation Programme","The strategy elaborates priority programs areas for environmental management based on thematic strategies in- cluding: conservation of biodi- versity",""],[1,"179","2","Natural and Cultural Heritage Site Preservation","The strategy elaborates priority programs areas for environmental management based on thematic strategies in- cluding: preservation of natural and cultural heritage sites",""],[1,"179","2","Community-Based Natural Resource Management","The strategy elaborates priority programs areas for environmental management based on thematic strategies in- cluding: encouragement to community- based natural resource management",""],[1,"258","8","Rangeland and Forest Restoration and Sustainable Use Programme","Restoration and Sustainable Use of Rangelands and forests, conservation of bio-diversity, and encouragement to Community Based Natural Resource Man- agement",""],[1,"258","8","Community-Based Natural Resource Management Promotion","Restoration and Sustainable Use of Rangelands and forests, conservation of bio-diversity, and encouragement to Community Based Natural Resource Man- agement",""],[1,"261","15","Greening of Afghanistan Public Works Program","Develop the new public work program (Greening of Afghanistan) to support re-foresting",""]],"32":[[1,"111","2","Environmental Regulatory Frameworks and Management Services","Environmental regulatory frameworks and management services will be established for the protection of air and water quality, waste management and natural resources.",""],[1,"119","4","National Resource Management Committees and Plans","The National Resource Program will establish National Resource Management committees and develop national resource management plans for forests, rangeland, wildlife and desertification control.",""],[1,"179","1","NEPA Capacity Development for Environmental Governance","Therefore the ANDS focuses on developing National Environment Protection Agency's (NEPA) capacity to perform its regulatory, coordination and policy-making duties.","National Environment Protection Agency (NEPA)"],[1,"179","3","EIA Awareness and Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening EIA awareness and institu- tional capacity of NEPA and the line minis- tries will be accorded priority.","NEPA | the line ministries"],[1,"179","4","Inter-Ministerial and Consultative Group Coordination Mechanism","Strategic coordination of the ANDS is to take place on a sector-by-sector basis through a inter-ministerial and consulta- tive group (CG) mechanisms.",""],[1,"179","5","Environmental Mainstreaming and Monitoring Framework","Environment as a cross-cutting issue, must be mainstreamed across all sectors and in each program area through the development of policy bench- marks to ensure that the Government, do- nors and implementing agencies follow established norms with respect to the in- corporation of environmental considera- tions into the design and implementation of projects, and provide adequate over- sight and monitoring of the environmental impacts of economic and social develop- ment projects.",""],[1,"179","6","Institutional Arrangement for Environment Theme Implementation and Monitoring","There is a defined institutional arrange- ment for implementation and monitoring of environment themes.",""],[1,"179","6","ANDS Implementation Issue Assessment and Reporting Mechanism","Their assess- ment must be frank, identifying the prob- lems encountered in the implementation of these activities.",""],[1,"179","6","Progress Reporting to Oversight Committee and JCMB","This will allow the Gov- ernment to more effectively address the issues and meet their obligation of report- ing to the Oversight Committee (OSC) and the JCMB on progress in fulfilling these objectives.",""]],"33":[[1,"64","1","Disaster Preparedness and Response Strengthening","Building more efficient disaster preparedness and response will decrease the risk of falling into poverty.",""],[1,"84","12","Policy Action Group Emergency Response Mechanism","The Na- tional Security Advisor identifies the needs and requirements of the sector and leads the Policy Action Group (PAG) which has been estab- lished as an emergency response mechanism to address the deteriorating security conditions in the six southern provinces.",""],[1,"84","17","Crisis Response and Emergency Management Participation","Play an active part to solve crisis and con- trol emergency situations;",""],[1,"84","18","Civilian Crisis and Emergency Assistance","Render assistance to civilian officials to control any emerging security crisis, natu- ral disasters and emergency situations;",""],[1,"91","7","National Disaster Management and Mitigation Policy Implementation","The national disaster man- agement and mitigation policy will be im- plemented.",""],[1,"167","6","Disaster Preparedness Institutional Linkages Program","Strategy is to develop institutional linkages in the areas of collaborative research, technology transfers and training/skills enhancement, and the exchange of scientific information with regard to Afghanistan's disaster preparedness program.",""],[1,"169","12","ANDMA Disaster Preparedness Coordination Capacity Strengthening","To improve ANDMA's capacity for co- ordinating the disaster preparedness",""],[1,"169","17","ANDAMA Equipment Modernization and Regional Warehouse Development","To modernize ANDAMA's equipment and build regional warehouses",""],[1,"259","15","Disaster Early Warning System Establishment","Support the establishment of disaster early warning system",""],[1,"259","16","Disaster and Epidemic Preparedness and Response System","Establish and operationalise a system for mitigation, preparedness and response to natural disasters and plant/animal diseases and epidemics",""],[1,"264","13","Legislative Reform to Strengthen ANDMA's Coordinating Role","Adjust the legislation to clearly reflect the leading role of the ANDMA in co- ordinating the national efforts for disaster preparedness and response but also for implementing of key programs and projects.",""],[1,"264","14","NGO Disaster Risk Reduction Coordination Network","Establish a coordination network of NGO's which are working in the field of disaster risk reduction by creating department of NGO in ANDMA structure",""],[1,"264","15","Academic Consultation Network for Prevention and Mitigation Projects","Establish academic consultation network with academy of science, faculty of Engineering and Polytechnic University for designing, prevention & mitigation projects",""],[1,"264","16","Provincial Emergency Operation Centers Establishment","Establish Emergency Operation Centers (EOCs) at the provincial level",""],[1,"264","17","Regional Response Centers and Teams","Establish response centers and teams at the regional level",""],[1,"264","18","Community Emergency Response System","Establish community emergency response system",""],[1,"264","19","Early Warning System Establishment","Establish effective early warning system",""],[1,"264","20","Back-up Communication System Development","Develop back-up communication system based on Codan",""],[1,"264","21","ANDMA Office and Operational Center Establishment","Establish ANDMA's offices along with the operational centers",""],[1,"264","22","Regional Aid and Equipment Storage Construction","Construct 12 regional storages for aid assistance and equipment",""],[1,"264","23","Annual Disaster Preparedness and Response Planning","Approve regular annual plans for disaster preparedness and response",""],[1,"264","24","National and Sub-national Risk and Vulnerability Information Collection and Disaster Risk Analysis","Complete collecting information related to risks and vulnerabilities at the na- tional and sub-national level and finalizes disaster risk analysis",""],[1,"265","1","Disaster Preparedness and Response Planning Guideline","Develop a guideline for disaster preparedness and response planning",""],[1,"265","2","Standardized Operational Procedures for Rapid Assessment and Response","Develop Standardized Operational Procedures(SPO) for quick assessment and response, reporting, and for rapid mobilization of international assistance",""],[1,"265","3","Provincial Disaster Management Plan Development and Operationalization","Develop and operationalize the provincial disaster management plans",""],[1,"265","4","Public Disaster Risk Awareness Campaign","Improve public awareness activities and raise national awareness about disaster risks and vulnerabilities",""],[1,"265","5","Disaster Risk Reduction Integration in Policies and Plans","Integrate disaster risk reduction in national and sub-national policies and plans",""],[1,"269","26","Disaster Preparedness and Response System","By Jaddi 1389 (end-2010), an effective system of disaster preparedness and response will be in place.",""],[1,"285","25","Disaster Preparedness and Response System","By end-2010 an effective system of disaster preparedness and response will be in place",""]],"34":[[1,"35","5","Regional Transport and Transit Infrastructure Development","Increased priority will be given to regional economic cooperation initia- tives aimed at developing regional transporta- tion and transit infrastructure, facilitating re- gional trade and investment flows and devel- oping Afghanistan as a regional business hub linking Central and East Asia with the Middle East and South Asia.",""],[1,"37","4","National Transport Network Upgrade and Maintenance Programme","The ANDS strategic goal for the transport sector is to have a safe, integrated transportation network that ensures connectivity and that enables low-cost and reliable movement of people and goods domestically as well as to and from foreign destinations.",""],[1,"37","4","Ring Road Rehabilitation and Road Maintenance System","Afghanistan will have a fully upgraded and maintained ring road, as well as roads connecting the ring road to neighboring countries by end-2008 and a fiscally sustainable system for road maintenance by end-2007;",""],[1,"37","4","Airport Compliance and Domestic Airport Upgrading Programme","By end-2010, Kabul International Airport and Herat Airport will achieve full International Civil Aviation Organization compliance; Mazar-i-Sharif, Jalalabad and Kandahar will be upgraded with runway repairs, air navigation, fire and rescue and communications equipment; seven other domestic airports will be upgraded to facilitate domestic air transportation;",""],[1,"37","5","Road Network Rehabilitation and Rural Access Road Improvement","The Government continues to give high priority to rehabilitate a badly damaged road system.",""],[1,"38","1","Rural Road Maintenance through Local Community Funding","Careful consideration will be given to increasing employment oppor- tunities, and assuring that the local resources or funds channeled through local communities are effectively used to maintain the rural roads established as part of this strategy.",""],[1,"64","2","National Road Network Expansion and Rural Roads Construction","Expanding the national road network, includ- ing the construction of the rural roads, will al- low poor households to diversify income gen- eration - from low profitable crops to more profitable activates such as trade, services and small businesses.",""],[1,"118","12","National Rural Access Program","The National Rural Access Program will support rural road construction and reha-",""],[1,"121","6","Ring Road Upgrade and Road Maintenance System","Afghanistan will have a fully upgraded and maintained ring road, as well as roads connecting the ring road to neighboring countries by end-2008 and a fiscally sustainable system for road maintenance;",""],[1,"121","6","Airport Compliance and Domestic Airport Upgrading Programme","By end-2010, Kabul International Airport and Herat Airport will achieve full International Civil Aviation Organization compliance; Mazar-i-Sharif, Jalalabad and Kandahar will be upgraded with runway repairs, air navigation, fire and rescue and communications equipment; seven other domestic airports will be upgraded to facilitate domestic air transportation;",""],[1,"122","4","Road Maintenance and Rehabilitation System","A system for road maintenance and rehabilitation urgently needs to be put into place and made operational.",""],[1,"122","10","Road Rehabilitation and Rural Access Improvement Programme","The Government continues to give high prior- ity to rehabilitate a badly damaged road sys- tem.",""],[1,"123","1","Rural Road Maintenance through Local Community Funding","Careful considera- tion will be given to increasing employment opportunities, and assuring that the local re- sources or funds channeled through local communities are effectively used to maintain the rural roads established as part of this strat- egy.",""],[1,"123","1","Regional and National Highways and Provincial Roads Program","The main programs of the strategy are (i) Regional, National Highways and Provincial Roads",""],[1,"123","1","Rural Road Program","The main programs of the strategy are (i) Regional, National Highways and Provincial Roads (ii) Rural Road (iii) Urban Transport (iv) Civil Aviation (v) Transport Sector Mainte- nance (vi) Pubic Transport (vii) Railway Pro- gram.",""],[1,"123","1","Transport Sector Maintenance Program","The main programs of the strategy are (i) Regional, National Highways and Provincial Roads (ii) Rural Road (iii) Urban Transport (iv) Civil Aviation (v) Transport Sector Mainte- nance (vi) Pubic Transport (vii) Railway Pro- gram.",""],[1,"123","10","Secondary and Rural Roads Investment Programme","Undertake transport development through investments in secondary and rural roads to significantly increase provincial and village access to the national road system.",""],[1,"163","12","Transport Connectivity Improvement","Improved transportation links will significantly improve Afghanistan's links with regional and international markets.",""],[1,"240","18","Road Rehabilitation, Improvement and Maintenance Program","Massive road rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance programs.",""],[1,"240","20","Road Rehabilitation, Improvement and Maintenance Programme","Massive road rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance programs.",""],[1,"240","21","Road Rehabilitation, Improvement and Maintenance Program","Massive road rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance programs (with its entire infrastructure including drainage, walkways and street lighting system for urban roads).",""],[1,"240","23","Road and Air Infrastructure Upgrading and Maintenance","The road and air infrastructure will be built and maintained to a higher quality, giving road users lower costs.",""],[1,"240","23","Railway Link Feasibility Study","Whereas, the Feasibility Study of the railway links will be done.",""],[1,"240","24","Road User Fee Rationalization and Road Fund Establishment","Rationalize road user fees (one fee) and use funds to establish a road fund",""],[1,"241","8","Urban Road Rehabilitation, Improvement and Maintenance Program","Massive road rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance programs (with its entire infrastructure including drainage, walkways and street lighting system for urban roads).",""],[1,"241","10","Public Transport Provision Improvement","Improve Public Transport Provision in Urban and inter-provincial (34 prov- inces) (with having bus and truck terminals in all the provincial centers)",""],[1,"241","24","Project Monitoring and Contract Management Capacity Building","Capacity building specially in the areas of project monitoring and contract management",""],[1,"241","24","Procurement Law Regulatory Framework Development","Completing the regulatory framework- developing the regulatory framework for the implementation of the Procurement law, developing roads standards",""],[1,"241","24","Road Standards Development","developing roads standards",""],[1,"242","6","Transport Sector Inter-ministerial Working Group","Establish a Transport Sector Inter-ministerial Working Group to determine the lines of authority between the transportation-related governance institutions and the roles and responsibilities of each institution.",""],[1,"242","8","Inter-Ministerial Costing Committee","Create an inter-ministerial costing committee to work with the Ministry of Finance to cost out annually programs that take five to fifteen years to imple- ment","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"242","16","Transport Sector Transparency Systems","Put in place systems to improve transparency in all functions of the govern- ment in the transport sector",""],[1,"242","18","Local and Provincial Road Improvement Autonomy","Give more autonomy to local communities and the Provincial Governments to determine how and when rural roads are improved, as well as provincial roads",""],[1,"242","19","Transport Sector Governance Coordination Mechanism","Improve coordination between transport sector governance institutions, the MoI and ISAF so that the transport sector can better develop in conflict- affected areas of the country as soon as possible","MoI | ISAF"],[1,"242","23","Annual Data and Database Assessment for Transport Planning","Annual assessment of data collected and databases maintained and updated in all planning departments, including municipalities, mapping progress against the goal of \"best practices\" data collection and databases for transport sector planning, with necessary funding mechanisms and capacity building programs",""],[1,"243","2","Ministry Planning Capacity Strengthening for Transport Functions","Strengthening the planning capacity of ministry staff for road transport, air- ports, and rail functions so that the ministry staff can perform feasibility stud- ies, Master planning, and multi-modal planning, as well as asset management planning, to international standards",""],[1,"243","5","Transport Sector Contracting and Regulatory Reform","Pass legislation and enabling regulations to allow transport sector governing institutions to competitively engage and manage private contractors, private contract supervision engineers to maintain roads, airports and other transport infrastructure, also regulations that protect the normal market rights of those contractors.",""],[1,"243","11","Fair Market Value Land Valuation Reform for Transport Projects","Reform laws relating to determining \"fair market value\" of lands purchased for transport sector improvements",""],[1,"243","13","Axle-Load Limit Violation Fee and Enforcement System","Develop and put in place an axle-load limit violation fees and an enforcement system",""],[1,"244","10","New Road Construction Feasibility Studies","Feasibility studies for building new roads",""],[1,"244","12","Urban Asphalt Road Reconstruction Programme","Increase reconstruction of asphalt roads in major and secondary cities",""],[1,"244","14","New Road Construction and Paving Programme","Design and build (asphalted) new roads",""]],"35":[[1,"121","6","Airport Compliance and Domestic Airport Upgrading Programme","By end-2010, Kabul International Airport and Herat Airport will achieve full International Civil Aviation Organization compliance; Mazar-i-Sharif, Jalalabad and Kandahar will be upgraded with runway repairs, air navigation, fire and rescue and communications equipment; seven other domestic airports will be upgraded to facilitate domestic air transportation;",""],[1,"121","10","Airport Rehabilitation and Expansion Programme","Four major airports (at Herat, Mazar-i- Sharif, Jalalabad, and Kandahar) as well as seven other regional airports are either slated for, or currently undergoing, exten- sive rehabilitation and expansion.",""],[1,"122","6","Open Skies Civil Aviation Regulatory Framework","much must still be done to create a truly 'open skies' regulatory framework that both encourages new entry but maintains international standards for safety.",""],[1,"123","1","Civil Aviation Program","The main programs of the strategy are (i) Regional, National Highways and Provincial Roads (ii) Rural Road (iii) Urban Transport (iv) Civil Aviation (v) Transport Sector Mainte- nance (vi) Pubic Transport (vii) Railway Pro- gram.",""],[1,"123","4","Kabul New Airport Development","The Government gives high priority to the development of a new airport in Kabul.",""],[1,"123","4","Airport and Civil Aviation Compliance Programme","the Government will implement programs to ensure that the principal airports and the civil aviation authorities conform to the requirements of the ICAO and IATA, including establishing a new Civil Aviation Authority to promote air transport in a competitive environment.",""],[1,"123","4","Open Skies Aviation Regulatory Framework","A regulatory framework will be introduced to encourage private investment under an 'open skies' policy.",""],[1,"123","9","Kabul International Airport Investment","The Government will seek investment in a new international airport in the Kabul area to provide Afghanistan with a modern international airport",""],[1,"123","9","Civil Aviation Standards Compliance Programme","implement programs to ensure that the principal airports and the civil aviation authorities conform to the requirements of the ICAO and IATA",""],[1,"123","9","Civil Aviation Authority Establishment","including establishing a new Civil Aviation Authority to promote air transport in a competitive environment",""],[1,"123","9","Open Skies Aviation Regulatory Framework","A regulatory framework will be introduced to encourage private sector investment under an 'open skies' policy",""],[1,"241","15","Massive Reconstruction of Kabul International Airport and Herat Airport","Massive reconstruction program (Kabul Int'l Airport, Herat in compliance with ICAO and IATA requirements)",""],[1,"241","16","Airport Reconstruction Program","Massive reconstruction program (Mazar-i-Sharif, Jalalabad, Kandahar airports)",""],[1,"241","17","Domestic Airports Reconstruction Program","Massive reconstruction program (Seven Other Domestic airports)",""],[1,"241","21","Civil Aviation Authority Establishment and Airspace Control Restoration","Institutional reform programs and a reduction in the requirement of ISAF to use air facilities (Create a new Civil Aviation Authority (CAA), and restore control of Afghan airspace to the Civil Aviation Authority.)",""],[1,"274","8","Airport Upgrading and Safety Equipment Installation","Mazar-i-Sharif, Jalalabad and Kandahar will be up- graded with runway repairs, air navigation, fire and rescue, and communications equipment by March 2011.",""],[1,"274","11","Domestic Airport Upgrading Programme","Seven other domestic airports will be upgraded to facilitate domestic air transportation by March 2011.",""],[1,"274","16","Airport Services Tariff Plan Development","ICAO person- nel is developing a tariff plan for various component of airport services on the basis of the Airport master Planning study report of 2004.",""],[1,"274","19","Civil Aviation Authority Establishment and Airspace Control Restoration","Create a new Civil Aviation Authority (CAA), and restore control of Afghan airspace to the Civil Aviation Authority.",""],[1,"274","22","Ministry Capacity Training Program","To enhance capacity of the Ministry, a train- ing program has been finalized to the tune of 640000.",""],[1,"275","1","Fire Fighter Training Programme","30 Fire Fighter have been trained in Oman and another 17 other personnel will be trained in 2008.",""],[1,"275","1","Air Traffic Control, CNS, and Fire Fighting On-the-Job Training","Under the Transition Plan also for key functions such as ATC, CNS and Fire Fighting on the job trainings will be provided by ICAO experts.",""],[1,"275","1","FAA Academy Student Training Programme","Further 200 students was sent to FAA academy in U.S.A and 20 others will be sent by end of 2008.",""]],"36":[[1,"123","1","Urban Transport Program","The main programs of the strategy are (i) Regional, National Highways and Provincial Roads (ii) Rural Road (iii) Urban Transport (iv) Civil Aviation (v) Transport Sector Mainte- nance (vi) Pubic Transport (vii) Railway Pro- gram.",""],[1,"123","1","Public Transport Program","The main programs of the strategy are (i) Regional, National Highways and Provincial Roads (ii) Rural Road (iii) Urban Transport (iv) Civil Aviation (v) Transport Sector Mainte- nance (vi) Pubic Transport (vii) Railway Pro- gram.",""],[1,"123","7","Urban Transportation Management Strengthening","Municipal transportation management will be strengthened to improve urban road quality, road network maintenance, road network planning, and transportation facilities and services.",""],[1,"123","7","Coordinated Urban Road Network Planning","The development of the national and regional road networks will be coordinated with municipal authorities with responsibilities for the urban road networks.",""],[1,"132","5","Urban Transportation Management Improvement","Improve urban transportation man- agement through improvements to circulation and road networks, transportation facilities and services by function, type, capacity, and condi- tion, bus system, bicycles and pedestrians, transportation demand management including on- and off-street parking system management.",""]],"37":[[1,"162","5","Civil Aviation Authority Strengthening","a Civil Aviation Authority will be given greater responsibility for civil aviation development and safety.",""],[1,"163","8","Transportation Ministry Governance Reform","The strategy provides a framework to improve governance in Trans- portation Ministry.",""],[1,"163","10","Narcotics Smuggling Enforcement and Border Security Measures","Support enforcement activities of the MoI and police against narcotics smuggling.","MoI | police"],[1,"163","13","Transportation Training Institute Establishment","A Transportation Training Institute will be established to boost capacity of sector ministries and institutions.",""],[1,"163","13","Transport Planning Capacity Strengthening","This will help strengthen the planning capacity of staff for all transport modes for feasibility studies and infrastructure planning.",""],[1,"163","13","Transport Regulatory and Safety Enforcement Capacity Upgrade","Capacity will be increased so that Minis- try staff are able to conduct drivers' li- censing tests, vehicle safety inspections and enforce traffic flow regulations.",""],[1,"163","13","Civil Aviation Authority Capacity Enhancement","Capacity will also be increased in the Civil Aviation Authority in order to take over control of civilian airspace from interna- tional forces",""],[1,"273","19","Transport Policy and Regulatory Update and Management System Improvement","Having updated transport policies/regulation and improved transport management system to enforce and implement the states law and regulations related to the transport sector.",""]],"38":[[1,"39","3","University Cooperation with Foreign Universities","the university cooperation plans that have already commenced will allow universities in Afghanistan to interact and be supported by recognized foreign universities.",""],[1,"142","7","Higher Education Quality and Independence Improvement","priority policies include an increase in the quality and independence of the Higher Education system",""],[1,"143","1","Higher Education Quality Improvement and Expansion","The next stage of rehabilitation involves improving the quality of education in existing institutions and expanding the number of places available.",""],[1,"143","1","University Partnership Capacity-Building Initiative","Partnerships with foreign universities and other educational institutions have been introduced in about half the universities.",""],[1,"144","3","University System Modernization Reform","In higher education there is a need to transform the monolithic system into a modern system of independent, well managed universities that operate in the interests of their students.",""],[1,"146","6","Higher Education Capacity and Quality Improvement Strategy","This will involve increasing the capacity to accommodate more qualified students, together with an improvement in the quality of higher education by improving the number and quality of lecturers and offering a greater variety of courses.",""],[1,"146","6","University Autonomy Reform","There are plans to provide universities with greater autonomy.",""],[1,"146","6","University Cooperation and Lecturer Exchange Partnerships","A key component of the strategy is to encourage universities to enter into cooperative arrangements with other universities, both domestic and foreign, so that there can be an exchange of lecturers.",""],[1,"147","1","University Library and Laboratory Construction","carry out construction of buildings for libraries and laboratories in the existing universities.",""],[1,"147","1","University Funding Review and Autonomy Reform","It is also important as part of the strategy to conduct a review of university funding so that universities have greater autonomy.",""],[1,"166","5","University Upgrading and External Partnership Support","The universities both in Ka- bul and in the provinces are to be considerably up- graded, and each university will be supported by a rec- ognized external university.",""],[1,"253","12","Merit- and Gender-Balanced University Recruitment Policy","Policies that require new university professors and lecturers to be hired on the basis of academic merit and gender balance.",""],[1,"253","15","Recruit Foreign-Residing Afghan and Regional Professors","Recruit foreign residing Afghan and regional Professors through regional agreements",""],[1,"253","23","Study of Funding Models for Greater Autonomy","Investigate possible funding models that would provide greater autonomy",""],[1,"253","24","Reorganized and Streamlined Recruitment and Hiring Process","A reorganized and streamlined recruitment and hiring process (PRR) at the MoHE within its departments and at the 19 institutions of higher learning","MoHE"],[1,"253","25","Women Professionals Recruitment and Female Teacher Re-employment","Adopt strategy to hire more women professionals; re-train female teachers who were dismissed during the PRR process and re-employ them",""],[1,"253","27","Standards and Accreditation Body for Higher Education","Establish a separate body responsible for standards and accreditation all degree granting institutions and professional programs, public and private, in Afghani-",""],[1,"254","7","University Rehabilitation and Library and Laboratory Expansion","Rehabilitate existing universities and build new library and laboratory facilities at existing universities.",""],[1,"254","8","Dormitory Construction Programme","Construction of 24 new dormitories 12 for men and 12 for women",""],[1,"254","9","Recruitment of New University Professors","Recruit 3000 new professors, including qualified Afghan professors from the region (India, Pakistan, Tajikistan, and Iran).",""],[1,"254","11","New MA Programs in University Departments and Faculties","New MA programs at departments of languages and literature at Kabul Univer- sity, and new programs for the faculties of social science, law, economics, geology, engineering, agriculture, and Islamic law.",""],[1,"254","14","Girls' College Entrance Exam Review Classes","Conduct review class for girls to prepare them for college entrance examina- tions",""]],"39":[[1,"20","46","National Vocational Education and Training Authority","Proposed National Vocational Education and Training Authority",""],[1,"39","1","Teacher Training and Private Investment Promotion in Education","Increased priority will be given to teacher training and other mechanisms to encourage private sector investment in educational activities.",""],[1,"39","2","National Vocational Education and Training Authority Establishment","A new organization, the National Vocational Education and Training Authority (NVETA), will be established and will: (i) manage, but not operate, all vocational training institutions; (ii) set minimum core competencies for courses, carry out accreditation, and inspect vocational institutions, to ensure that they meet minimum standards; and (iii) call for tenders by ministries or by the private sector to operate vocational training facilities owned by the Government.",""],[1,"39","3","Contracting Private and NGO Providers for Educational Services","NVETA will contract with private sector groups or NGOs for provision of educational services.",""],[1,"39","5","Youth Education System Expansion and Rehabilitation","Extensive reforms have been introduced within the education strategy that is designed to assist youth.",""],[1,"39","5","Youth Rehabilitation Programmes","These include expansion of the education system; rehabilitation programs for young people whose education may have been limited because of the security situation; and reforms to vocational education to provide youth with marketable skills and better employment opportunities.",""],[1,"39","5","Vocational Education Reform","and reforms to vocational education to provide youth with marketable skills and better employment opportunities.",""],[1,"62","7","Skills Development Expansion for the Unemployed","Skills development programs will expand to help the unemployed obtain in demand qualifications.",""],[1,"67","4","Workforce Capacity Development Investment","A critical element in achieving this objective will be to substantially increase investment in the development of capacity of the workforce in order to expand employment opportunities and increase incomes.",""],[1,"79","4","Capacity Development and Skilled Workforce Investment","A critical element in achieving this objective will be to substantially increase investment in capacity development and creating a skilled workforce in order to expand employment opportunities and increase incomes.",""],[1,"142","7","Vocational Education Sustainability Reform","a move to place vocational educational on a more sustainable basis that can better contribute to emerging demands for skills.",""],[1,"144","3","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Improvement","Technical/vocational education and training are overloaded with academic subjects, have poor laboratory environments for practical training, are short of teaching aids and lack adequate training materials.",""],[1,"147","3","National Vocational Education and Training Board Establishment","The strategy that has been proposed to address this is to establish a new organization, National Vocational Education and Training Board (NVETB) that would manage, but not operate, all vocational training institutions.",""],[1,"147","3","Vocational Training Accreditation System","Part of the strategy would involve the development of an accreditation system for NGO and private sector providers who provide the bulk of vocational training.",""],[1,"147","3","Apprenticeship Formalization and Expansion Plan","By 2008 there would be a plan to formalize existing apprenticeship arrangements and expand the system.",""],[1,"147","5","National Institute of Administration and Management Establishment","Under the former a National Institute of Administration and Management is being established to address the lack of capacity in both the public and private sectors in basic project management, accountancy and booking and information and communication technology.",""],[1,"147","5","Nationwide Literacy and Productive Skills Programme","A nation-wide literacy and productive skills pro- gram is being launched that is envisaged mak- ing at least half a million people literate and numerate with skills that will enable them to find employment.",""],[1,"147","5","Coordination of Literacy Service Providers","This would be in addition to numerous other literacy service providers who coordinate their activities and interventions under the leadership of the National Literacy Centre.",""],[1,"147","6","Education Regulatory Boards Establishment","There are now firm proposals agreed to by relevant institutions to the establishment of regulatory bodies to operate across the whole of the education spectrum in order to improve educational standards.",""],[1,"147","6","Afghanistan National Qualifications Framework Implementation","It has been agreed to establish the necessary leg- islation for these Boards and for the implemen- tation of the Afghanistan National Qualifica- tions Framework.",""],[1,"147","6","Education and Skills Policy Committee","In order to oversee these components of the strategy a committee on education and skills policy has been estab- lished.","MoE | MoHE | MoLSAMD | MoF"],[1,"147","6","Capacity Utilization Monitoring Committee","A committee to monitor Capacity Utiliza- tion, headed by the Minister of economy will also be established.",""],[1,"164","17","Demand Reduction through Employment and Vocational Training","Contributions could be made to demand-reduction through sustainable employment and vocational training.",""],[1,"170","14","Afghan Workforce Skills Development Support","Government, donors, the private sector and NGOs will provide additional support to increase the skills of the Afghan workforce.",""],[1,"214","3","Human Capacity Development and Skilled Workforce Investment","A critical element in achieving this objective will be to substantially increase investment in human capacity development and creating a skilled workforce in order to expand employment opportunities and increase incomes.",""],[1,"235","9","Private Sector Short-Cycle Certificate Education Initiative","Facilitate private sector involvement to offer short-cycle certificate-level education for school leavers to rapidly develop the skills of young people and adults that are crucial to economic development.",""],[1,"235","11","Public-Private Partnership Framework for Education Provision","Establish the modality for public-private partnerships in the provision of education from basic education through to tertiary levels, including provision of professional and vocational education.",""],[1,"235","14","National Vocational and Professional Education Policy Framework","Establish a coherent national policy framework to guide professional and vo- cational education, linked to the overall higher education strategy that will ensure coordination, assign clear accountability and set world-class standards (including the process for licensing, certification and accreditation).",""],[1,"235","18","Market-Based Vocational and Professional Training Pilot","Consider quickly piloting specific market-based vocational and professional training initiatives through coalition of Government, industry groups and train- ing institutions with special consideration to women.",""],[1,"235","20","Private Sector Incentives for Skills Training Investment","Create incentives for private sector to invest in education specific to skills training, mentoring and on-the-job training.",""],[1,"235","24","Vocational and Professional Education Investment","Invest urgently in vocational and professional education to meet current needs, while simultaneously making parallel investments in reform of basic and",""],[1,"253","8","National Institute of Management and Administration Establishment","Establish National Institute of Management and Administration at MoE /TVET Department.","MoE /TVET Department"],[1,"254","19","Apprenticeship Formalization and Expansion Programme","Proposal to formalize existing apprenticeship arrangements and expand the system.",""],[1,"254","20","Vocational Education and Skills Development Capacity and Quality Improvement","Expand the capacity and improve the quality of Vocational Education and Skill Development",""],[1,"254","21","National VET System Capacity Enhancement","Improve the capacity of the national VET system to manage and deliver market-driven skills training and linkages to micro-credit and business development support services is planned to have increased.",""],[1,"254","22","National Vocational Education and Training Authority Establishment","Within the next 12 months, establish an independent National Vocational Edu- cation and Training Authority with the responsibility for managing and co-",""],[1,"255","2","National VET Policy Coordination Mechanism","coordinating national VET policy will be established.",""],[1,"255","2","Contracting Out of VET Institution Operations","Teaching and operation of individual VET institutions to be contracted out.",""],[1,"255","3","Targeted Training and Employment Opportunities for Vulnerable Women and Youth","Target the most vulnerable women and youth in the selection of training and provision of employment opportunities",""],[1,"255","6","Regional TVET School and Training Center Expansion","Develop an accessible, regional network of TVET schools and training centers, including 17 new schools and a school for those with special needs",""],[1,"255","7","Provincial Job Placement Centers","Establishment of job-placement centers in all 34 provinces",""],[1,"255","8","Competitive Procurement of Vocational Training Providers","The NSDP will procure the services of a variety of training providers (pri- vate/public) for the provision of training to 150,000 unemployed Afghan women and men through competitive bidding procedures",""],[1,"255","21","Education Advisory Committees","Establish advisory committees consisting of academy members and MoE and MoHE officials.","MoE | MoHE"],[1,"261","5","Priority Skills Development Training for the Most Vulnerable Groups","Change the NSDP terms of references to introduce the most vulnerable catego- ries as priority group for receiving the skill development trainings",""],[1,"261","12","Accreditation Framework for Skills Development Training Providers","Establish the institutional framework for accrediting service providers for skills development training and for issuing the certificates",""],[1,"261","25","Labor Market Study Completion","Complete the Labor Market Study to ensure that NSDP will meet the needs for",""],[1,"266","4","Employment Opportunities Improvement Program","Implement programs for improved employment opportunities, skill develop- ment, basic literacy and numeracy, access to health care",""],[1,"266","4","Skills Development Program","Implement programs for improved employment opportunities, skill develop- ment, basic literacy and numeracy, access to health care",""],[1,"266","4","Basic Literacy and Numeracy Program","Implement programs for improved employment opportunities, skill develop- ment, basic literacy and numeracy, access to health care",""],[1,"280","29","Unemployed Women and Men Training Programme","The NSDP will provide training to 150,000 unemployed Afghan women and men through competitive bidding procedures",""]],"40":[[1,"39","3","Expansion of Private and NGO School Provision","In the primary and secondary education area there will be an expansion in private and NGO schools, encouraged by a more accommodating regulatory environment.",""],[1,"39","3","Private Sector Provision of Preschool Education","Some areas will be left to the private sector, including preschool education.",""],[1,"63","2","Free Universal Education Policy","The Government will continue the policy of providing free universal education.",""],[1,"63","2","Inclusive Education Access for Persons with Disabilities","Higher attention will be given to supporting disabled peoples access to facilities, including specialized institutions and adjusting schools and universities to meeting their needs.",""],[1,"141","13","Balanced Expansion of Free Public Education","the State is obliged to devise and implement effective programs for a balanced expansion of education all over Afghanistan",""],[1,"142","6","Teacher Retraining Programme","Priority short term policies over the next four years involve re- training 70 percent of teachers in primary and secondary school",""],[1,"142","6","Education Enrollment Expansion","coping with increased demand for education by increasing enrol- ments from 6.1 million to 7.7 million",""],[1,"144","3","Primary School Curriculum Review and Textbook Production","Primary school curriculum has been reviewed and revised and new textbooks developed; production and distribution of these textbooks is still ongoing.",""],[1,"144","3","Secondary Curriculum and Learning Materials Development","While a new curriculum has been developed over the last 12 months, the development, production and distribution of textbooks, teachers' guides and learning materials will take a further 12-18 month period.",""],[1,"144","3","Teacher Training for New Curriculum Implementation","Teacher training in the use and teaching of the new curriculum still needs to be addressed.",""],[1,"145","2","Primary and Secondary Education Infrastructure and Equipment Expansion Program","the government plans to pursue an aggressive building and equipment program",""],[1,"145","4","Teacher Training Program","This indicates the need for a teacher training program that consists of both subject-content training as well as pedagogical training.",""],[1,"145","4","Curriculum Updating and Revision","The quality of education will also be improved by continued updating and revision of the curriculum and by increased community involvement in the management of education delivery.",""],[1,"145","4","Community Participation in Education Management","The quality of education will also be improved by continued updating and revision of the curriculum and by increased community involvement in the management of education delivery.",""],[1,"145","4","Teacher Monitoring and Coaching System","the systems put in place to monitor and coach teachers on a regular basis.",""],[1,"145","6","Curriculum Revision and Relevant Education Reform","The review and revision of curriculum to make Islamic education broad-based to allow multi- ple career paths for graduates, the teaching and learning of technical and vocational skills that are in demand and will lead to jobs, adult liter- acy that is linked to productive skills, are some examples of how government is attempting to make education more relevant to present day Afghanistan.",""],[1,"145","7","National Strategy for Equal Access to Education","The underlying principle of government in ensuring equal access to education for all is to develop a strategy that is national in scope but local in focus and delivery.",""],[1,"154","8","Food-for-Education and Food-for-Training Support","Payment in kind, through distribution of humanitarian assistance, will continue to be used to support higher children's enrolment in schools (e.g., food for education) and training of teachers (e.g., food for training).",""],[1,"166","2","Women’s Access to Education Sector Initiative","The strategy re- duces barriers for women to enter the education sector both as students and teaching staff.",""],[1,"166","3","School Anti-Narcotics Curriculum Programme","There will be spe- cific counter nar- cotics programs introduced into primary and sec- ondary school cur- ricula.",""],[1,"166","4","Environmental Issues Curriculum Integration","Environmental issues will be incorporated into the primary and secondary curriculum",""],[1,"166","5","Support for Remote and Disadvantaged Communities in Primary and Secondary Education","The primary and secondary strategy has a component to support remote and disad- vantage communities.",""],[1,"251","18","Independent Boards and Education Quality Assurance Legal Framework","Approval of laws for setting up of Independent Boards for secondary education, vocational education and for national standards of accreditation and regulatory framework for quality assurance of education services",""],[1,"251","19","Non-Government Service Provision Policy","Develop policies to encourage the non-government sector to offer services",""],[1,"251","20","School Advisory and Support Councils Establishment","Establish School Advisory and Support Councils (SASC) in all schools",""],[1,"251","21","Establishment of Independent Education and Management Boards","Establish Independent Boards for secondary education, NESA and National Institute of Management and Administration",""],[1,"251","22","National Institute of Curriculum Development","Establish a National Institute of Curriculum Development incorporating national standards benchmarks",""],[1,"251","23","Curriculum Development Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen institutional and staff capacities in curriculum development",""],[1,"252","10","National Partnership Program for Literacy and Non-Formal Education","Build a national partnership program of literacy and non-formal education",""],[1,"252","11","Female Teacher Recruitment, Retraining, and Re-employment Initiative","Increase the number of female primary and secondary teachers including re- training all female teachers who were separated from service during the PRR process and re-employing them.",""],[1,"252","13","Teacher Training College Expansion and Strengthening","Establish/strengthen teacher training colleges in all provinces",""],[1,"252","15","Teacher and Mullah Literacy Course Training Programme","Train 17,000 teachers and 3,500 mullahs in the delivery of literacy courses with at least 30% of them being female teachers.",""],[1,"252","16","Primary and Secondary Teaching Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of primary and secondary teaching (training teachers, school principals)",""],[1,"252","17","Secondary School Teaching Materials and Curriculum Improvement","Improve teaching material and new curricula for secondary schools",""],[1,"252","19","Compulsory Education Policy Implementation","Adopt an enabling policy to implement the Constitutional provision of compulsory education up to intermediate level",""],[1,"252","22","Female Dropout Follow-up and School Re-entry Incentive System","Adopt a system to follow up female drop outs and provide incentives to return them to school",""],[1,"252","25","Parent-Oriented Campaign for Girls' Enrollment","Implement parent-oriented campaign to promote support to girls' enrolment",""],[1,"252","27","College Entrance Exam Review Classes for Girls","Conduct review class for girls who graduate from secondary schools to prepare for college entrance examinations",""],[1,"253","3","Remedial Education Programme","Have a program of remedial education to address literacy rates",""],[1,"253","5","Construction of School Dormitories and Pro-Women Facilities","Construct dormitories and pro-women facilities, especially in the secondary level schools",""],[1,"253","7","Textbook and Teacher Guide Production","Produce new textbooks and teacher guides",""],[1,"263","10","Kindergarten Privatization Strategy","Develop the strategy for privatization of kindergartens",""],[1,"263","11","Kindergarten Privatization Reform","Gradually privatize kindergartens",""],[1,"280","2","School Construction and Teacher Recruitment Programme","establishment of (1,200 new schools and 1,200 CBS)and construction of 692 new schools, recruitment of 149,000 teachers (40,000 Female)",""],[1,"280","8","Faculty Capacity Building through Partnership Programs","Capacity building of faculty members through partnership programs",""],[1,"280","18","University Facilities Expansion","Construct 41 new facilities at universities across the coun- try.",""],[1,"280","21","University Dormitory Construction Programme","Construction of 24 new dormitories (12 for women and 12 for men)",""]],"41":[[1,"137","14","Health Sector Stewardship and Service Delivery Reorganization","The strategy is for the MoPH to maintain and strengthen its stewardship role for the Health and Nutrition Sector.","MoPH"],[1,"137","14","Basic Package of Health Services Contracting-Out Initiative","The overarching priority policy of the MoPH has been to obtain nearly universal coverage of a standard Basic Package of Health Services (BPHS) through a 'contracting out' initiative, to create strong linkages with the hospital sector through an effective referral mechanism.","MoPH"],[1,"137","14","Health System Expansion Enabling Environment","However, the MoPH will also be responsible for creating an enabling environment for expansion of the Health Care System beyond the provision of the BPHS.","MoPH"],[1,"137","17","Health Care Services Monitoring and Evaluation","Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of health care services in order to ensure quality, equity and effi- ciency of the health system;",""],[1,"137","18","Health and Nutrition Sector Coordination and Service Mapping","Coordinating the contributions of all national and international agencies involved in the Health and Nutrition Sector, upholding standards and mapping services to avoid duplication and gaps;",""],[1,"137","19","Provincial Decentralization of Responsibilities and Managerial Autonomy","Decentralization of appropriate responsi- bility and managerial autonomy to the provincial level;",""],[1,"137","20","Community Participation in Local Health Service Management","Increase the active participation of communities in the management of their local health care services through developing strong, active participatory links with shura (community committees) and training and supporting community health workers;",""],[1,"137","21","Health Care Legislation and Regulatory Reform","Developing legislation and regulations to facilitate growth and assure quality in the private sector provision or civil service provision of health care services.",""],[1,"139","3","Health System Policy and Planning Support Program","The national health care system will be organized and managed to reduce inequity and improve efficiency and accountability at all levels.",""],[1,"139","4","Health Sector Coordination and Policy Standardization Mechanism","MoPH will enhance coordination between the MoPH and partner organizations through formal and informal mechanisms and facilitate stronger donor coordination, especially when undertaking assessment and planning missions and in supporting health priorities.","MoPH"],[1,"139","4","Health Service Delivery Coordination with Donors, Partners, and Private Sector","MoPH will also work with both donors, partners and the private sector to coordinate the delivery of health care services by setting and distributing policies, standards and guidelines, convening","MoPH"],[1,"139","5","Health and Nutrition Consultative Group and Technical Task Forces","the Consultative Group on Health and Nutri- tion and task forces to work on specific techni- cal issues under the leadership of the MoPH and further develop Provincial Public Health Coordination Committees within each prov- ince.","MoPH"],[1,"140","2","Health Sector Financing Advocacy and Resource Mobilization","The MoPH will undertake health advocacy to increase funds and resources to the health sector, ensure spending is in line with priorities and coordinated across sectors, strengthen transparency in the allocation of financial resources and financial management, strengthen coordination of different sources of funding, and monitor different mechanisms of financing the delivery of services for their cost-efficiency and acceptability.","MoPH | Ministry of Finance"],[1,"140","2","Alternative Health Care Financing Development","MoPH will also coordinate closely with the Ministry of Finance on the National Development Budget, the development of mechanisms to improve total public expenditure from internal and external resources, the development of alternative health care financing.","MoPH | Ministry of Finance"],[1,"140","3","Continuation of NGO Partnerships in Health Service Delivery","Strategic actions related to the private sector include: (i) continuing the effective partnership with non-governmental organizations in the health sector","MoPH"],[1,"140","3","Strengthening MoPH Stewardship and Health Sector Coordination Capacity","further developing the MoPH's capacity to establish policies, strategies and plans, monitor performance in delivery of health services and coordinate diverse actors from the public and private sectors working within health and nutrition; and (iii) developing regulatory mechanisms for engaging the for-profit private sector.","MoPH"],[1,"140","3","Regulatory Framework for For-Profit Private Sector Engagement in Health","developing regulatory mechanisms for engaging the for-profit private sector.","MoPH"],[1,"140","5","Civil Society Participation in Health Service Delivery","Civil society plays a role in the delivery of health services and in the interaction between government and the population in determining health needs and priority areas.",""],[1,"140","5","Health Sector Coordination with Development Partners","the MoPH has pursued a strategy of close coordination with all actors in the health sector.","MoPH"],[1,"141","4","Support Mechanisms for For-Profit Private Health Providers","mechanisms will be developed by which 'for profit' private sector providers of medical and hospital services can be supported by Govern- ment.",""],[1,"141","4","Competition Promotion Between Public and Private Health Providers","As part of the ANDS, an effort will be made to foster competition between public sector providers, public sector contractors and 'for profit' private sector operations.",""]],"42":[[1,"63","3","Health Sector Strengthening and Rural Health Center Expansion","The Health sector will continue to be strength- ened. Building new health centers in rural and poor urban areas will be priority for health sec- tor public spending.",""],[1,"63","3","Inclusive Basic Package of Health Services","The special needs of dis- abled will be better accounted for in the Basic Package of Health Services (BPHS).",""],[1,"63","9","Water Access and Health Protection Investment","The Government will increase public spending on improving the access clean water as well as improved health protection to address this.",""],[1,"250","14","Performance-Based Health Service Delivery Reform","Making service delivery performance based through incentives and contract monitoring and exploring options for implementing results based financing of health service delivery in Afghanistan.",""],[1,"250","18","Primary Health Care Program","Implement the Primary Health Care Program",""],[1,"250","19","Integrated Health Referral System Development","Develop a comprehensive referral system integrated with BPHS to improve the service delivery level",""],[1,"250","20","Essential Medicines Procurement and Disbursement Harmonization","Harmonize the system of procurement and disbursement of essential medicines",""],[1,"250","21","Comprehensive Communicable Disease Care System","Develop a comprehensive care system for communicable diseases like TB, HIV and malaria",""],[1,"250","22","TB Diagnostic and Treatment Health Facilities Expansion and Maintenance","Establish and maintain required number of Health Facilities providing diagnos- tic and treatment TB services",""],[1,"251","2","Malaria Diagnostic and Treatment Health Facilities Expansion","Establish number of Health Facilities providing diagnostic and treatment Ma- laria services",""],[1,"251","3","Provincial HIV Surveillance and Counseling and Testing Centers","Establishing effective surveillance system and Volunteer Confidential Counsel- ing and Testing Center for HIV cases in each province",""],[1,"251","8","Regional Health Cooperation for Facility Access","Promotion of regional cooperation to make health facilities available to the people of Afghanistan if such facilities are not available in the country.",""],[1,"251","11","Integrated Reproductive and Child Health Care System","Develop an integrated reproductive and child health care system with the support of development partners",""],[1,"251","12","Effective Immunization Coverage System","Develop effective immunization coverage system with adequate doses of DPT vaCross Cutting Issuesne & Hepatitis, measles and polio in all provinces",""],[1,"251","13","Special Gender Issues Cell","A Special Cell be created to take care and promote all gender issues especially health of females and mothers",""]],"43":[[1,"138","8","Disease Early Warning System","MoPH will establish and maintain a surveil- lance system (Disease Early Warning System) to respond to epidemics and other risks to hu- man health as well as responding to health emergencies in a timely manner.","MoPH"],[1,"138","8","Integrated Communicable Disease Prevention, Control and Treatment Actions","This will in- volve implementing actions needed to better control communicable diseases through strengthened management of integrated, cost- effective interventions for prevention, control and treatment.",""],[1,"138","8","Outbreak Prevention and Rapid Response Strengthening","The prevention and manage- ment of outbreaks will also be strengthened further through raising public awareness and responding more rapidly through the Disease Early Warning System.",""],[1,"138","8","Comprehensive Health Preparedness Plan","A key action will be the development and institutionalization of a Comprehensive Health Preparedness Plan at the national and provincial levels and allocate appropriate resources for responding to natural and man-made emergencies in an effective and timely manner.",""],[1,"168","5","Implementation of International Health Regulations 2005","Afghanistan is fully committed to the implementation of International Health Regulations 2005, through which the MoPH is responsible for detecting, reporting and responding to all public health emergencies of international concern.","MoPH"],[1,"168","31","Regional Health Collaboration and Cross-Border Health Partnership","Declaration on Regional Collaboration in Health; and fostering a stronger partnership with Iran and Pakistan that will provide a platform for dialogue and ensure joint actions for addressing critical cross-border health issues.",""]],"44":[[1,"41","1","Social Risk Management Reform and Partnership Strengthening","Efforts will now focus on: (i) improving efficiency of public arrangements for social risk management; (ii) diversifying market-based arrangements for social risk management; (iii) strengthening informal arrangements for social risk management (iv) capacity building and restructuring in the MoLSAMD; and (vi) improving partnership with civil society and NGOs to enhance aid coordination.","MoLSAMD"],[1,"41","1","Public-Private Social Support Partnership Expansion","Finally, strengthening the public/NGOs/private sector partnership will support the Government's intention to remain mainly in the area of policy making and providing regulations and having the private sector and NGOs increasingly involved in service delivery.",""],[1,"61","8","Fiscally Affordable Social Protection Safety Nets","In parallel, fiscally affordable social protection safety nets will be undertaken as part of regular Government business.",""],[1,"63","5","Social Protection Support for the Most Vulnerable","Social protection programs will focus on supporting the most vulnerable and the poorest of the poor.",""],[1,"64","3","Social Protection Safety Net Strengthening","Social protection safety nets will be strengthened to ensure the poor can cope with the planned elimination of energy subsidies, which will increase the risk of the poor and marginal households falling further into poverty, especially for the urban households.",""],[1,"152","12","Disability Support and Social Integration Programme","By end-2010 increased assistance will be provided to meet the special needs of all disabled people, including their integration into society through opportunities for education and gainful employment;",""],[1,"153","7","Targeted Social Protection Programs and Transfers","the focus will be put on supporting the most vulnerable (i.e., the poorest of the poor) by allocating adequate resources to the poorest areas through nationwide targeted programs and transfers",""],[1,"153","7","Phase Out Non-targeted Subsidies","and by phasing out non-targeted subsidies (such as energy subsidies)",""],[1,"153","7","Strengthen Social Protection Planning and Administrative Capacity","and building the planning and administrative capacity of the MoLSAMD (and other line ministries) to deliver coordinated programs and improve social protection","MoLSAMD | other line ministries"],[1,"153","11","Public Social Risk Management Efficiency Reform","Reform in this area will focus on the following priority policies: (i) to im- prove efficiency of the public arrangements for social risk management;",""],[1,"153","11","Market-Based Social Risk Management Diversification","Reform in this area will focus on the following priority policies: (ii) to diversify market based arrangements;",""],[1,"153","11","Informal Social Risk Management Strengthening","Reform in this area will focus on the following priority policies: (iii) to strengthen infor- mal arrangements;",""],[1,"153","11","Social Assistance Targeting Improvement","Reform in this area will focus on the following priority policies: (iv) to improve targeting;",""],[1,"153","11","MoLSAMD Capacity Strengthening and Restructuring","Reform in this area will focus on the following priority policies: (v) to strengthen the capacity and restructure the MoLSAMD;","MoLSAMD"],[1,"153","11","Civil Society Partnership and Aid Coordination Improvement","Reform in this area will focus on the following priority policies: (vi) to improve partner- ship with the civil society (NGOs) and enhance aid coordination.",""],[1,"153","12","Social Protection Targeting for At-Risk Populations and War Survivors","In the future social protection will target two main groups: the population \"at risk\" and war survivors.",""],[1,"153","13","Public Debate on Zakat-Based Tax Introduction","Given this, the MoLSAMD will initiate public debate about prospects and modalities for introduction of the Zakat-based tax.","MoLSAMD"],[1,"154","4","National Social Protection Sector Program","Implementation of this will be through the Na- tional Social Protection Sector Program and will consist of: (i) public arrangements; (ii) market-based arrangements; (iii) informal ar- rangements; and (iv) capacity building.",""],[1,"154","5","Social Support Reform and Public Assistance Package","Future social support systems will include most of the existing public arrangements such as: (i) direct cash payments; (ii) payments in kind; (iii) public works; (iv) skills development; (v) lump sum payments; (vi) support to orphanages; and (vii) land distribution.",""],[1,"154","6","Gradual Elimination of Subsidies","some arrangements like sub- sidies (for fuel, pensions, and kindergartens) will gradually be eliminated.",""],[1,"154","6","Orphanage Reorganization for Child Day Care Services","Support to or- phanages will remain part of the social support system; however, they will be reorganized to provide day care services for other children \"at risk\".",""],[1,"154","7","Direct Cash Transfers for Poor Disabled People","The new direct cash transfers will be gradually introduced for the poor disabled with non-war related disability.",""],[1,"154","7","Direct Cash Transfers for Poor Families with Small Children","The inclusion of the poorest families with small children into direct cash transfers will depend on mobilization of domestic revenues and possible introduction of the Zakat-based tax.",""],[1,"154","8","Winterization Assistance for Poor Families","Therefore, a new system of payments in kind will be introduced for the poorest families with small children (winterization).",""],[1,"154","8","Basic Food and Non-Food Parcel Distribution","The parcels with basic food and non- food items will be distributed through Afghan Red Crescent Society to support the poorest households in the most difficult period of year.",""],[1,"155","1","Targeted Support for War Victims and Disaster Victims","targeted land distribution and lump sum payments will continue to be used to help the poorest war victims and victims of natural disaster.",""],[1,"155","2","Strengthen Microfinance Schemes for Social Protection","These will be further developed and strengthened.",""],[1,"155","2","Financial Literacy and Community-Based Insurance Expansion","efforts will be made to develop other market-based arrangements such as increasing financial market literacy and the introduction of community-based insurance schemes.",""],[1,"155","2","Women's Inheritance Rights Enforcement Measures","future Government policies will introduce measures to enforce women's rights to inheritance.",""],[1,"155","7","Winter Food Parcel Distribution Projects","Develop projects for the distribution of food parcels in winter (winterization);",""],[1,"155","9","Direct Cash Entitlements for Poor Persons with Non-War-Related Disabilities","Develop mechanisms for distributing direct cash entitlements to poor disabled individuals with non-war related disabilities",""],[1,"155","12","Pilot Support Projects for Extremely Vulnerable Groups","In cooperation with NGOs implement pilot projects to support extremely vulnerable groups which will include options for rein- tegration into families;",""],[1,"155","14","MoLSAMD Capacity Building and Restructuring Plan","Conduct reviews of the MoLSAMD and prepare plans for capacity building and re- structuring, including the establishment of the Child Secretariat within MoLSAMD.","MoLSAMD"],[1,"155","15","MoLSAMD Capacity Building and Restructuring for Social Protection Reform","Implementation of effective social protection reform will require significant capacity building of the MoLSAMD.","MoLSAMD"],[1,"160","3","Social Protection and Disaster Preparedness Improvement","improve social protection and disaster pre- paredness;",""],[1,"169","1","Direct Cash Transfer Management Improvement","to improve management of the direct cash transfers and eliminate",""],[1,"169","6","MoLSAMD Capacity Strengthening for Vulnerability Analysis and Project Preparation","to improve MoLSAMD's capacity for vulnerability analysis, targeting and project preparation and implementa- tion","MoLSAMD"],[1,"207","9","Social Protection and Welfare Programmes for Vulnerable Groups","social protection and welfare programs have also been developed, within which the needs of particularly vulnerable groups can be targeted.",""],[1,"260","2","Afghanistan Welfare Fund and Zakat-Based Tax Introduction","Initiate and complete the public debate about establishment of the Afghanistan Welfare Fund and introduction of the Zakat-based tax",""],[1,"260","3","Zakat-Based Tax Introduction","Introduce the Zakat-based tax in line with the recommendations from the pub- lic debate and consultations that will take place in 2008",""],[1,"261","6","Integration of the ANDS Social Protection Strategy into the Core Budget","Cost, reprioritize and integrate The ANDS Social Protection Strategy into the Core Budget",""],[1,"261","9","Poverty-Targeted Social Protection Eligibility Criteria","Approve poverty-targeted criteria for channeling social protection",""],[1,"261","14","Community-Based Insurance Scheme Development Project","Develop the project for establishing community based insurance scheme",""],[1,"261","20","Afghanistan Welfare Fund Establishment","Establish the Afghanistan Welfare Fund in line with recommendations from the consultations that will take place in 2008",""],[1,"262","6","Proxy Means Test Development","Develop a Proxy Means Test (PMT) based on non-income variables",""]],"45":[[1,"41","2","Voluntary Return and Reintegration Management","The ANDS strategic objective with respect to refugees, returnees and IDP's is to efficiently manage the voluntary return of refugees and IDPs and their reintegration into productive participation in society.",""],[1,"157","10","Refugee, Returnee and IDP Voluntary Return and Reintegration Strategy","The ANDS strategic objective for the Refugee, Returnee and Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) strategy is to facilitate the planned and voluntary return of refugees and IDPs and the reintegration of returnees and IDPs into society.",""],[1,"157","10","Government Coordination for Refugee and IDP Reintegration","This strategy establishes the Governments efforts in coordinating and reintegrating refugees and the IDPs into society.",""],[1,"158","7","Voluntary Return and Reintegration Support for Refugees and IDPs","The sector strategy provides policies for voluntary, planned and sustainable return of the refugees and IDPs that will support stability of Afghanistan, its economic development and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"158","7","Safe and Sustainable Reintegration for Returnees and IDPs","The strategic vision of the sector strategy is to provide safe, voluntary, gradual and sustainable reintegration possibilities for all Afghan refugees, returnees and IDPs choosing to return.",""],[1,"158","7","Protection Measures for Vulnerable Refugees and IDPs","Greater attention to protection of the vulnerable groups among refugees and IDPs, including children and women is an important part of this vision.",""],[1,"158","10","Safe Voluntary Refugee Return Support","support the safe, voluntary, an gradual re- turn of refugees from Pakistan, Iran and elsewhere;",""],[1,"158","11","Sustainable Reintegration Programs and Interventions","prepare and implement more visible and effective, sustainable reintegration pro- grams and interventions;",""],[1,"158","14","Internal Displacement Crisis Response Planning","prepare plans to improve the response to internal displacement crisis; and",""],[1,"158","16","Voluntary Return Facilitation for Afghan Returnees","improve the facilitation for gradual return of all Afghans who wish to return voluntarily from Pakistan, Iran and other host",""],[1,"159","2","Reintegration Support Capacity Strengthening","strengthen the Government's capacity to plan, manage, and assist the reintegration of returning Afghans and IDPs;",""],[1,"159","3","Internal Displacement Planning and Response Capacity Improvement","improve the capacity of the Government to plan for and respond to internal displace- ment;",""],[1,"159","6","Land Access Support for Refugees and IDPs","improve access to land for the refugee and the IDP population.",""],[1,"159","8","Rehabilitation and Local Integration Support for Returnees and IDPs","By end-2010, all refugees opting to return and internally displaced persons will be provided assistance for rehabilitation and integration in their local communities; their integration will be supported by national development programs, particularly in key areas of return",""],[1,"160","2","Reintegration Assistance for Returning Refugees and IDPs","prepare and implement more visible and effective reintegration programs and inter- ventions and to improve mechanism for delivering immediate reintegration assis- tance to returning refugees and IDPs;",""],[1,"160","5","Policy Responses to Population Movements","develop broader policy responses to population movements;",""],[1,"160","6","Tripartite Agreements for Refugee Policy Coordination","retain the Tripartite Agreements is an im- portant tool to ensure policy coordination and respect for refugee law and humanitar- ian principles;",""],[1,"160","7","Land Access Support for Refugees and IDPs","improve access to land for the refugee and the IDP population;",""],[1,"160","18","National IDP Protection Framework and Policy Guideline","promote a national framework and policy guideline for the protection of IDPs as well as the IDP mapping exercise.",""],[1,"160","19","Voluntary, Planned and Sustainable Repatriation Support","The Government's policy supports the voluntary, planned and sustainable repatriation movements.",""],[1,"160","19","Return Rate Increase through Livelihood and Welfare Improvement","At the same time, the Government is committed to increasing the overall rate of returns.",""],[1,"161","1","Returnee Housing, Land, and Infrastructure Support","The Government will continue to provide housing facilities, land plots and infrastructure to returnees to encourage voluntary returns.",""],[1,"161","6","Social Services for Returnees, Refugees, and IDPs","The Government will also increase the provision of social services available to returnees, refugees and IDPs.",""],[1,"161","9","Emergency Preparedness Support for IDPs","enhancing emergency preparedness for IDPs to ensure the timely and necessary support is provided to minimize hardship and suffering;",""],[1,"161","11","Return Management Capacity Strengthening","Ongoing efforts to increase Government capac- ity to manage returns will continue.",""],[1,"161","12","Government Coordination and Inter-Ministerial Cooperation for Refugee and IDP Return","improve internal Government coordination mechanisms, intern-ministerial cooperation and capacity for refugee and IDPs return;",""],[1,"161","15","National IDP Protection Framework and Mapping Exercise","promote a national framework and policy guideline for the protection of IDPs and an IDP mapping exercise;",""],[1,"161","16","Voluntary Refugee and IDP Return Support Programme","identify and implement programs and in- terventions to support voluntary refugee and IDPs return;",""],[1,"161","17","IDP and Returnee Integration and Protection Framework","incorporate IDPs and returnees into development and national programs and to provide for a national framework for their protection;",""],[1,"161","18","Land Access Support for Refugees and IDPs","ensure greater access to land for the refu- gee and IDP population;",""],[1,"161","20","Capacity Improvement for the Ministry for Refugees and Returnees","improve the capacity of the Ministry for Refugees and Returnees.","Ministry for Refugees and Returnees"],[1,"265","8","Returnee Reintegration and Durable Solutions Support","Identify bottlenecks (political, security, economic, social and legal) facing re- turnees (refugees and IDPs) and promote sustainable solutions for them with special focus on chronically poor women, disabled and widows.",""],[1,"265","8","Returnee Support Measures for Land, Livelihoods, and Shelter","(dispute settle- ment mechanisms land tenure, pasture management, rehabilitated livestock, productive infrastructure, vocational skills, shelters and etc",""],[1,"265","16","Donor-Supported Reintegration Assistance","Ensure continued donor support for initial reintegration assistance in critical areas like housing, water/sanitation, and financial support",""],[1,"266","7","Inclusion of Returning Refugees and IDPs in National Programs","Policies adjusted to make provisions for returning refugees and IDPs in national programs",""],[1,"266","13","Land Allocation Scheme Expansion and Anti-Corruption Monitoring","Management and implementation of Land Allocation Scheme is improved and supported to increase number of sites (5-10) in key returnee provinces.",""],[1,"267","2","Returnee and Host Community Support Program","National initiatives addressing returnee needs (both Male and Female) and local host communities developed and enhanced in housing, area-based and commu- nity development programs with particular emphasis on employment, liveli- hoods, and skill development.",""]],"46":[[1,"260","16","Support for Afghan Red Crescent Shelter Construction","Provide support to the Afghan Red Crescent Society for building the new shel- ters/marastoons",""],[1,"260","17","Free Distribution of Livestock, Orchards, and Farming Tools Project","Develop the project and criteria for free distribution of the livestock, orchards and tools for farming",""],[1,"261","7","Long-Term Direct Support Agreement for Civilian Victims of Conflict","Reach the agreement with the ISAF/NATO on long term direct support to civil- ian victims of conflict",""],[1,"261","8","Winterization Parcel Distribution Project","Develop the project and criteria for free distribution of the parcels with food and non-food items in winter period (winterization)",""],[1,"261","11","Civilian Victim Support Policy and Criteria Development","Develop the policy and criteria for supporting the civilian victims of conflict",""],[1,"261","16","Natural Disaster Victim Support Policy and Criteria","Develop the Policy and criteria for supporting the victims of natural disasters",""],[1,"262","9","Comprehensive Survey of Martyrs' Families and War-Related Disabled Persons","Conduct the comprehensive survey to collect data on number of martyr's fami- lies and individuals with war related disability, and on their socio-economic situation",""],[1,"262","19","Support and Reintegration Programme for Victims of Violence","Develop the policy and criteria for supporting the victims of violence to in- clude the program for reintegration into families, schools and society, as well as developing the criteria for establishing the NGOs-run shelters for women \"at risk\" and vulnerable children",""],[1,"262","20","Free Legal Advice and Mediation Services for Vulnerable Groups","Develop and approve the guidance for providing the free legal advice and mediation services (for reintegration into families) to all vulnerable groups",""],[1,"262","21","Community-Based Rehabilitation and Reintegration Policy for Drug Addicts","Develop and approve the policy, program and criteria for community based rehabilitation of drug-addicts and their reintegration into society",""],[1,"262","23","Pilot Project to Support Extremely Vulnerable Groups","In cooperation with NGOs implement the pilot project to support extremely vulnerable groups (homeless, mentally imperiled, elders without family sup-",""],[1,"263","4","Kuchi Poverty Support Project","Develop the project to support the poor Kuchi",""],[1,"263","8","Direct Cash Transfer Distribution Reform","Eliminate all existing misuses and irregularities in distributing the direct cash transfers",""],[1,"263","9","Revised Direct Cash Transfer Payment Schedule","Implement the new schedule for payments of the direct cash transfers (twice a year) in order to decrease cost of collecting the payments for vulnerable mar- tyr's families and individuals with war related disability who are living in re- mote areas",""],[1,"263","12","Civilian Conflict Victim Survey and Data Collection","Conduct the survey and collect data on civilian victims of conflict",""],[1,"266","2","Social Protection Referral and Support Networks","Continued emphasis on social protection (e.g. establishment of referral systems, centers, networks for vulnerable groups and individuals with focus on women)",""]],"47":[[1,"28","4","Targeted Poverty Reduction Programs for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","The Government is committed to programs and projects that directly target the poorest and most vulnerable groups for assistance.",""],[1,"28","4","Integrated Poverty Reduction Strategy","Well targeted poverty reductions programs are emphasized both in the strategy for social protection and integrated into the design of strategies across the other sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"34","7","Religious Organization Support for Poverty Reduction and Vulnerable Groups","support efforts by religious organizations to help allevi- ate poverty and protect vulnerable groups;",""],[1,"235","22","Private Sector Employment Strategy for Women","Conceptualization of Private Sector Employment Strategy for Women that will yield to pro-women employment strategies in the private sector",""],[1,"241","5","Subsidy for Private Bus Operators","Subsidy to private bus operators to implement the policy on promoting equitable access to transportation",""],[1,"246","30","Alternative Livelihoods in Narcotics Cultivation Areas","Priority to areas having substantial narcotics cultivation to promote economic activity to generate alternate livelihoods",""]],"48":[[1,"260","11","Comprehensive Support Policy for Female-Headed Chronically Poor Households","Develop the policy and criteria for providing comprehensive support to the female headed chronically poor households with small children",""],[1,"260","13","Orphan Family Reunification Programme","In cooperation with the NGOs develop the programs for reunifying the orphans with their living parent/parents.",""],[1,"260","14","Day Care Center Policy and Standards for Orphanages and NGOs","Develop and approve policy and standards for establishing day care center within orphanages and by the NGOs",""],[1,"260","15","National Day Care Center Network Development","In cooperation with the NGOs develop the network of day care centers throughout the country",""],[1,"260","18","Orphan Family Reunification Program","In cooperation with the NGOs develop the programs for reunifying the orphans with their living parent/parents.",""],[1,"260","19","Day Care Center Policy and Standards for Orphanages and NGOs","Develop and approve policy and standards for establishing day care center within orphanages and by the NGOs",""],[1,"260","20","Policy and Standards for Children in Conflict with Law and Children Living with Mothers in Detention","In cooperation with the NGOs develop the policy and standards for dealing with the children in conflict with law and with children who live with mothers in detention",""],[1,"260","21","Pilot Project for Supporting Children of Detained Mothers and Children in Conflict","In cooperation with the NGOs implement the pilot project for supporting the children that are living with mothers in detention and for children in conflict",""],[1,"262","10","Survey of Female-Headed Chronically Poor Households","Conduct the survey to collect data about the female headed chronically poor households with small children",""],[1,"262","13","Evening Classes and Skills Development Training for Street Working Children","Develop the program for evening classes and skill development training for street working children",""],[1,"263","23","Awareness Campaign Against Harmful Child Labor","Implement the awareness campaign against harmful child labor",""]],"49":[[1,"62","7","Public Works Expansion in Poorest Provinces","The Government, supported by the donors, will increase public work activities and their presence in the poorest provinces.",""],[1,"62","7","National Solidarity Program Job and Income Support","The National Solidar- ity Program (NSP) will continue to play an im- portant role in generating jobs and income for the rural poor.",""],[1,"64","5","Expanded NGO Service Delivery for the Poor","The role of the NGOs in delivering the services to the poor will also increase as will",""],[1,"152","13","Skill Development Training for Unemployed People","By end-2010 skill development training will be provided for 150,000 unemployed of which women will comprise 35 percent and the disabled will comprise minimum 10 percent;",""],[1,"154","8","Livestock, Orchard, and Farm Tool Distribution Program","Given the high incidence of rural poverty the new program will be developed to provide free distribution of livestock, orchards and tools for farming helping the poor to diversify agriculture production.",""],[1,"154","8","Conditional Cash Transfer and In-Kind Assistance Scheme","Both, direct cash transfers and payments in kind, will be made conditional: poor families will have to enroll children in school and take them to regular health check- ups.",""],[1,"154","9","Skills Development Training for the Most Vulnerable","the terms of reference of the NSDP will be changed to introduce the most vulnerable as the highest priority group for skills development training.",""],[1,"154","9","Public Works Job Creation Programmes","Public works programs, such as NSP, NABDP and NRAP will continue to provide job opportunities for the poor.",""],[1,"155","1","Afghanistan Reforestation Programme","to re-forest Afghanistan (i.e., \"Greening of Af- ghanistan\") will be introduced to supply addi- tional jobs to decrease deforestation of the country.",""],[1,"155","1","Remote Area Programme Redesign","All programs will be redesigned to reach the most isolated and remote areas.",""],[1,"155","6","Livestock, Orchard, and Farm Tools Distribution Project","Develop projects for the distribution of livestock, orchards and tools for farming;",""],[1,"160","20","Returnee Reintegration Support Programme","The Government will work to address the constraints returnees face on returning, including increasing economic opportunities (employment) and social services (health and education).",""],[1,"161","2","Public Works and Skills Development Programme","Public works programs will provide job opportunities together with skill development training.",""],[1,"161","10","Public Works Employment and Skills Training Programme","providing public works programs will provide job opportunities together with skill development training.",""],[1,"161","19","Microfinance Access for Refugees and IDPs","ensure refugees and IDPs have greater ac- cess to microfinance loans;",""]],"50":[[1,"39","5","Expansion of Facts Collection and Heritage Protection","facts collection held by the Ministry will be expanded.","the Ministry"],[1,"39","5","Museum Establishment and Expansion","museums will be established and or expanded and historical or heritage sites will be protected.",""],[1,"42","7","Natural and Cultural Heritage Preservation","preservation of Natural and Cultural Heritage sites or resources;",""],[1,"132","6","Heritage Area Identification and Conservation Planning","The most significant heritage areas will be identified and a detailed inventory of heritage assets will be undertaken.",""],[1,"132","6","Heritage Area Conservation Plan Implementation","Conservation plans for each heritage area (rehabilitation and preservation) will be developed and implemented through efforts to raise public awareness, economic incentives to private owners, tourism development, legal protection, public investment, and outreach to international bodies.",""],[1,"149","4","Afghan Cultural Heritage Revival and Protection Measures","measures will be taken to revive the Afghan cultural heritage, to stop the illegal removal of cultural material and to restore damaged monuments and artifacts by end-2010.",""],[1,"149","13","Cultural Artifact Protection and Repatriation Initiative","There is an urgent need to take action to prevent the looting of valuable cultural ar- tifacts and to encourage other countries to return them.",""],[1,"150","5","Cultural Artifacts Database Development","Establish an accessible and well maintained cultural artifacts data base;",""],[1,"150","6","Regional Museum Establishment Initiative","Plans will be accepted, and donors will be identified, to establish regional museums;",""],[1,"150","7","Kabul Museum Maintenance and Thematic Museum Establishment","Maintain Kabul museum and take measures to establish thematic museums such as ethnology, anthropology, science and technology, handicrafts and community museums;",""],[1,"150","8","Cultural Artifacts Collection Expansion","The cultural artifacts collection held by the Ministry will be expanded;",""],[1,"150","9","Promotion of Live Culture","Take appropriate measures to promote live culture (Music, Poetry, Arts, Theater & Dance)",""],[1,"166","7","Security Procedure Review","there will be a review of security procedures.",""],[1,"166","7","Legal and Diplomatic Artifact Recovery Efforts","Legal and diplomatic efforts to retrieve missing artifacts will also be made",""],[1,"166","11","Legal Protection and Enforcement for Archaeological Sites","Regional cooperation can also support and ensure the efforts of MoIC by strengthening the legal framework and the enforcement of the law in relation to archaeological sites to stop illicit traffic at the borders, and awareness-raising at both the national and the international level.","MoIC"],[1,"256","10","Cultural Heritage and Cultural Infrastructure Rehabilitation Programme","Rehabilitation of Kabul theater, Ministry complex, 20 historical monuments, building for MoIC provinces Dept. libraries in provinces, music institute in Kabul construction of museum in Nangarhar, Bamyan etc ...","Ministry complex | MoIC provinces Dept."],[1,"256","12","Afghan Cultural Heritage Protection and Restoration Measures","Measures to be taken to revive the Afghan cultural heritage, to stop the illegal removal of cultural material and to restore damaged monuments and artifacts",""],[1,"256","14","Monument Registration and Conservation Programme","The MoIC will continue registration and conservation of monuments, repair and preservation of museum, archeology items and historical monuments","MoIC"],[1,"256","17","Live Culture Promotion Measures","Take appropriate measures to promote Live Culture (Music, Cinema and Arts)",""],[1,"281","15","Afghan Cultural Heritage Revival and Protection Programme","Measures will be taken to revive the Afghan cultural heri- tage, to stop the illegal removal of cultural material and to restore damaged monuments and artifacts by end-2010",""]],"51":[[1,"110","13","Urban Water Supply and Sanitation Investment","Urban Development: Investment in water supply and sanitation will ensure that 50",""],[1,"111","4","Rural Basic Services Expansion","Rural development will be enhanced for 90 percent of villages through the provision of safe drinking water, sanitation (50 percent) and small scale irrigation (47 percent) by the end of 2010.",""],[1,"111","9","Donor-Funded Water Projects","meeting some of the most pressing needs through donor funded projects.",""],[1,"111","12","Urban Water Supply Utility Transformation","The urban water supply systems will be transformed into quasi-public agencies.",""],[1,"119","2","Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Program","The Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Program will assure that by 2013 98 percent of villages will have access to safe drinking water and 50 percent of villages will have improved sanitation facilities.",""],[1,"129","1","Urban Water Supply and Sanitation Investment","in line with MDG in- vestments in water supply and sanitation will have ensured that 50 percent of house- holds in Kabul and 30 percent of house- holds in other major urban areas will have access to piped water.",""],[1,"164","3","Clean Water and Sanitation Improvement","Access to clean water and im- proved sanitation facilities will im- prove health in households, thereby benefiting all household members but par- ticularly women who often are care- takers and who face threats to health during child birth.",""],[1,"244","8","Piped Water Systems and Drainage Network Investments","Investments in piped water systems and drainage networks (improved sanita- tion),",""],[1,"245","23","Underground Water Development Master Plan","Master plan on underground water development",""],[1,"248","10","Drinking Water Supply System Improvement and Expansion","Improve existing drinking water supply systems and build new systems in villages and cities, including Kabul",""],[1,"248","14","Rural Water and Sanitation Access Provision","Provision of access to water and sanitation facilities to rural people",""]],"52":[[1,"110","12","Sustainable Water Resource Management Strategies and Plans","The Afghanistan Compact Benchmarks for Wa- ter Management commit both the Government and the donors to the development of sustain- able water resource management strategies and plans covering irrigation and drinking water supply, and irrigation investments will result in at least 30 percent of water coming from large waterworks by end 2010.",""],[1,"111","9","Improved Water Management and Governance Reform","Given the importance of water resources, the Government has made improved water management a high priority.",""],[1,"111","9","Water Governance Improvement Measures","Steps are being taken to address shortcomings in governance",""],[1,"111","10","Supreme Council for Water Affairs Management Coordination Mechanism","The formulation of the Supreme Council for Water Affairs Management (SCWAM) to coordinate and overcome the problems of diverse ministerial responsibilities for water management.",""],[1,"111","10","Water Law and Policy Development Technical Secretariat","A Technical Secre- tariat has been established to develop new water laws and develop a consistent set of policies for water management.",""],[1,"111","11","Integrated Water Resource Management System","Steps have been undertaken to re-organize water resource management on the basis of an Integrated Water Resource Management System based on the five main river basins.",""],[1,"111","11","River Basin Organizations Establishment","in the future individual river basin organizations or authorities will be established.",""],[1,"113","1","National Water Resources Governance and Devolution Framework","The Government, acting through its operating entities, can influence the necessary international cooperation relating to several international water bodies.",""],[1,"113","2","Integrated Water Resources Management Program","Adoption and implementation of an effective IWRM program will take into consideration all activities and development requirements influencing water resources.",""],[1,"113","3","River Basin Water Management and Surface Water Storage Program","The river basin approach to water management will lead to improvements in capturing surface water using storage reservoir and recharge ba- sins.",""],[1,"113","3","Devolution of Authority to the River Basin Authority","By devolving authority to the RBA and thus encouraging more effective use of water resources, the water resource strategy",""],[1,"113","3","Integrated Water Resource Strategy Across Key Sectors","the water resource strategy (when integrated with programs in the transport, ag- riculture, health, education, power sectors, along with counter narcotics programs, private sector development programs) will contribute to sustainable development and poverty reduc- tion.",""],[1,"113","4","Comprehensive River Basin Data Management Programs","supplementary comprehensive river basin data management programs are needed to support this approach.",""],[1,"113","4","Water Use Regulation Improvement","It is important to improve mechanisms regulating water use and to attract investment to rehabilitate and construct irriga- tion, water supply and sanitary systems, as well as hydropower generation.",""],[1,"113","4","Sector-Wide Integrated Water Resources Management Transition","The sec- tor is in the process of transitioning from a pro- ject-by-project approach to a sector-wide ap- proach, using an integrated water resources management (IWRM) system.",""],[1,"113","4","Supreme Council for Water Affairs' Management and Technical Secretariat","Foremost among them was the formation of the Supreme Council for Water Affairs' Management (SCWAM), and its associated Technical Secretariat.",""],[1,"113","6","Unified Water Sector Strategy Development","Development of a water sector strategy therefore requires coordinating all relevant water sub-sector strategies being administered by individual government entities into one single unified water sector strategy document.",""],[1,"113","6","Water Sub-sector Institutional and Legal Strengthening","Facilitating related development of each of these sub-sectors will require institution building, enhancement of legal frameworks, capacity development, enlisting economic mechanisms, and intensive rehabilitation of infrastructure.",""],[1,"114","1","Water Law Revision and Water Resources Governance Framework","Under this policy framework, the Water Law of 1991 will be revised; water re- sources and irrigation policies and regulations will be established along with an institutional framework for water resources management; regulations for Water User Associations will be developed; plans will be developed and steps taken to preserve surface and underground water resources; national urban and rural wa- ter supply and sanitation policies and institu- tional development will be implemented; ac- cess to safe drinking water and improved drainage and sanitation systems will be estab- lished; and key groundwater and hydropower development plans and policies will be estab- lished.",""],[1,"114","2","Water Resources Policy, Legislation, and Institutional Reform","For the immediate future, the Government will play the dominant role in setting policy priorities and decisions pertaining to the development and management of water resources.",""],[1,"114","2","Water Sector Program Structuring","Ongoing and planned water sector projects have been structured into eight programs (i) Institutional Set- up and Capacity Building (ii) National Water Resources Development (iii) National River Basin Management (iv) Irrigation Rehabilita- tion (v) Urban Water Supply and Sanitation (vi) Rural Water Supply and Sanitation (vii) River- bank Protection (viii) Agriculture \"Food Secu- rity for All\".",""],[1,"114","3","Institutional Building and Capacity Development Program","Institutional Building and Capacity De- velopment Program: Activities in this pro- gram focus on the institutional and human capacity development of water resources management as well as infrastructure de- velopment at national, river basin and sub- basin levels.",""],[1,"114","4","National Water Resources Development Program","National Water Resources Development Program: Under the Water Law the Ministry of Energy and Water is responsible for the preparation of a national water resources development plan.","Ministry of Energy and Water"],[1,"115","2","Donor Water Program Coordination","It is essential that these activities be effectively coordinated and aligned with the priorities in the ANDS.",""],[1,"115","2","SCWAM Water Sector Coordination Leadership","SCWAM will undertake a leadership role among government organizations in providing coordination with the international community.","SCWAM"],[1,"115","2","Integrated Water Resources Development Strategy","The ANDS water sector goals are achievable with the implementation of an effective integrated water resource development strategy.",""],[1,"115","5","Sustainable Water Resource Management Strategies and Plans","Sustainable water resource management strategies and plans covering drinking and irrigation water supply developed and implemented.",""],[1,"162","5","River Basin Authority Autonomy and Development Mandate","river basin authorities will eventually be given greater autonomy and responsibility for development of the five major river basins in the country;",""],[1,"164","2","River Basin Administrative Decentralization Reform","Adoption of a River Basin ad- ministrative struc- ture should de- centralize tradi- tional mecha- nisms which have been prone to foster corruption.",""],[1,"164","4","Participatory Water Strategy Programs","Implementing strong water strategy programs having extensive user participation should infuse effective anti- narcotics sentiments into the populace.",""],[1,"164","4","Water Allocation Controls to Discourage Poppy Cultivation","Control of water allocations could be sued to discourage the poppy cultivation and encourage production of other high value crops.",""],[1,"164","5","Environmental Policy and Regulatory Enforcement Framework","Environment Law establishes a framework for the conservation and productive use of natural resources, including water, granting enforcement and permitting rights to the government to be implemented through NEPA.",""],[1,"164","5","Water Sector Strategy Support for Environmental Policies","Water sector strategy programs and the sector's institutional structure will be used to support environmental policies, regulations and laws.",""],[1,"164","6","Regional Cooperation for Shared Water Resources Management","regional cooperation is required for effective management of water resources shared by different countries.",""],[1,"164","7","Water Sector Capacity Building Programs","Water sector capacity building programs are essentially targeted at the three principal development components: Institutional, organizational, and individual.",""],[1,"247","2","Water Law and Supplementary Regulations Reform","Assess, identify, draft, review, debate, resolve, finalize water law and supplementary regulations",""],[1,"247","4","River Basin Institutional Design and Pilot Program Development","Conduct appropriate studies, identify specific pilot programs, experimentation, and customize river basin institutional structures.",""],[1,"247","8","Integrated Water Resources Management Staff Training","Training of staff from various sector ministries on integrated water resources management",""],[1,"247","10","River Basin Agency and Council Establishment and Capacity Building","Establishment of organization and capacity building of River Basin Agencies and Sub-agencies (RBA/ SBA) and River Basin and Sub-basin Councils (RBC/SBC)",""],[1,"247","15","Water Resources Management Curriculum Development","Development of curriculum in water resources management at local universi- ties/technical colleges",""],[1,"247","19","Hydraulic Modeling Training Programme","Institute training in HEC RAS and other appropriate modeling techniques",""],[1,"247","29","Inventory Studies and Basin Master Planning","Initiate appropriate inventory studies, water resources planning studies and basin master plans",""],[1,"248","1","Project Identification, Design, Procurement, and Implementation","Identify, study, design, procure and implement projects",""],[1,"248","3","Rehabilitation Program","Identify, prioritize, and implement rehabilitation program",""],[1,"248","6","Enhanced National Solidarity Programme Achievement Tracking","Enhance achievement tracking procedures and augment NSP resources",""],[1,"248","12","River Basin Technical and Management Planning","Development of technical plans, management plans, and implementation strategies for Amu Darya River Basin, Northern River Basin, Western River Basin, Helmand River basin, and Kabul River Basins,",""],[1,"248","13","Traditional Irrigation Scheme Rehabilitation and Water User Association Strengthening","Rehabilitation of all small, medium, and large traditional irrigation schemes and strengthen water users association",""],[1,"276","19","Sustainable Water Resource Management and Sanitation Planning","by 2013 Sustainable water resource management strategies and plans covering drinking water supply will be developed along with improved sanitation.",""],[1,"276","24","Sustainable Water Resources Management Strategies and Plans","Sustainable water resources management strategies and plans covering irrigation and drinking water supply developed and implemented.",""],[1,"276","27","Sustainable Water Resource Management Strategy and Plan Development","Sustainable water resource management strategies and plans covering irrigation and drinking water supply will be developed by end-2008",""],[1,"276","27","Irrigation Investment Expansion through Large Waterworks","irrigation invest- ments will result in at least 30% of water coming from large waterworks by March, 2011",""],[1,"278","31","Kabul River Basin Water Assessment Study","Recently assessment study in Kabul river basin has been started through research and Geo engineering enterprises with support of JICA and USGS",""]],"53":[[1,"38","4","Urban Basic Services Expansion","increased access to basic services for urban households",""],[1,"38","4","Informal Settlement Tenure Regularization","phased regularization of tenure for 50 per- cent of households living in informal settle- ments",""],[1,"38","4","Urban Service and Facility Upgrading","upgrading public services and facili- ties, including new urban area development",""],[1,"38","4","Affordable Housing and Serviced Land Expansion","increased availability of affordable shelter, including a 50 percent increase in numbers of housing units and 30 percent increase in area of serviced land on the market, coupled with ac- cess to affordable finance",""],[1,"38","4","Urban Green Space Improvement","improved urban environment with green areas and open spaces",""],[1,"129","8","Pilot Land Tenure Security Project","a pilot land tenure security project is underway in Kabul",""],[1,"129","15","Historic Quarter Conservation Initiatives","Three conservation initiatives are under way in historic quarters of Kabul, Herat and Tashqurghan.",""],[1,"131","4","Developable Land Provision and Housing Development Options","Sectoral agencies will consider other options for providing de- velopable land including: land-sharing, land readjustment, land pooling, and infill devel- opment.",""],[1,"131","5","Land Mapping, Surveying, and Tenure Formalization Programme","Land security will be improved through map- ping and land surveying of communities, ten- ure formalization, and land registration.",""],[1,"131","6","Dehsabz New City Development Project","The Government, through the Dehsabz City Development Authority, will continue to examine the potential for the development of a new city on the Dehsabz plain north of the existing Kabul City.",""],[1,"131","6","Basic Urban Infrastructure Investment for Dehsabz","The extent of the Government's direct role will generally be limited to planning, investment in some of the basic urban infrastructure and facilitating private commercial investment.",""],[1,"131","6","Government Land Sale and Lease Financing for Kabul Reconstruction","Most of the land in Dehsabz belongs to the Government hence, the sale and lease of land will generate revenues needed for investment in the new city and for the pressing reconstruction and infrastructure development needs of Kabul.",""],[1,"131","7","Public Sector Housing Production","Housing: New housing will be produced and improved through: (i) public sector housing production",""],[1,"131","7","Support for Informal and Small Housing Producers","support to informal and small",""],[1,"132","1","People's Housing Process Support","scale housing producers - the 'peoples housing process';",""],[1,"132","1","Research and Development for Appropriate Building Materials and Technologies","support to research and develop- ment of appropriate building materials and technologies;",""],[1,"132","1","Construction Skills Upgrading Programme","upgrading the skills of con- tractors and laborers;",""],[1,"132","1","Building Components Manufacturing Support","supporting entrepre- neurs to upgrade or set up building compo- nents manufacturing units;",""],[1,"132","1","Private Sector Rental Housing Production Support","support to pri- vate sector production, particularly of rental housing.",""],[1,"132","2","Inclusive Housing Programmes for Vulnerable Groups","Housing programs will consider the particular needs of various groups such as civil servants, returnees, Kuchis, IDPs, widows and other vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"132","2","Housing Finance Expansion Measures","Housing finance will be provide - for purchase, rehabilitation, and con- struction of new housing - through: integrating housing finance; stimulating private banks to increase mortgage lending to low-income households, through, for example, mortgage guarantees; initiating community mortgage schemes; lowering mortgage interest rates; re- ducing collateral and down payment require- ments; introducing flexible repayment schemes.",""],[1,"132","3","Housing Subsidy Program for Very Low-Income Households","Housing subsidy programs will be provided for very low income households, including both owners and renters.",""],[1,"132","4","Urban Infrastructure and Services Improvement","A concerted effort will be made to improve infrastructure including roads, footpaths, storm drainage, water supply, electricity, street lights, sanitation, and solid waste collection.",""],[1,"132","4","Urban Social Infrastructure Improvement","Social infrastructure will be improved, including open space, children's' parks, community and",""],[1,"132","5","Housing Construction and Rehabilitation Support","Support will be provided to house construction and re- habilitation, but only in line with an approved plan and with careful consideration given to levels of cost recovery.",""],[1,"132","5","Water Supply and Sanitation Rehabilitation and Expansion","Steps will be taken to rehabilitate and extend water supply and sani- tation services, giving priority to rehabilitating existing areas to an adequate level of service before extending service to new areas.",""],[1,"133","6","Phased Regularization of Tenure in Informal Settlements","Phased regularization of tenure for 50 per- cent of households in informal settlements, in parallel with upgrading of public ser- vices and facilities, as well as new urban area development.",""]],"54":[[1,"257","24","Land Use Review and Government Land Leasing Reform","Review, revise and formulate land use and government owned land for lease",""],[1,"270","18","Community-Based Land Registration and Title Registration","A community based process for registration of land in all administrative units and the registration of titles will be started for all urban areas and rural areas by Jaddi 1387 (end-2008).",""],[1,"270","18","Land Dispute Settlement System","A fair system for settlement of land disputes will be in place by Jaddi 1386 (end-2007).",""],[1,"275","13","Urban Land Title Registration and Land Dispute Settlement System","The registration of titles will be started for all major urban areas and a fair system for settlement of land disputes will be in place.",""]],"55":[[1,"148","4","Private Sector Support for Sports Development","there will be an effort made to encourage private sector support.",""],[1,"148","4","Sports Complex Construction and Sports Strengthening Programme","Provided funds are available, there is a program to build sports complexes and strengthen sports through provincial sports departments and sports improvement pro- grams in capital and provinces.",""],[1,"148","4","Anti-Narcotics Messaging Through Sports Activities","The anti- narcotics message will be promoted strongly through sports activities.",""],[1,"166","3","Anti-Narcotics Sports Messaging Initiative","In addition an anti narcotics message will be built into the sports program",""],[1,"255","12","National Sports Services Coordination Reform","Delegate the overall authority to coordinating sports services in the country to the Olympic Committee",""],[1,"255","13","National Olympic Committee Staff Capacity Building","Build capacity of professional staff of the National Olympic Committee for quality programming of administration and service delivery",""],[1,"255","14","International Training and Competition Access for Athletes","Approach countries and foreign sporting agencies with facilities for advanced athletes to allow Afghan sports people to train and compete in foreign countries",""],[1,"255","15","Women's Sports Access, Leadership, and Participation Strategy","Adopt and implement a strategy to realize the benchmark of increasing women's access, leadership and participation in sports",""],[1,"255","17","Sports Infrastructure and Sports Development Programme","Improve Infrastructure (build sports complexes and strengthen sports through provincial sports departments, sports improvement programs in capital and provinces)",""],[1,"280","32","Provincial Sports Facilities Improvement Programme","Sport facilities will be improved in all provinces of Af- ghanistan (2013)",""]],"56":[[1,"149","12","Joint National Youth Program","In Youth a Joint National Youth Program is being implemented.",""],[1,"150","20","Joint National Youth Program","In addition a Joint National Youth Program is now in the process of being implemented.","Ministries of the Government of Afghanistan"],[1,"151","3","Youth Needs Response Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of the Govern- ment to respond to the needs of the youth of the country;",""],[1,"151","4","Non-Formal Youth Education and Skills Development","Promoting non-formal education, increas- ing awareness and developing skills (liter- acy, leadership, strategic planning, conflict resolution, peace-building, etc.) in young people so to provide better quality of life and livelihood opportunities;",""],[1,"151","5","Youth Participation in Governance and Civic Processes","Engaging youth in governance, develop- ment and social-political processes at local, district, municipal, provincial and national level, ensuring the participation of young women and men in democracy and advo- cacy;",""],[1,"151","6","Youth Volunteer Corps","Promoting voluntary efforts for peace and development and establishing a youth vol- unteer corps for the country.",""],[1,"151","7","Joint National Youth Program Implementation","as well as the implementation of the Joint Na- tional Youth Program.",""],[1,"256","23","Non-Formal Youth Education and Skills Development Programme","Promoting non-formal education, increasing awareness and developing skills (literacy, leadership, strategic planning, conflict resolution, peace-building, etc.) in young people so to provide better quality of life and livelihood oppor- tunities.",""],[1,"257","3","Youth Volunteer Corps for Peace and Development","Promoting voluntary efforts for peace and development and establishing a youth volunteer corps for Afghanistan",""],[1,"266","8","National Information Outreach Capacity Enhancement","Enhance capacity to prepare and reach out information to Afghans either in or outside of the country.",""]],"57":[[1,"82","1","Regional Cooperation and Diplomatic Counterterrorism Initiatives","Given that many of these groups receive support from foreign sources, both regional cooperation and diplomatic initiatives are vital.",""],[1,"87","4","Regional Security Cooperation and Intelligence Sharing","The Government seeks to cooperate with its neighbors by strengthening regional security linkages with intelligence sharing to tackle cross-border infiltration, terrorism and narcotics trafficking.",""],[1,"87","5","Regional Security and Diplomatic Cooperation Initiative","The Government will work with the international community and neighboring countries for an effective diplomatic solution to security challenges.",""],[1,"87","5","Counter-Terrorism Diplomatic Pressure","This will require: (i) concerted diplomatic pressure against the safe havens enjoyed by terrorist groups outside of Afghanistan's borders;",""],[1,"87","5","Border and Cross-Border Security Strengthening","This will require: (ii) coordinated and effective measures for strengthening border and cross-border security;",""],[1,"87","5","Tri-Partite Commission Strengthening","and (iv) a further strengthening of the Tri-partite Commission to dialogue with Pakistan on substantial issues.",""],[1,"88","12","Cooperative Border Management and Anti-Trafficking Initiative","Enhance cooperative border management with Afghanistan's neighbors to crack down on illegal border crossing and trafficking.",""]],"58":[[1,"72","10","Opium Poppy Eradication Targeting Programme","Focus eradication efforts on wealth- ier opium poppy cultivating areas and also areas that are new to poppy cultivation;",""],[1,"73","1","Drug Trafficker Interdiction Intensification","Increase interdiction efforts against medium and large drug traffickers and their sponsors;",""],[1,"84","9","Poppy Eradication and Drug Trafficking Crackdown","Eventual eradication of Poppy Production and crack down on drug trafficking.",""],[1,"86","11","National Drug Control Strategy Implementation","The Ministry of Counter Narcotics is responsible for the implementation of the National Drug Control Strategy (NDCS).","Ministry of Counter Narcotics"],[1,"86","11","Drug-Related Crime Control Mechanisms","development of effec- tive mechanisms to deal with drug-related crimes",""],[1,"86","11","Poppy Eradication Programme","poppy eradication programs ..",""],[1,"173","3","Force Protection for Eradication Operations","Provision of force protection for eradica- tion in targeted areas;",""],[1,"173","13","Opium Eradication Strengthening Programme","The Government will increase its eradication efforts.",""],[1,"263","19","Drug Prevention Awareness Campaign","Implement Drug Prevention Awareness Campaign through media, schools and religious leaders",""],[1,"269","1","Poppy Eradication and Drug Trafficking Crackdown","Eventual eradication of Poppy Production and crack down on drug trafficking",""]],"59":[[1,"93","7","Information and Human Resource Management Systems","Information management and human re- source management to be established;",""],[1,"93","14","Legal Education Strengthening","legal education;",""],[1,"93","15","National Legal Training Centre Establishment","establishment of National Legal Training Centre for vocational education and vocational excellence",""],[1,"94","13","Justice Professional Practical Skills Training","Justice institutions equip new professionals with the practical and professional skills necessary to fulfill their duties",""],[1,"94","13","Continuing Legal Education System for Justice Professionals","A system of continuing legal education for justice professionals, paying specific attention to women, is in place and operational.",""],[1,"224","27","Justice Institution University Recruitment Linkages","Justice institutions to establish links with universities for recruiting candidates (e.g., job fairs and short internships).",""],[1,"224","28","Career Development Practice Improvement Measures","Survey, develop and implement recommendations to im- prove existing career development practices in each institu- tion with particular attention to complying with gender benchmarks.",""],[1,"224","29","Institutional Capacity Development for Professional Training","Develop institutional capacity to train professionals",""],[1,"225","16","Core Subject Curriculum Development and Launch","Create and launch agreed core subject curriculum for Sharia, law and political science faculties.",""],[1,"225","17","Core Subject Curriculum Development and Launch","Create and launch agreed core subject curriculum for Sharia, law and political science faculties.",""],[1,"226","3","Legal Research Facilities Enhancement Study","Survey and make recommendations for enhancement of legal research facilities, including a feasibility study of the establishment of an advanced legal research institute.",""],[1,"226","4","Stakeholder Consultations for Legal Research Capacity Development","Create stakeholder consultations to develop policy and planning mechanisms for enhancing legal research capacity.",""],[1,"226","5","International Legal Education Partnerships and Study Programs","Law and Sharia faculties establish links with foreign legal educational institutions to enhance research capacity, in- cluding foreign study programs for both students and staff.",""],[1,"226","6","University Infrastructure Upgrades for Female Inclusion","Universities identify and enhance infrastructure so as to accommodate female students and staff",""],[1,"226","7","University Gender Inclusion Policy","Universities develop and implement policies to raise per- centage of female students and staff to at least 30 percent",""],[1,"226","8","Vocational Training Courses for Justice Professionals","Justice institutions, in coordination with the Independent National Legal Training Center, develop appropriate vocational training courses for justice professionals, paying specific attention to the needs of female professionals.",""],[1,"226","9","Specialized Continuing Legal Education Programmes","Justice institutions, in coordination with the Independent National Legal Training Center, develop and implement specialized programs for continuing legal education, paying specific attention to the needs of female professionals.",""]],"60":[[1,"42","1","Regional Cooperation Initiatives","The regional cooperation initiatives are intended to increase access to power; generate revenues through transit trade; reduce impediments to trade and expand both import and export opportunities; increase investment and contribute to improved employment and business opportunities; facilitate the free flow of goods, services, and technology; allow the costs or benefits of development of common resources to be shared; reduce regional tensions and facilitate regional efforts to reduce cross border crime and terrorism; and facilitate the voluntary return of refugees.",""],[1,"48","2","ANDS International Consultation and Coordination Support","The ANDS Secretariat provides support to these structures to enhance coordination and effectiveness and the linkage with the national consultation process.",""],[1,"81","3","Strengthen Military, Economic, and Political Ties with Regional and International Partners","To counter these threats and ensure national interests the Government plans to strengthen the military, economic and politi- cal ties with its regional and international part- ners.",""],[1,"86","5","Foreign Policy Alignment with National Security Strategy","Set foreign policy objectives in line with national military strategies and activities of the National Army and border police;",""],[1,"86","6","International Law and Convention Compliance Promotion","Support and promote international peace and welfare by upholding and implementing international laws, conventions and national development strategies ;",""],[1,"86","10","Bilateral and Multilateral Economic Cooperation Initiative","Support and promote bilateral and multi- lateral economic initiatives with neighbors to secure national interests.",""],[1,"87","5","Regional Economic Cooperation Program Support","This will require: (iii) support for the programs agreed in recent regional economic co- operation conferences;",""],[1,"172","4","Regional Cooperation Project-Based Activities","Part of the Government's efforts will be to work with regional partners on implementing practical project based activities.",""],[1,"172","4","Regional Knowledge Transfer Initiative","This includes and emphasis on increasing the transfer of knowledge with regional partners.",""],[1,"172","4","Cross-Border Human Interaction Enhancement","Increas- ing the human interaction between Afghani- stan and it's neighbors, at the government, dip- lomatic, social and local level will lead to im- proved relationships.",""],[1,"172","5","Pro-active Regional Diplomacy Program","The Government is implementing a multi-faceted Pro-active Regional Diplomacy Program (PRDP).",""],[1,"172","7","Regional Cooperation Strengthening Projects","the Government gives the highest priority to the development of projects to strengthen regional cooperation.",""]],"61":[[1,"124","12","E-Government Modernization Initiative","A modern telecommunications sector, incorpo- rating e-government initiatives will enhance",""],[1,"126","4","National Data Center and E-Government Services","With the establishment of a national data center by end of 2008, and implementation of e- Government, e-Commerce, e-Health (telemedi- cine) towards the end of 2010 Afghan citizens will be able to more fully participate in the in- formation age.",""],[1,"126","6","E-Afghanistan Programme","The key programs of the ICT sector are (i) Ena- bling Environment (ii) Infrastructure Develop- ment (iii) E-Afghanistan (iv) ICT Literacy.",""],[1,"126","10","Transparency and Public Information Access Measures","By end-2008, actions designed to promote transparency and citizen access to public information will be implemented.",""],[1,"127","1","Government ICT Efficiency and Interoperability Rules and Procedures","tions designed to promote Government ef- ficiency, reduce costly waste and ensure in- formation system inter-operability will be implemented.",""],[1,"127","1","E-Government Resource Center","An e-Government resource center will be established for the design and im- plementation of projects.",""],[1,"127","1","Afghan Post ICT Modernization","Afghan Post offices will be modernized us- ing ICT to ensure reliable collection and distribution of mail.",""],[1,"127","1","Mobile Commerce-Ready Mobile Network Infrastructure","The infrastructure of mobile networks will be adapted to enable mobile commerce, meaning the use of phones to transfer funds and conduct other financial transactions (pay utility bills and taxes, make retail purchases).",""],[1,"127","1","Afghanistan National Data Center for E-Government Applications","The Afghanistan Na- tional Data Center will be ready to host the e-government applications.",""],[1,"127","3","Government Service Anti-Corruption Review and ICT Automation","By end-2009, further efforts will be made to reduce corruption by reviewing all Government services and making recommendations for the adoption of ICT to streamline and automate (for example, customs processing, procurement and licensing).",""],[1,"128","3","E-Government and Telecommunications Modernization Initiative","A modern telecommunications sector, incorporating e-government initiatives wher- ever possible, will enhance the effectiveness and efficiency of the public sector.","MoCIT"],[1,"128","3","Public Sector ICT Capacity-Building Investment","By mobiliz- ing resources to build up the ICT sector within the public sector institutions, MoCIT will also be accelerating the development of ICT support capabilities of the private sector in Afghanistan, both through contracts and via participation in the policy processes of the ICT Council.","MoCIT"],[1,"162","2","Telecommunications Sector Enabling Environment and Regulatory Framework","A model for these efforts to be considered is what has been accomplished in the telecommunications sector.",""],[1,"164","9","E-Governance and E-Enabled Services","E-Governance and other E- Enabled services will reduce the scope for corrup- tion because it provides better record sand more information",""],[1,"271","3","District Center Internet Connectivity Expansion","By end-1389 (20 March 2011), all the district centers of the country will have internet facility to facilitate the flow of information between the districts, municipalities, provinces and, the centre i.e. Kabul.",""],[1,"277","16","E-Government Policies, Strategies and Pilot Projects","E-Government policies, strategies and pilot projects are already launched.",""]],"62":[[1,"24","11","Community-Led Development Councils","Some 18,000 CDCs have been established and are implementing community-led de- velopment projects.",""]],"63":[[1,"11","2","Sustained Fiscal Support for ANDS Implementation","Sustained fiscal support and continuous evaluation and monitoring are essential now to meet the challenges ahead related to ANDS implementation.",""]],"64":[[1,"67","5","Domestic Revenue Mobilization","a high priority for the Government is to significantly increase domestic revenues.",""],[1,"74","9","Revenue Administration and Tax Base Broadening Reform","The Government continues efforts to increase revenues by improving revenue administration and enforcement and broadening the tax base.",""],[1,"74","9","Broad-Based Consumption Tax Introduction","In the medium-term, a broad-based consumption tax will play an important role in domestic revenue mobilization.",""],[1,"74","9","Tax Policy, Administration, and Enforcement Improvements","broadening the tax base, improvements in tax policy, administration and enforcement will be implemented.",""],[1,"74","9","Income Tax Law Amendment Enactment","an immediate high priority for the Government is the enactment of the amendments to the income tax law by National Assembly.",""],[1,"74","9","New Tax Measures for Revenue and Competitiveness","New tax measures will focus equally on improving the revenue intake, while simulta- neously reducing the cost of doing business, improving the country's investment environ- ment and enhancing competitiveness.",""],[1,"185","4","Tax System Strengthening","its further strengthening will increase domestic revenues and the Government's potential to allocate more resources to fund recurrent costs of donor-funded projects.",""],[1,"185","4","Tax Administration Capacity Strengthening","The tax system is in the process of being strengthened.",""],[1,"185","4","Tax Administration Capacity Improvement","Institutional capacity for efficient tax collection will improve tax administration at all levels.",""],[1,"187","7","Domestic Revenue Mobilization","to (ii) increasing collection of domestic revenues,",""]],"65":[[1,"73","19","Financial Sector Strengthening for Expanded Access to Finance","Strengthen the financial sector to increase access to credit and financial services, paying special attention to alleviating capacity constraints.",""],[1,"77","7","Bank Supervision and Risk Management Oversight","DAB is com- mitted to help banking institutions to manage the risks involved in their operations.",""],[1,"77","8","Expanded Credit and Mortgage Lending Reform","DAB will strive to encourage financial institu- tions to actively take part in economic devel- opments by granting short-term, medium-term and long-term credits to small and medium enterprises (SMEs), owners of factories and construction companies and to start mortgage lending to commercial and residential custom- ers.",""],[1,"77","8","Financial Sector Legal and Regulatory Reform","To do so, DAB needs to remove any prevailing obsta- cles and unnecessary legal constraints by draft- ing required laws and regulations and submit- ting them for approval to the National Assem- bly as quickly as is practicable.",""],[1,"77","8","Drafting of Lending Facilitation Laws","Fortunately, DAB has already taken significant steps in drafting four laws which will facilitate me- dium- to long-term lending in the country.",""],[1,"232","8","Financial Audits of State-Owned Enterprises","Undertake financial audits of State Owned Enterprises",""],[1,"232","9","Privatization of State-Owned Assets","Privatize and corporative state owned assets",""],[1,"232","10","Insurance Law Reform","Implement an adequate insurance law.",""],[1,"232","11","Private Insurance Sector Regulatory Development","Encourage the development of an appropriately regulated private insurance sector.",""],[1,"232","12","Investor Risk Management Tools Development","Work with donors to create risk management tools for domestic and foreign investors, appropriate to the specific risks of investing in Afghanistan.",""],[1,"232","14","Financial Products and Services Expansion Strategy for SMEs","Lay out a concrete strategy with time-bound actions to significantly expand the outreach and range of financial products and services, especially targeting small and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"232","16","Financial Legal Framework Reform","Enact an appropriate legal framework including passage of four financial laws: Secured Transactions, Mortgage, Leasing and Negotiable Instruments.",""],[1,"232","17","Independent Banking and Business Training Institute","Build capacity in the financial sector by establishing an independent banking and business training institute as a joint commercial bank - DAB initiative.",""],[1,"232","19","Credit Information Bureau Establishment","Establish a credit information bureau to facilitate commercial and consumer lending.",""],[1,"232","22","Micro and SME Finance Expansion","Expand provision of donor and private sector micro and SME finance",""],[1,"232","24","Cash-in-Transit Security Office","Establish an office in DAB in conjunction with Ministry of Interior to provide security for cash in transit between banks and bank branches in Kabul.","DAB | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"232","26","Expansion of Rural Financial Services","Increase the offering of financial services in rural areas through the further",""],[1,"233","3","Bank Privatization and Governance Restructuring","Implement the agreed upon privatization strategies in Bank-e-Milli and Pash- tany Bank, including the placement of professional management and board to restructure the banks free of government interference.",""],[1,"236","9","Professional Accounting and Auditing Associations and Standards Support","Support the establishment of accounting, auditing and other professional asso- ciations and the adoption of related professional standards",""]],"66":[[1,"103","20","Pro-Trade Policy and Liberal Foreign Exchange Regime","Maintain a pro-trade environment: The Government remains committed to maintaining trade policies with low barriers for imports and exports and a liberal foreign exchange system.",""],[1,"103","20","Trade Policy Reform to Support Domestic Revenue and Production","The Government's trade policies will take into account the need to increase domestic revenues and support increased domestic production by the private sector.",""],[1,"104","1","Systematic Tariff Reform","The Government will undertake systematic tariff reform as part of the budget process and in consultation with the private sector and will avoid ad hoc changes.",""],[1,"104","1","Trade Market Access Expansion","The Government will continue to vigorously seek to increase access for Afghan goods and services in foreign markets though bilateral, regional and multilateral trade agreements.",""],[1,"104","1","WTO Accession","The Government remains committed to WTO accession.",""],[1,"104","2","Firm-Level Technical Assistance for Export Competitiveness","The Government will seek firm-level technical assistance to increase the ability of firms in these and other new industries to compete more effectively in potential export markets.",""],[1,"104","3","Trade Facilitation Measures","The Government will introduce trade facilitation measures to reduce the costs of moving goods within the country and across borders, including endeavoring to relax restrictions arising from transit agreements with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"104","3","Export Capacity Support for Domestic Goods and Services","Institutional capacity to support the export of domestically produced goods and services will be increased, including for example the technical resources to establish that Afghan agricultural products meet sanitary and phyto-sanitary (SPS) requirements of importing countries and international product standards are met.",""],[1,"104","3","Export Documentation Streamlining","The Government will reduce the burden of export documentation and processes will be further streamlined and essential services,",""],[1,"122","2","Automated Customs and Data Systems Introduction","The introduction of the automated customs and data systems (ASYCUDA) has been initiated which will reduce transit times and encourage promote trade, and aid in tracking customs collections.",""]],"67":[[1,"35","5","Open Trade Policy and Regional Economic Cooperation Initiative","An open trade policy will facilitate a competi- tive environment for private sector develop- ment, avoid the high costs incurred with pro- tectionist policies and facilitate Afghanistan becoming better integrated as a 'trading hub' in the region.",""],[1,"37","4","Trade Transit Time Reduction and Border Management Cooperation","By end-2010 Afghanistan and its neighbors will achieve lower transit times through Afghanistan by means of cooperative border management and other multilateral or bilateral trade and transit agreements.",""]],"68":[[1,"42","7","Pollution Prevention and Abatement Measures","pre- vention and/or abatement of pollution;",""],[1,"42","7","Environmental Management Education and Awareness","improved environmental management, educa- tion and awareness.",""],[1,"42","7","Environmental Cost Appraisal Requirement","Throughout all sectors, any environmental costs will be fully ac- counted for in appraisals aimed at ensuring that benefits of proposed programs or projects.",""],[1,"98","5","Public Environmental Rights Framework","The Government will establish the following rights of the public (individuals and their associations) with regard to the environment:",""],[1,"163","5","Environmental Regulation and Standards Enforcement","Improved sector govern- ance includes environ- mental regulation as well as meaningful measures for enforcement of stan- dards.",""],[1,"163","5","Development of Environmental Protections under the Energy Law","The current energy law provides for environ- mental protections that are now being developed.",""],[1,"163","11","Environmental Impact Assessment and Management Plan Compliance","Environmental impact assessments and management plans will be prepared and implemented in accordance with Afghan Law for all works.",""],[1,"164","18","Environmental Planning and Regulatory Framework Reform","Introduction of an environ- mental focus in planning proc- esses and new regulatory frameworks, to cover wa- ter/waste management, pollu- tion control, etc.",""],[1,"164","18","Mandatory Environmental Impact Assessment for Urban Projects","Enforcement of environmental impact assessments for all ur- ban projects",""]],"69":[[1,"170","13","Regional Cooperation and Cross-Border Linkages for Private Sector Development","Efforts at developing closer regional coopera- tion with neighboring countries will help ex- pand markets for the private sector and con- tribute to the success of the private sector devel- opment strategy.",""],[1,"170","13","Domestic Market Integration and Cross-Border Connectivity","Open domestic markets with a strong private sector will further in- crease integration as trade, transport, com- munication and other links are made with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"179","8","Regional Cooperation for Investment and Trade Facilitation","A key objective in the regional cooperation strategy is to re- move barriers to investment and trade so that regional investors will be better able to do business in Afghanistan and Afghan firms will have greater access to regional markets.",""]],"70":[[1,"38","2","Telecommunications Access Expansion","With respect to telecommunications, the ANDS strategic objective is to expand access to mobile phone service to 80 percent of the country and greatly increase access and use of the internet by consumers, the private sector and the Government.",""],[1,"124","12","Affordable Communication Services Expansion","The ANDS strategic vision and goal for the In- formation and Communication Technology (ICT) sector is to make affordable communica- tion services available in every district and vil- lage of Afghanistan through an improved ena- bling environment for private sector invest- ment.",""],[1,"124","14","National Telecommunications Network Expansion","By end-2010, a national telecommunications network to be put in place so that more than 80 percent of Afghans will have access to affordable telecommunica- tions; and more than $100 million dollars per year will be generated in public revenues.",""],[1,"125","1","Telecom Infrastructure and Regulatory Reform","The basic principles have been given a statutory basis, in the form of the Telecom Law that was promulgated in December 2005.",""],[1,"125","1","ICT Applications and Information Society Programme","the ICT applications aspects are being implemented via the ICT Council, which was established in May 2007.",""],[1,"126","4","Telecommunications Access Expansion Program","The immediate goal of the sector is to increase access to telecom services to cover 80 percent of the country.",""],[1,"126","4","Fibre Optic and Copper Cable Network Completion","A key component of this effort will be the completion of the Fibre Optic Cable and Copper Cable Network, allowing an expansion of high-speed data services and extending mobile phone coverage.",""],[1,"126","4","Satellite-Based Telecommunications Services Deployment","For the next five years, MoCIT policies, working through ATRA will also de- ploy satellite-based services to the less popu- lated areas where personal mobile facilities are too costly.","MoCIT"],[1,"126","4","Village Telecommunications Coverage Expansion","The current program is to reach at least 3,000 villages by 2010.",""],[1,"126","6","ICT Enabling Environment Reform","the policy priority for the Government is the passage and implementation of ICT legislation that will create an appropriate environment for further growth and development.",""],[1,"126","6","ICT Infrastructure Development","The key programs of the ICT sector are (i) Ena- bling Environment (ii) Infrastructure Develop- ment (iii) E-Afghanistan (iv) ICT Literacy.",""],[1,"127","7","National ICT Network Expansion and Interconnection","National ICT networks will be expanded and interconnected so that at least 80 per- cent of Afghans will have access to afford- able telecom services.",""],[1,"127","9","Subnational ICT Consultation and Outreach","The ICT sector strategy incorporates feedback, proposed projects and comments from the Sub National Consultations.",""],[1,"127","9","Provincial and District ICT Outreach via Video Conferencing","The ministry actively utilized its video conferencing capabilities to reach out to all 34 provincial capitals and many of the 240 district capitals that are presently served by the District Communications Net- work (DCN) infrastructure.","MoCIT"],[1,"127","9","Telecom Development Fund Support for Remote Communities","ATRA is in the process of instituting greater responsiveness to the needs of remote communities, by making available financial support from the Telecom Develop- ment Fund (TDF) upon request from commu- nity leaders.","ATRA"],[1,"128","8","ICT Facilities Expansion","Access to facilities will be expanded.",""],[1,"235","12","MoCI HRM and Project Computerization","Computerize all HRM and project activities in MoCI to strengthen Human Resource and Program Management","MoCI"],[1,"249","5","Telecom Policy and Regulatory Reform","Development of policies, laws, regulations procedures and other normative acts to accelerate the role of telecom services to citizens",""],[1,"249","6","Telecom Development Fund Establishment","Establish Telecom Development Fund (TDF)",""],[1,"249","9","Curriculum and Regulatory Framework for ICT Training Centers","Developing Curriculum and Regulatory Framework for ICT Training Centers in the Private Sector",""],[1,"249","13","Pilot Home-Based ICT Work for Women","Pilot home based ICT related work for women",""],[1,"249","16","Establishment of ICT Centers in Provincial Capitals","Establishment of ICT centers in 34 Provincial capitals",""],[1,"249","19","District Communication Network Expansion","Expansion of District Communication Network (DCN)",""],[1,"277","31","ICT Sector Institutional Development","ICT Sector institutions will be built (2013)",""],[1,"278","3","National Telecommunications Network Expansion","By end-2010, a national telecommunications network to be put in place so that more than 80% of Afghans will have access to affordable telecommunications.",""]],"71":[[1,"42","3","National Anti-Corruption Strategy","The National Anti-Corruption Strategy is based on the following key goals: (i) enhancing government anti-corruption commitment and leadership; (ii) raising awareness of corruption and evaluating the effectiveness of anti- corruption measures; (iii) mainstreaming anti- corruption into government reforms and na- tional development; and (iv) strengthening the legal framework for fighting corruption and building an institutional capacity for effective implementation of the United Nations Conven- tion Against Corruption (UNCAC).",""],[1,"64","4","Anti-Corruption Reform in Key Sectors","The ANDS will also reduce corruption in key sectors such as justice, health, public administration and education, which will have a significant benefit for the poor.",""],[1,"72","7","Anti-Corruption Governance Reform","Fighting corruption will require credible demonstrations by high-level government - including strong commitments and clarification of institutional arrangements; public administration reform including merit-based selection and appointment of civil servants; improving governance at the sub-national",""],[1,"84","6","Anti-Corruption Reduction Measures in Security and Government Institutions","Reduction of corruption in the ANA, ANP and amongst other government officials;",""],[1,"88","14","Corruption Monitoring Mechanism","A monitoring mechanism to track corruption at high places, including the security sector, will be put in place by Jaddi 1387 (end- 2008).",""],[1,"91","3","Anti-Corruption Measures in Judiciary and Government","Measures to achieve a reduction of corruption in the judiciary and throughout the government will be introduced.",""],[1,"98","2","Corruption Monitoring Mechanism","A monitor- ing mechanism to track corruption in",""],[1,"174","15","Anti-Corruption Preventative Mechanisms","The Government is fully committed to control- ling corruption, promoting transparency and accountability through establishing new and effective preventative mechanisms and imple- menting the Afghanistan Compact Anti- Corruption Benchmarks.",""],[1,"174","15","Integrity-Based State Administration Reform","A key ANDS strategic objective is to establish a state administration that operates with integrity and accountability to provide an enabling environment for eco- nomic and social development, based upon the rule of law, impartiality in political decision- making, the proper management of public re- sources, the provision of efficient administra- tive systems and the active engagement of civil society.",""],[1,"174","16","National Anti-Corruption Strategy and Roadmap Implementation","The National Anti-Corruption Strategy and Roadmap developed as part of the ANDS will be implemented in support of the following strategic aims:",""],[1,"175","4","Public Accountability Strengthening","Strengthening Public Accountability: aimed at increasing the transparency and accountability of procedures and controls for the management of public resources and thereby deterring corrupt practices, or increasing the likelihood of detection of those practices and generating systemic improvement to prevent their future reoc- currence.",""],[1,"175","5","Legal and Judicial Framework Reinforcement for Anti-Corruption","Reinforcing the Legal Framework and Judicial System: aimed at ensuring the comprehensiveness and robustness of the legal and regulatory framework in order to support activities and measures of Afghanistan's anti corruption institutions and measures.",""],[1,"175","6","Anti-Corruption Mainstreaming Process","The anti-corruption mainstreaming process will be applied jointly with the security sector strategy and the economic and social develop- ment sector strategies to guide their completion in order to ensure that anti-corruption meas- ures are explicitly included and implicitly re- flected in their development proposals.",""],[1,"175","13","Anti-Corruption Measures Implementation","The Government is firmly committed to fully and effectively implementing these anti- corruption measures.",""],[1,"185","9","Anti-Corruption Measures for Aid Delivery","Some mitigating measures to improve anti-corruption in the area of aid delivery will be as follows: (i) increase publicly available information about donor aid provision at the national and provincial levels; (ii) harmonization of donor support around the Government's anti-corruption strategy as prescribed in the ANDS;",""],[1,"186","1","Corruption Vulnerability Assessment-Based Preventive Action","crease donor support for preventive action based on corruption vulnerability assessments of specific processes and actions practiced by government departments and agencies",""],[1,"186","2","Anti-Corruption and Rent-Seeking Reduction Measures","the Government will address this issue in an affirmative manner to win the trust, confidence and continued support of the donor community.",""],[1,"189","4","Public Administration Reform and Anti-Corruption Effort","However, for this to hap- pen, the Government is aware that continuous progress will need to be made in fighting cor- ruption and implementing public administra- tion reforms.",""],[1,"221","20","Anti-Corruption Measures","Take effective measures to Reduce Corruption",""],[1,"221","23","High-Level Government Corruption Monitoring","Monitor Corruption at high places of Government",""],[1,"221","29","Public Complaints Mechanism","Implement Public Complaints Mechanism",""],[1,"222","4","Public Anti-Corruption Awareness Programs","Implement Public awareness programs on anti-corruption issues",""],[1,"229","11","Public Anti-Corruption Awareness Campaign","Generate public awareness about corruption and anti- corruption issues",""],[1,"237","10","Conference Road Map Monitoring and Stocktaking System","Establish a system of stocktaking at six-month intervals to monitor implemen- tation of the Conference Road Map, with public dissemination of results.",""]],"72":[[1,"89","2","Sub-national Governance Strengthening","The main priorities for the governance sector are (ii) strengthen sub-national governance structures;",""],[1,"89","5","Provincial Functional Institutions and Trained Staff Establishment","Functional insti- tutions with trained staff will be established in each province to implement appropriate legal frameworks and appointment procedures.",""],[1,"89","6","Local Gender Equality Institutional Frameworks","Institutional and administra- tive frameworks will be established at the local government level that will enable women to play an important role in decision making (such as the CDCs established under the NSP).",""],[1,"89","6","Provincial and Local Council Elections","Provincial Councils (PC) with elected members are to be formed in every Province and, that District, Village and Mu- nicipal Councils and Mayors are to be elected through, free, general, secret and direct elec- tions every three years.",""],[1,"91","13","Sub-national Governance Policy Development","A sub-national governance policy will be developed.","Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG)"],[1,"91","13","Provincial Council Empowerment","Provincial Councils will be empowered.","Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG)"],[1,"91","13","Local Council Legal Framework Reform","Laws on District Councils, Municipal Councils, and Village Councils will be introduced.","Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG)"],[1,"91","13","Regular Local Elections","Regular elections of District Councils, Municipal Councils, Mayors and Village Councils will be held.","Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG)"],[1,"98","7","National Assembly Capacity Building Programme","The capacity of National Assembly Members will be built in drafting and ratification of legislation, re- view and input to the national budget review, oversight, and representation, and on issues related to women's rights, national security, international relations, and inter- ethnic relations.",""],[1,"98","7","Provincial Councils Capacity Strengthening","The Government will strengthen the capacity of Provincial Councils, support knowledge sharing and exchange among Provincial Coun- cils.",""],[1,"98","7","Sub-national Representative Bodies Strengthening","The Government will strengthen the elected sub-national representative bodies enabling them to perform their roles and fulfill their responsibilities towards their constituent citizens.",""],[1,"162","5","Devolution of Urban Development Responsibilities to Municipalities","responsibility for Urban Development is being devolved down to Municipalities, where municipal lead- ers are expected to be more responsive to real- istic needs of their cities and more accountable to their residents for municipal services.",""],[1,"162","5","National Solidarity Program Community Project Delivery","the National Solidarity Program's efforts to enable Commu- nity Development Councils implement projects to the benefit of their communities.",""],[1,"162","5","Provincial Development Oversight Coordination","provincial gov- ernors are being given greater responsibility to oversee development activities in their relevant provinces, to be coordinated by the Independ- ent Department for Local Governance under the supervision of the President for more effi- ciency.",""],[1,"164","20","Urban Institutional Reform and Strengthening","The strategy includes a strong focus on reform and strengthening of key urban institutions, both at the central and re- gional level, as a precon- dition of effective urban governance.",""],[1,"257","21","Sub-national Governance Legislation Review and Update","Review and update legislation concerning sub-national governance formal and informal structures, roles and responsibilities",""],[1,"257","22","Sub-national Development Coordination Requirement","Formulate and implement policy imperatives requiring all development actors to carry out their activities through the established sub-national structures",""],[1,"259","9","Capacity Development for Sub-National Governance Structures","Continue capacity development of the sub-national governance structures to enable them to play a greater role in the development process",""],[1,"259","10","Strengthen Sub-national Governance Structures through Sustainable Financial Mechanisms","Strengthen the sub-national governance structures through sustainable financial mechanisms",""],[1,"259","11","Local Governance Structure Development","Continue the establishment of the local governance informal and formal struc- tures and village and district levels",""],[1,"266","19","Kabul-Province Communications and Interaction Enhancement","Enhance communications and interactions between Kabul and provinces",""],[1,"270","21","Sub-national Governance Policy and Legal-Regulatory Framework","By end-1389 (20 March 2011), the Government will ensure formulation and implementation of sub-national governance policy and, its legal and regula- tory framework.",""],[1,"270","24","Basic Facilities and Mobility Support for Councils and Offices","By end-1392 (20 March 2013), all the councils and offices including munici- palities will have basic facilities and amenities including adequate built up space, computers, communication facility and furniture.",""],[1,"270","24","Mobility Support for Key Officials","The key officials at national and sub national level will have adequate means of mobility to make connection with the communities they are serving",""],[1,"282","38","Local Governance Strengthening","Local Governance will be strengthened (2013)",""]],"73":[[1,"170","10","Women’s Training and Credit Access Program","Also programs that will provide women with greater access to training and credit facilities and will encourage the women- owned and op- erated busi- nesses.",""]],"74":[[1,"91","16","Action Plan on Peace, Justice and Reconciliation Implementation","the Action Plan on Peace, Justice and Reconciliation will be implemented.",""],[1,"92","1","Transitional Justice and Peace, Reconciliation, and Justice Mechanism","The Government's Action Plan for Peace, Reconciliation and Justice in Afghanistan acknowledges that any mechanism for building peace and justice must be carried out with the active and meaningful participation of all national stakeholders, including the justice institutions.",""],[1,"94","31","Transitional Justice System Establishment","Begin the process of establishing a transitional justice system to record past human rights abuses and preserve the rights of victims consistent with the government's action plan for peace, reconciliation and justice.",""]],"75":[[1,"34","2","Integrated National Security Policy and Strategy","implementing an integrated and comprehen- sive national security policy and strategy",""],[1,"34","2","Security Sector Reform Program","building a robust security sector reform pro- gram",""],[1,"34","2","Civil-Military Coordination Strengthening","strengthening civil and military op- erations and coordination",""],[1,"34","2","Counter-Narcotics Role Expansion for Security Forces","increasing the role of security forces in counter-narcotics ac- tivities",""],[1,"34","2","Civilian Component Strengthening in Security Entities","strengthening the civilian com- ponents of security entities",""],[1,"81","2","Army Design and Force Structure Review","The \"Afghanization\" of the country's security will require: (iii) a reassessment of the design, composition and size of the army;",""],[1,"81","2","Accelerated Officer Training Programme","The \"Afghanization\" of the country's security will require: (iv) accelerated training for the officers; and (v) an intensified national recruitment drive.",""],[1,"81","2","National Recruitment Drive for the Army","The \"Afghanization\" of the country's security will require: (iv) accelerated training for the officers; and (v) an intensified national recruitment drive.",""],[1,"81","4","Build Capacity of National Armed and Security Forces","The Government aims to secure stronger commitments from NATO whilst building the capacity of Afghanistan's national armed and other security forces.",""],[1,"82","1","Professional Capacity Building for Afghan Security Forces","This includes special attention to building the professional capabilities of Afghan security forces designed to defeat terrorism and to render assistance to victims of war and avoid civilian casualties.",""],[1,"83","5","Afghan National Army Security and Stability Support","Through Jaddi 1389 (end-2010), with the support of and in close coordination with the government, the NATO-led ISAF, Operation Enduring Freedom (OEF) and their respective Provincial Reconstruction Teams (PRTs) will promote security and stability in all regions of Afghanistan, including by strengthening Afghan capabilities.",""],[1,"83","6","National Army Professionalization and Expansion Programme","the Government will establish a nationally respected, professional, ethnically balanced ANA that is accountable, organized, trained and well equipped to meet the security needs of the country.",""],[1,"84","13","Ministry of Defense Reform and Capacity Building","Reforms and capacity building initiatives are in process to make the MoD more transparent and accountable with a strong administration and internal discipline.","MoD"],[1,"84","13","Professional National Army Development","The MoD is developing an ethnically balanced, non- political army with a single military doctrine and operational capabilities.","MoD"],[1,"84","13","National Army Education, Training, and Equipping Programme","Education, train- ing and equipping the national army to create a professional army with strong operational ca- pability to fight terrorism and armed groups are top priorities.","MoD"],[1,"85","4","National Army Recruitment and Training Drive","A reassessment of the design, composition and size of the ANA has led to intensified national recruitment drive and training.",""],[1,"85","5","National Army Development and Expansion","Following a presidential decree to establish a National Army in 2003 the Ministry of Defense and the Afghan National Army have achieved considerable progress.","Ministry of Defense"],[1,"87","1","Afghan National Army Professionalization and Operational Cohesion Programme","Phase Three will encompass efforts to further improve professionalism, discipline and operational cohesiveness and the ANA will conduct independent operations and lead the fight.",""],[1,"88","13","MoD Reform and Reconstruction","MoD reform and reconstruction aim to rehabilitate a strong defense sector to protect national security and to be able to begin assuming primary responsibility for Afghanistan's security with a gradual withdrawal of international security forces.",""],[1,"88","13","Intensive Field and Operational Training for ANA and ANP","Intensive field and operational train- ing is and will continue to further enhance the capabilities of the ANA and ANP.",""],[1,"88","21","Security Force Capacity Development Programs","Specific capacity development programs will be required for preparing the security forces for counter narcotics operations.",""],[1,"219","7","Army Personnel Expansion and Mentorship Staffing","Recruit additional personnel to reach the newly agreed 80,000 army ceiling with additional 6000 staff of mentors, trainers etc",""],[1,"219","9","Technical and Administrative Support for the ANA","Equip the ANA with technical and administrative support",""],[1,"219","11","New ANA Training Centers","Establish new ANA training centers",""],[1,"219","12","Upgrade Existing ANA Training Centers and Academies","Equip existing ANA training centers/Academies",""],[1,"219","13","ANA Reform and Capacity Building Programme","Reform and capacity building of the ANA to a sustainable level",""],[1,"219","14","Army Logistical Support Strengthening","Strengthen logistical support to the Army in regional and provincial battalions",""],[1,"219","15","Computerized Management System for the Ministry of Defense","Establish computerized system in MoD to strengthen human resource, financial and program management","MoD"],[1,"219","16","Counterterrorism Training Schemes for National Units","Extensive training schemes to equip national units to fight terrorism and anti gov- ernment elements",""],[1,"219","20","Right-Financing Approach for the Security Sector","Develop a 'Right-financing' approach to the security sector",""]],"76":[[1,"34","3","Training and Equipment Support for the ANP","The ANP has been receiving extensive training and equipment from the international community.",""],[1,"82","4","Police Reform and Judicial Strengthening Initiative","As the police are re- formed and the judicial system strengthened, a major effort will be made to reduce corruption, better policing officials involved in cultivation and interfering with eradication efforts.",""],[1,"83","7","Professionalization and Expansion of the Afghan National Police and Border Police","By Jaddi 1389 (end-2010) a fully constituted, professional, functional and ethnically balanced Afghan National Police and Afghan Border Police with a combined force of up to 82,180 will be able to effectively meet the security needs of the country and will be increasingly fiscally sustainable.",""],[1,"85","9","Border Police Force Establishment","Establish a border police force to control cross-border movements and assist with collection of customs revenues in coopera- tion with MoD, ANA and Ministry of Fi- nance (MoF);","MoD | ANA | Ministry of Finance (MoF)"],[1,"85","13","Police Reform and Capacity-Building Programme","The Police are undergoing reforms aimed enhancing efficiency by improving police training and education, upgrading staff and equipping the department adequately.",""],[1,"219","23","Police Technical and Administrative Support","Equip the Police with technical and administrative support",""],[1,"219","24","ANP and ABP Reform and Capacity Building","Reform and capacity building of the ANP and ABP to a sustainable level",""],[1,"219","25","Logistical Support Strengthening for ANP and ABP","Strengthen logistical support to ANP and ABP in regional and provincial centers",""],[1,"220","2","Police Station and Substation Construction","Construct new Stations and Substations for Police in Provinces",""],[1,"220","5","Police Health Care Center Establishment and Equipping","Establish/Equip Health care centers/facilities for Police in center and provinces",""],[1,"220","6","Counterterrorism Training Schemes for National Units","Extensive training schemes to equip national units to fight terrorism and anti gov- ernment elements",""],[1,"220","9","Police Capacity-Building for Drug Law Enforcement","Conduct training to increase the capacity of Afghan National Police forces to en- force the law against poppy cultivation and drug trafficking",""],[1,"220","10","Ministry of Interior Reform to Support Police Transformation","MoI reform to support the transformation of police",""],[1,"220","11","Computerized Management System for the Ministry of Interior","Establish computerized system in MoI to strengthen human resource, financial and program management","MoI"],[1,"220","13","Border Police Reform, Training, and Equipment Programme","Reform, train and equip the Border Police",""],[1,"220","14","Border Post Establishment and Rehabilitation","Establish/Rehabilitate and equip Border Posts",""],[1,"220","16","Right-Financing Approach for the Security Sector","Develop a 'Right-financing' approach to the security sector",""],[1,"220","17","Security Sector Revenue and Financing Reform","Improve revenues and finance security sector spending; this includes licenses to private security companies",""],[1,"235","16","Border Crossing Points and Facilities Establishment Initiative","Border Management Initiative to focus on the establishment of effective and efficient Border Crossing Points/Facilities at each Border Control Zone of Afghanistan.",""]],"77":[[1,"64","4","Justice Access and Reform Initiative","Greater access to justice, especially for women, is an important component of the ANDS to empower the poor and provide more efficient protection to victims of violence.",""],[1,"85","11","Witness Protection and Victim Support Services","Provide witness protection and support to victims of crime and establish detention centers;",""],[1,"91","12","Fair Land Dispute Settlement System","A modern and community-based land administration system and establishment of a fair system for settlement of land disputes will be established.",""],[1,"93","16","Nationwide Legal Information and Representation Access","nationwide ac- cess to legal information and representa- tion",""],[1,"94","24","Legal and Policy Framework for Juvenile Offenders Reform","Enhance legal and policy framework related to juvenile offenders and children in conflict with the law.",""],[1,"228","18","Legal Awareness Programs","Design legal awareness programs paying particular atten- tion to: · Successes and lessons learned from previous campaigns · Human rights and Islamic values · The rights of women and children · The needs of illiterate persons · Transitional justice · The roles of each justice institution in promoting access to justice for all.",""],[1,"228","19","Legal Awareness Programs","Implement legal awareness programs, in coordination with",""],[1,"229","2","Expansion of Formal Justice Systems to Provinces","activities expanding formal justice systems to provinces.",""],[1,"229","3","Legal Aid Service Provision Baseline Survey","Conduct baseline survey legal aid service provision",""],[1,"229","4","Legal Aid System Design and Recommendation Development","Consider options and costs of various models for legal aid delivery, and draw up recommendations for a legal aid system.",""],[1,"229","5","Legal Aid Recommendation Implementation","Implement legal aid recommendations",""],[1,"229","6","Needs Assessment and Legal Access Barrier Survey","Conduct needs assessment and survey of obstacles to access to and use of formal legal system.",""],[1,"229","7","Formal Legal System Access and Use Expansion","Draw up recommendations to increase access to and use of formal legal system",""],[1,"230","7","Criminal Justice Rights Information Campaigns","Develop information campaigns to enhance the public's knowledge of the rights of victims, witnesses, and the accused in the criminal justice system",""]],"78":[[1,"194","21","Human Capital Capacity-Building Strategy","Improve government and civil society capacity through a human capital strategy;",""],[1,"195","6","Private Sector Skills Development Programme","Apart from this the high priority will be given to skill development programs to meet the needs of the private sector and increase employment.",""]],"79":[[1,"42","8","Aid-Funded Activity Monitoring and Aid Coordination Unit","The Government has implemented processes to increase the monitoring of aid-funded activities and to improve the efficiency of implementation.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"42","8","Increased Core Budget Support","The Government would like to see increased core budget support (direct budget support), giving greater ownership and enabling a more effective allocation of resources based on needs and priorities.",""],[1,"42","8","Use of Established Trust Funds for Aid Channeling","Channeling aid through established trust funds is also effective, with the Government able to access funds on an as needed basis.",""],[1,"42","8","Pooling of Donor Funds","Pooling of donor funds also significantly reduces the duplication of",""],[1,"43","4","Donor Project Alignment and Core Budget Channeling Mechanism","prove its absorption capacity and fiduciary practices to encourage donors to implement their projects through the National (Core) Budget or, if this is not possible, to assure that programs or projects implemented through the external budget are aligned with the ANDS objectives and priorities.",""],[1,"43","5","Consultative and Working Groups for Aid Coordination","The Consultative and Working Groups will continue to be the key forums for improving aid coordination and ensure alignment of the donor programs and projects with the ANDS.",""],[1,"62","1","Donor Coordination and Aid Effectiveness Improvement","Improving donor coordination and aid- effectiveness: donor support as well as im- proved donor coordination together with the elimination of duplication in delivering assistance to the poor will be essential to the success of the ANDS poverty reduction strategy.",""],[1,"183","1","Aid Effectiveness Framework Strengthening","the Government remains concerned about the urgent need to strengthen the aid delivery framework (management, coordination, mobilization, and effectiveness) to improve results, particularly at the sub-national level.",""],[1,"184","2","Aid Effectiveness and Donor Coordination Initiative","The Government is strongly committed to making aid more effec- tive by working with donors to achieve the benchmarks set out in the Paris Declaration and the Afghanistan Compact.",""],[1,"184","2","ANDS Ownership and Implementation Support","The Government will continue to work on to deepen the ownership and successful implementation of the ANDS.",""],[1,"184","10","Aid Effectiveness Improvement Framework","Key objectives are to increase aid effectiveness and maximize the impact of international assistance and achieve the following objectives: (i) improved security and stability; (ii) reduced poverty; (iii) enhanced environment for private sector development; (iv) further democratization of Afghan society in accordance with the Islamic values; and (v) increased social inclusion and equality.",""],[1,"185","2","Aid Effectiveness Reform","The Government will implement reforms that will lead to higher transparency and absorption capacities.",""],[1,"185","2","Donor Aid Delivery Improvement Measures","Donors will be expected to under- take measures to improve aid delivery in line with the Paris Declaration.",""],[1,"185","3","Aid Portfolio Monitoring and Donor Alignment Mechanism","the Ministry of Finance will monitor the Government's total aid portfolio and it will, in collaboration with line ministries, encourage donors to channel their resources in a manner that is consistent with the principles of Islam, the Government's Aid Policy and the ANDS priorities.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"186","3","Aid Flow Reporting and Predictability Improvement","Improve information on aid flows and predictability:","MoF"],[1,"186","5","Financial Reviews and Harmonized Reporting Format for Aid Management","The conduct of the Financial Reviews and the implementation of the Harmonized Reporting Format since October 2007 will enable the Government to access comprehensive and coordinated information on aid flows as well as highlight the problems and issues impeding project implementation, improving aid management.",""],[1,"186","10","Aid Coordination and Parallel Funding Integration Mechanism","Prior to the allocation of resources for parallel funding, there should be consultation with the Government through existing consultation mechanisms (CGs, WGs, Aid Effectiveness CG and JCMB).",""],[1,"187","2","Aid Management Procedure Simplification and Flexible Conditionality Reform","Both the Government and donors should aim to further simplify their processes and procedures for implementation of programs and projects, to avoid unnecessary delays in implementation.",""],[1,"187","5","Donor Coordination Harmonization Framework","The ANDS sets the framework for improving donor coordination in line with the Paris Declaration which recommends greater alignment between ODA and the ANDS.",""],[1,"187","7","Government-Donor Mutual Accountability Framework","Future Government / donor cooperation needs to be based on the basic principle of mutual accountability.",""],[1,"187","7","Benchmark Development for Commitment Tracking","Furthermore, benchmarks will be developed to measure progress against commitments on both sides.",""],[1,"187","7","Alignment of Donor External Funding with ANDS Priorities","From the donor side the Government expects that the donor external funding will be in line with the ANDS priorities.",""],[1,"190","2","Government-Donor Partnership Strengthening Policy","The Government's aid policy aims to strengthen the partnership with the donors by encouraging information sharing and policy dialogue, at both sectoral and program levels.",""],[1,"190","2","Joint Analytical Projects with Donors","the Government's policy will en- courage the launching of joint analytical pro- jects between the Government and donors.",""],[1,"190","2","Memoranda of Understanding with Donors","the Government will develop agree- ments-in the form of Memoranda of Under- standing with all donors in which rights; mu- tual obligations; and accountabilities are clearly identified.",""],[1,"190","5","Improved Government and Donor Representation in Consultations","Government and donors will improve their representation to ensure that only representatives with adequate technical expertise will take part in consultations;",""],[1,"190","6","Consultative Group Meeting Secretariat Establishment","The ministries and agencies chairing the meetings will establish secretariats including the participation of technical people from the leading donor agencies;",""],[1,"190","8","Joint Government-Donor Sub-Groups on Specific Issues","Where necessary, joint Government/Donor sub-groups should be formed on specific issues to improve efficiency of develop- ment work.",""],[1,"190","9","Continued Donor Support for Long-Term Sustainable Development","For Afghanistan to shift from recovery-related growth to long-term sustainable development, additional continued and efficient donor sup- port will be required.",""],[1,"190","10","Aid Delivery Mechanism Improvement","both the Government and donors will have to do more to improve aid delivery mechanism and efficiency to bring more tangible changes to the life of ordinary Afghans.",""],[1,"197","13","Aid Alignment and Development Partnership Framework","A forward-looking partnership between Afghanistan and the international community is needed to ensure external aid is managed in line with the ANDS and recommendations of the Paris Declaration.",""],[1,"197","13","Core Budget Aid Delivery Expansion","The implementation of the ANDS will depend upon the donors to implement more programs and projects through the Core Budget.",""],[1,"213","4","Government-Donor Coordination Framework","As such, the ANDS will help to coordinate and guide the joint activities of the Government and donors.",""],[1,"215","7","Aid Alignment and Coordination under the Integrated Approach","The ANDS addresses the questions of the amounts and distribution of aid that will be required in the coming five years and the most effective modes of delivery.",""]],"80":[[1,"39","5","Media Legislation Reform","Media legislation will be enacted to provide a stable and predictable environment in which a largely privately run and independent media can operate.",""],[1,"39","5","Public Afghan Media Expansion","Key priorities include a country-wide coverage of public Afghan media (radio and television), an increased number of hours of public broadcasting, and improved quality of programming.",""],[1,"39","5","State-Owned Media Public Information Use","state-owned media will be used to promote and convey information on gender policies, public health and national security.",""],[1,"91","4","Public Right to Information Expansion","Public rights to access to information will be increased.",""],[1,"149","8","Media Independence and Public Debate Support","The Government is committed to furthering this public debate and independence of media.",""],[1,"150","2","State-Owned Media Reform for Editorial Independence","State-owned media needs to be reformed in order to ensure that it promotes democratic values and is editorially independent of influences from various interested factions.",""],[1,"150","3","Media Legislation for Free and Independent Media","Media legislation that will provide an environment in which a free, independent and responsible media can operate has been drafted.",""],[1,"150","12","Independent Media Legal Framework","To establish legislation that will provide a stable and predictable environment in which a largely private sector, independent media can operate;",""],[1,"150","13","Media for Education Initiative","Media will be employed as an educational tool in addition to entertainment.",""],[1,"150","15","New Media Legislation and Open Administration","New Media legislation will have been passed and Government and the Ministry will successfully administer this legislation in an open manner;","Government | the Ministry"],[1,"150","16","Country-wide Public Afghan Media Coverage","A country-wide coverage of public Afghan media (radio and television);",""],[1,"150","18","Media Independence and Press Freedom Protection","the need to promote and protect the independence of the media as well as ensure press freedom is extremely important;",""],[1,"150","19","Press Freedom Protection Reform","the Government will work to reverse setbacks and ensure that press freedom be protected both in legislation and in practice.",""],[1,"151","7","New Media Legislation and Implementation","the passage of the new Media legislation and its implementation",""]],"81":[[1,"73","15","Land Access Facilitation Measures","Implement measures to facilitate access to land by clarifying property rights, simplifying procedures for the transfer of titles, and allowing for longer-term leases.",""],[1,"73","17","Private Land Transfer Procedure Simplification","Implementing improved and sim- plified procedures for transfer of privately owned land;",""],[1,"73","18","Land Registration and Adjudication Legal Framework Reform","Developing better legal frameworks for land registration and land adjudication.",""],[1,"91","12","Modern and Community-Based Land Administration System","A modern and community-based land administration system and establishment of a fair system for settlement of land disputes will be established.",""],[1,"223","10","Modern Land Administration System","Establish Modern Land Administration System",""],[1,"223","14","Land Dispute Settlement System","Establish A fair System for Settlement of Land Disputes",""]],"82":[[1,"81","1","National Security Policy and Security Sector Reform Program","The Government has developed the National Security Policy to be implemented through the Security Sector Reform (SSR) program.",""],[1,"81","2","Comprehensive Security Sector Reform","The \"Afghanization\" of the country's security will require: (i) comprehensive security sector reform;",""],[1,"81","2","Security Force Division of Labor Reconfiguration","The \"Afghanization\" of the country's security will require: (ii) a new division of labor between the international security forces and the Afghan National Army (ANA);",""],[1,"81","4","Strengthen NATO Security Commitments","The Government aims to secure stronger commitments from NATO whilst building the capacity of Afghanistan's national armed and other security forces.",""],[1,"82","1","Strengthening ISAF and Coalition Forces Assistance","To defeat terrorism, new strategies attuned with political objectives of the Government are being adopted, such as strengthening the effectiveness of ISAF and Coalition Forces assistance.",""],[1,"82","1","Strengthening Government Ownership of Law Enforcement","The government aims at strengthening its ownership over law enforcement to effectively overcome internal security problems.",""],[1,"82","1","Integrated Counter-Crime and Narcotics Control Strategy","Furthermore, combating criminal activity and increased narcotics production are integrated components of the security strategy.",""],[1,"83","3","Security Sector Reform Coordination Mechanism","The Security Sector Reforms Strategy establishes a mechanism to regulate relations between ministries and departments to ensure effective coordination.",""],[1,"84","11","Coordination of Security Institutions","To improve professional capabilities of the security institutions their duties and responsibilities need to be coordinated.",""],[1,"84","12","National Security Council Strategic Coordination and Oversight","The Council, led by the President, is responsible for developing strategies and policies, determining priorities, and is responsible for the oversight and coordination of the security sector and institutions.",""],[1,"86","13","Accelerated Development of Afghan Security Forces","In line with a three phased effort to develop the Afghan military, coalition allies will move progressively from carrying the major burden of combat operations to a supporting and enabling role.",""],[1,"87","6","Integrated National Security Policy and Strategy","The Government is fully committed to success- fully: (i) implementing an integrated and com- prehensive national security policy and strat- egy;",""],[1,"87","6","Security Sector Reform Programme","The Government is fully committed to success- fully: (ii) building a robust security sector reform program;",""],[1,"88","7","Defense and Security Sector Reform","Reforming defense and the security sector is a priority of the Afghan Government to strengthen Afghan capabilities and transform the Afghan security forces into effective and modern force, confirming to",""],[1,"193","1","Security Operations and Rule of Law Stabilization","Stabilizing conditions in Afghanistan will require continuing security operations combined with the implementation of the rule of law and credible sub-national governance.",""],[1,"194","19","Security Improvement through Governance, Rule of Law, and Regional Cooperation","Improve security through governance, rule of law and regional cooperation;",""],[1,"213","4","Security and Governance Improvement Measures","This requires simultaneous progress on improving security, strengthening governance, increasing the effectiveness in delivering basic social services and taking the actions necessary to ensure that the private sector can invest and operate competitively.",""],[1,"214","7","Integrated National Security Policy and Strategy","the Government is fully committed to successfully: (i) implementing an integrated and comprehensive national security policy and strategy;",""],[1,"214","7","Security Sector Reform Program","(ii) building a robust security sector reform program;",""],[1,"214","7","Civil and Military Operations Strengthening","(iii) strengthening civil and military operations;",""],[1,"214","7","Security Capability Enhancement for Armed Forces","This requires sufficient resources to enhance the capabilities of the country's armed forces, including the ANA, ANP and NSD, which is only possible through joint efforts and long-term commitments of the international community to Afghanistan.",""]],"83":[[1,"102","8","Establishment of Effective Commercial Courts","A high priority of the ANDS is the strengthening of the institutions, including the establishment of effective commercial courts, responsible for the implementation of commercial laws.",""],[1,"103","2","Commercial Law Reform for Private Sector Development","Legislative Reform: Enact and implement key commercial laws and amendments to establish the basic legal and regulatory framework that will encourage private sector involvement in social and economic development and consistent with the Afghan conditions.",""],[1,"103","3","Implementation of Remaining Commercial Laws","The Government will introduce and implement the remaining commercial laws included in the Afghanistan Compact benchmark.",""],[1,"103","4","Inclusive Policy and Law Consultation Mechanism","The Government will consult with representatives from private business and civil society in a meaningful and timely manner during the process of drafting policies and laws.",""],[1,"103","5","Mediation and Arbitration Tribunals for Dispute Resolution","The necessary steps will be taken to establish the authority of mediation and arbitration tribunals to resolve private-private and private-public disputes, including land issues.",""],[1,"103","6","Public Law and Regulation Publication Requirement","The Government will ensure that no law will be implemented unless it has been published in the newspapers, and made available electronically and in hard copy to the public.",""],[1,"103","6","Online Disclosure of Regulations and Import Tariff Rates","Regulations, including import tariff rates, will be made readily available on the Ministry of Finance website.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"103","7","Administrative Reform for Commercial Law Administration","The Government will ensure that ministries and agencies are able to competently administer commercial laws and regulations in an unbiased and predictable manner.",""],[1,"103","8","National Assembly Capacity Development","Invest in capacity development for National Assembly so that MPs are better informed and supported in their role and understanding of proposed laws.",""],[1,"103","9","Tribunal Competency and Transparency Capacity-Building","Ensure the competency and transpar- ency of tribunals by establishing stan- dards and building the capacity of arbi- trators, mediators and lawyers.",""],[1,"103","19","Financial Tribunal Establishment","The financial tribunal will be established to provide swift legal resolution of financial disputes.",""],[1,"231","10","Private Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework Reform","Enact the required laws (Corporations, Partnerships, Commercial Arbitration, Commercial Mediation, Contracts, Agency, Standards, Copyrights, Trade- marks, and Patents) to complete and update the basic legal and regulatory framework governing private sector activity in social and economic develop- ment.",""],[1,"231","14","Private Sector and Civil Society Consultation Mechanism","Establish the principle and formalize and standardize processes to consult with the private sector (business and civil society) in a meaningful and timely man- ner during the process of drafting policies and laws.",""],[1,"232","4","Tariff Legislation Amendment for ROZ Trade Facilitation","Amend the tariff legislation to facilitate ROZ (Reconstruction Opportunity Zone) trade along the border with Pakistan",""],[1,"232","6","Mediation and Arbitration Tribunal Authority for Dispute Resolution","Endorse the authority of mediation and arbitration tribunals to resolve private- private and private-public disputes, including land issues.",""],[1,"232","7","Tribunal Competency and Transparency Strengthening","Ensure the competency and transparency of tribunals by establishing standards and building the capacity of arbitrators, mediators and lawyers.",""],[1,"232","21","Financial Tribunal Establishment","Establish a financial tribunal to provide swift legal decisions on financial disputes.",""],[1,"243","7","Mortgage Law Legislation and Enforcement","Pass required legislation and enabling regulations so that the Mortgage law is passed and enforced.",""],[1,"243","9","Contract Law and Enforcement Reform","Pass any required legislation and enabling regulations so that private and pub- lic sector rights are protected in contract law, enforcement, and penalties for violation.",""],[1,"243","14","Insurance, Auditing, and Bonding Sector Regulatory Reform","Pass any required legislation and enabling regulations so that private sector insurance, auditing, and bonding industries can develop, and foreign insurance firms can operate in Afghanistan, protecting rights of the companies and the public, with penalties for violations.",""]],"84":[[1,"40","2","Health Regulatory and Accreditation Reform","The Ministry of Public Health (MoPH) will review and develop relevant legal and regulatory mechanisms, such as accreditation systems, that govern health and health related work in the public and private sectors.","Ministry of Public Health (MoPH)"],[1,"40","2","Health Service Contracting and Private Sector Expansion","The goal of the regulatory system will be to facilitate competitive and cost effective provision of services, carrying out its broader mandate to not only contract out service provision to civil and private groups but also to facilitate growth of the 'for profit' sector.",""],[1,"40","2","Evidence-Based Health Research Coordination","The MoPH will work to identify, encourage, coordinate, and review and in some cases conduct relevant, useful research that can assist evidence-based decision making and the formulation of new policies, strategies and plans.","MoPH"],[1,"139","6","Health Sector Regulatory and Accreditation Reform","MoPH will also review and develop relevant legal and regulatory mechanisms, such as accreditation systems, that govern health and health related work in the public and private sectors.","MoPH"],[1,"139","6","Health Service Quality and Public Protection Enforcement","MoPH will also review, develop and enforce relevant legal and regulatory instruments that govern health and health related work to safeguard the public and ensure service quality.","MoPH"],[1,"139","6","Health Research Coordination and Evidence-Based Policy Support","MoPH will work to identify, encourage, coordinate, and review and in some cases conduct relevant, useful research that can assist evidence-based decision making and the formulation of new policies, strategies and plans.","MoPH"],[1,"139","6","Private Health Provider Growth Facilitation","One area of resource is with respect to facilitating the growth of the private sector providers operating on their own outside the framework of contracts from MoPH.","MoPH"],[1,"139","7","Competitive Recruitment for Health Workforce Placement","The MoPH will work closely with the Civil Service Com- mission to implement the National Priority Re- form and Restructuring competitive recruit- ment processes for placing the most highly qualified Afghan health professionals in estab- lished posts throughout all levels of the health system.","MoPH | Civil Service Com- mission"],[1,"139","7","Health Sector Quality Improvement Measures","Efforts will be made to promote a cul- ture of quality throughout the Health and Nu- trition Sector, especially in health facilities, through leadership and good examples set in day-to-day work, strengthen the use of quality standards, and promote frequent supportive- supervision.",""],[1,"139","7","Private Health Sector Regulatory Enforcement","Once effective regulatory mechanisms are developed and can be enforced, the MoPH will address quality issues in the private-for-profit sector, especially pharmacies and drug sellers.","MoPH"],[1,"139","7","Comprehensive Health Workforce Development Strategy","A comprehensive approach to human resource development will be developed to produce, deploy and retain where they are needed an appropriately trained health workforce pos-",""],[1,"140","1","Health Care Worker Registration and Certification System","Further develop and maintain a health care worker registration system and a national testing and certification examination process (in collaboration with the Ministry of Higher Education) will be established standards for accreditation of training institutes and pro- grams.","Ministry of Higher Education"],[1,"140","1","Community Midwife Training Program Expansion","There will be a significant Expansion of the community midwife training program model to other cadres of health workers, with particular emphasis on recruiting, training and deploying couples to work together in health facilities in their community after graduation.",""]],"85":[[1,"151","11","Civil Servants and Military Basic Pension Scheme","Although highly dependent on budget transfers, the basic pension scheme for civil servants and military personal has been established.",""],[1,"151","11","Pension Department Technical Assistance","the MoLSAMD's Pension Department receives technical assistance for further improvements","MoLSAMD"],[1,"151","11","Pension Contribution Collection Intensification","the MoF has intensified its effort on collecting pension contributions.","MoF"],[1,"153","4","Pension Reform Implementation","By 2012/13 pension reforms will be implemented;",""],[1,"153","10","Fiscally Sustainable Social Support and Pension Systems","build fiscally sustainable social support and pension systems",""],[1,"154","7","Pension System Integration of Cash Transfers","The current cash transfers to the martyr's families and individuals with war related disabilities will be integrated into the pension system and will cease to be part of the social support system.",""],[1,"155","5","Integration of Cash Transfers into the Pension System","Integrate the current direct cash transfers to martyr's families and people with disabili- ties into the pension system;",""],[1,"155","16","Pension Reform","Pension reform: The main objective of pen- sion reform will be to improve old-age protec- tion (especially for civil servants and military) and establish fiscally sustainable pension schemes.",""],[1,"155","16","Pension Contribution Collection Enhancement","Priorities will include the enhance- ment of fiscal sustainability by increasing col- lection of the pension contributions, and build- ing the capacity of the Pension Department",""],[1,"155","16","Pension Department Capacity Building","Priorities will include the enhance- ment of fiscal sustainability by increasing col- lection of the pension contributions, and build- ing the capacity of the Pension Department",""],[1,"155","17","Pension Reform Design","Design of the pension reform: Coverage: The future pension system will cover the same groups of employees that are covered in the current system (civil servants and military per- sonal).",""],[1,"156","1","Pension System Reform","Pension benefits will be increased in absolute terms (as a result of Pay and Grading reform), but reduced as a percentage of last drawn pay of an employee.",""],[1,"156","1","War Survivor Pension Benefits","In addition to regular pen- sions benefits will be provided to pre- retirement and post-retirement war survivors.",""],[1,"156","1","Integration of War-Related Cash Transfers into Pension System","The existing direct cash transfers to martyr's families and individuals with war related dis- ability will be integrated into the future pen- sion system.",""],[1,"156","2","Pension System Self-Financing Reform","The pension system will be self-financed from government and employee contributions on wages (payroll tax).",""],[1,"156","3","Pension Reform Support under the National Social Protection Sector Program","The implementation of pension reforms will also be supported through the National Social Protection Sector Program.",""],[1,"156","5","Pension Reform Decree","Promulgate pension reform by the Gov- ernment decree;",""],[1,"156","6","Pension Department Capacity Building and IT System Upgrade","Conduct capacity building and training for the staff and managers of the Pension De- partment, and develop new IT system and processes;",""],[1,"156","7","Accounting and Internal Procedures Modernization","Modernize accounting and internal opera- tional procedures in harmony with the IT system implementation and improve re- cord keeping and processes;",""],[1,"156","8","Pension Payroll Tax Collection and Central Pension Database","Improve collection of the pension payroll taxes and establish a central database to store and process the details on pensioners and their bank accounts;",""],[1,"156","9","Pension Payment Through Banks","Introduce payments of pensions through banks in Kabul by mid-2009, and through- out the country by end 2010 subject to availability of banking services.",""],[1,"156","10","Pension Department Capacity Strengthening and Pension Payment Reform","Employees of the current pension department, including management, will be required to go through comprehensive training.",""],[1,"169","10","Pension Department Capacity Building for Pension Reform Implementation","To improve the capacity of the Pension Department for implementation of the pension reform",""],[1,"264","2","Pension Reform Decree","Promulgate the pension reform by the Government decree",""],[1,"264","3","Pension Department Accounting and Internal Procedures Modernization","Modernize accounting as well as internal operational procedures of the Pension Department",""],[1,"264","4","Pension Department IT System and Process Development","Develop the new IT system and processes of the Pension Department",""],[1,"264","5","Pension Contribution Collection Improvement","Improve collection of the pension contributions (payroll taxes)",""],[1,"264","6","Central Pensioners Database","Establish a central database to store and process the details on pensioners and their bank accounts",""],[1,"264","7","Pension Payments Through Banks","Introduce payments of pensions through banks",""],[1,"264","8","Pension Department Capacity Strengthening","Improve the capacity of the Pension Department of MoLSAMD","MoLSAMD"],[1,"264","9","Pension Department Record-Keeping and Anti-Corruption Reform","Improve record keeping and processes of the Pension Department and mini- mize any corrupt practices",""],[1,"264","11","Pension Department Capacity Building and Training","Conduct the capacity building and training for the staff and managers of the Pension Department",""],[1,"285","22","Pension Reform and Contribution Collection Improvement","By 2012/13 implement the pension reform and increase collec- tion of the pension contributions",""]],"86":[[1,"177","9","Institutional Capacity Development Leadership Mechanism","The Government, through specific institution build- ing will take the lead in directing capacity de- velopment to where it is most needed and to evaluating the impact of capacity development and technical assistance programs.",""],[1,"177","9","Inter-Ministerial Commission for Capacity Development","This insti- tutional responsibility will be with Inter- ministerial Commission for Capacity Devel- opment (ICCD) that will serve as a single re- porting point for both the Government and donors.",""],[1,"177","9","Cross-Sector Capacity Development Goal Setting","ICCD will work out detailed goals for capacity development that will serve cross- sectoral purposes.",""],[1,"177","10","Use of Afghan Expatriates and Regional Technical Experts in Donor-Funded Projects","The Government encourages donors to donor- funded projects to engage to the maximum ex- tent possible qualified Afghan expatriates and to make greater use of technical experts from the region.",""],[1,"177","10","Capacity-Building Project Design Based on Regional Human Resources","Development projects that focus on capacity building should increasingly be designed to build on regional human resource capacity.",""],[1,"177","10","Managerial Capacity Building for Public and Private Sectors","The Government also recognizes that increasing reliance on building managerial ca- pacity in both the public and private sectors will be necessary to effectively implement the goals of the ANDS.",""],[1,"177","11","Institutional Mechanism for Capacity Development","this will require a well structured institutional mechanism which has to be built and constantly strengthened.",""],[1,"180","3","Capacity Development Coordination Mechanisms","The Government has established mechanisms to ensure that the enormous resources being devoted to developing capacity in the public and private sectors are utilized in the most effective ways possible.",""],[1,"193","1","Integrated ANDS Implementation Framework","The implementation framework for the ANDS is based on an integrated approach that will be structured to address the three interdependent pillars of security; governance, rule of law and human rights; and economic and social development, and five cross-cutting issues.",""],[1,"193","7","Integrated Joint Implementation Approach","The implementation of the ANDS will be based on an integrated approach to these challenges, uniting government, international community, civil society and private sector effort in support of common goals, shared policies and joint programs.",""],[1,"193","8","National Program Development and Approval Process","This process would then lead to the development of a national pro- gram, which would be introduced both to the National Assembly and to donors as part of the national budget process.",""],[1,"193","9","Institutional Capacity Development and Coordination Framework","However, the functioning of these institutions needs to be improved and their capacity further developed.",""],[1,"194","10","Joint Planning and Evaluation for Donor-Supported Program Integration","The Government will concentrate on integrating and delivering donor-supported programs that achieve the ANDS goals of (i) stability, (ii) delivery of basic services and infrastructure and (iii) enabling a vibrant national economy.",""],[1,"194","11","Government Machinery Strengthening and Programmatic Capacity Approach","This integration will require a strengthening of government machinery both at the centre (OAA, NSC, Ministry of Finance, IARCSC and JCMB Secretariat) and at sub-national level (through the Ministry of Interior, MCN, IDLG and Ministry of Economy).","Ministry of Finance | Ministry of Interior | Ministry of Economy"],[1,"195","2","National Program Implementation through Budget and Private Sector Instruments","The ANDS sector strategies will be imple- mented through national programs which will generate results at the local level, as well as being synchronized with national and provin- cial budgeting and legislative and evaluation cycles.",""],[1,"195","2","Budget and Private Sector Implementation Instruments","The main instruments for the implemen- tation will be the Budget and private sector.",""],[1,"195","6","Institutional Strengthening and Capacity Building for ANDS Implementation","To sup- port this process, institutions will be strength- ened and capacity build within the central gov- ernment and at the sub-national level.",""],[1,"195","14","Alignment of National Programs and Projects with ANDS Sector Strategies","all line ministries and agencies will develop and align their national programs and projects with the ANDS Sector Strategies, which will then be costed and prioritized against the fiscal framework",""],[1,"197","1","Integrated Planning and Implementation Approach","The integrated approach to planning and implementation will ensure that priorities and potential synergies (across national programs as well as across the public/private sector divide) are identified at",""],[1,"202","3","Integrated Approach to ANDS Implementation","In the framework of such a strategy, the Integrated Approach in ANDS implementation aims to bring visible improvements to the lives of all Afghans.",""],[1,"213","4","Integrated National Development Framework","The primary goal of the ANDS is to establish a framework in which the Government and international community can work jointly to substantially reduce poverty based on a foundation of a private sector led sustained economic growth.",""]],"87":[[1,"184","6","Performance-Based Monitoring, Coordination, and Evaluation System","A performance/results-based approach: with improved monitoring , coordination and evaluation of development programs and projects by both the Government and the international community;",""],[1,"194","22","Poverty and Economic Growth Diagnostic Monitoring and Impact Evaluation","Enhance poverty and economic growth diagnostic monitoring and impact evalua- tion.",""],[1,"201","9","Ongoing Evaluation and Monitoring Framework","The implementation framework conceived in this strategy requires an ongoing evaluation and monitoring, and an enhanced risk man- agement mechanism, as there are continuing significant risks to stability which may yet un- dermine the underlying assumptions.",""],[1,"201","9","Enhanced Risk Management Mechanism","The implementation framework conceived in this strategy requires an ongoing evaluation and monitoring, and an enhanced risk man- agement mechanism, as there are continuing significant risks to stability which may yet un- dermine the underlying assumptions.",""],[1,"203","1","Central Monitoring and Reporting System","The Government has already begun establishing a Central Monitoring and Reporting System (CMRS) to fulfill both internal and PRSP reporting func-",""],[1,"203","2","Provincial and National Monitoring and Evaluation System","an effective monitoring and evaluation system will need to be established in both the provinces and by the Government in Kabul.",""],[1,"203","6","High-Level Strategic Monitoring of the Afghanistan Compact and MDGs","The JCMB Secretariat, as the body responsible for high-level co-ordination, together with the line ministries, will play a key role in high-level, strategic monitoring of the implementation of the Afghanistan Compact and the MDGs.","line ministries"],[1,"203","7","ANDS Monitoring and Oversight Framework","It will be important to distinguish between two levels of monitoring and oversight: (a) in- put/output or program monitoring of the im- plementation of the ANDS, and (b) out- come/impact monitoring for high level Gov- ernment institutions (OSC, Cabinet) and the JCMB to ensure that the strategic priorities of the ANDS are met.",""],[1,"203","8","Monitoring and Evaluation System Development","In developing a responsive, manageable and outcome oriented monitoring and evaluation system, the Government commits to:",""],[1,"203","9","Centralized and Provincial Monitoring and Reporting System","Establishing a centralized and eventually provincial based monitoring and reporting system;",""],[1,"203","11","Evidence-Based Policy Monitoring and Evaluation System","Adopting evidence-based systems for monitoring and evaluating policy and im- plementation;",""],[1,"204","2","Knowledge and Information Access Strengthening for the M&E System","Strengthening the management of knowl- edge and information access around the M&E system;",""],[1,"204","3","Strengthening Linkages Between the M&E System and Provincial Planning","Increasingly, over the course of the ANDS, seeking to strengthen linkages between the M&E system and the provincial planning process;",""],[1,"204","5","Core M&E Institutional Capacity Building","Building the core institutional capacities needed to sustain M&E processes, both within the CMRS, as well as the CSO, NRVA and line ministry systems;",""],[1,"204","8","Monitoring Institutional Structure","The institutional structure for monitoring will include a number of government, donor and non-government intuitions, however; the JCMB, line ministries and the CSO will play the most important roles.",""],[1,"204","9","ANDS Coordination and Monitoring by the OSC","The OSC will remain the key high-level government body coordinating and monitoring the implementation of the ANDS.",""],[1,"204","10","Joint Coordination and Monitoring Board","The JCMB is the strategic level coordination mechanism between the Government and the international community.",""],[1,"204","11","JCMB Secretariat Policy Analysis and Monitoring Support","The JCMB secretariat will provide policy and strategy analysis/assessment, monitoring and evaluation reports to JCMB on the overall implementation of ANDS and Afghanistan Compact Benchmarks as well as supporting the work of the standing committees.",""],[1,"204","11","Strengthening JCMB Secretariat Analytical Capacity","It will strengthen its capacity to provide independent analysis to enhance the high level oversight and problem solving role of the JCMB.",""],[1,"204","11","JCMB Secretariat Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of the JCMB Secretariat must be significantly strengthened to perform these tasks.",""],[1,"204","12","Central Monitoring and Reporting System Development","The CMRS will be developed within the JCMB Secretariat and Ministry of Economy as the central machinery of government to support the monitoring and reporting process.","JCMB Secretariat | Ministry of Economy"],[1,"204","12","National Monitoring Hub and Apex Monitoring Body","Along- side the CSO, it will provide the central hub for all national monitoring as an apex monitoring body, with a particular focus on monitoring and evaluating the impact of the Compact and the ANDS.","CSO"],[1,"204","12","Integrated National Monitoring Information System","It will not function in isolation but will bring together existing information from the CSO, consumer price indices, the NRVA, Afghanistan Financial Monitoring Information System, Afghanistan Country Stability Picture","CSO"],[1,"205","2","Conflict Monitoring and Reporting System","The CMRS will focus on data analysis and reporting of outputs, outcomes and impacts.",""],[1,"206","4","Annual ANDS Progress Reporting","The JCMB Secretariat will produce and the Government will approve annual progress reports on ANDS implementation, to serve as the basis for reporting.",""],[1,"206","4","Annual ANDS Reporting to International Financial Institutions","The Annual ANDS report will be presented to the Board of Directors of the WB and the IMF.",""],[1,"206","6","ANDS/PRSP Full Update and Impact Evaluation","Based on annual progress and evaluation reports every two years, a full update of the ANDS/PRSP, developed with broad participation will be constituted as an impact evaluation.",""],[1,"206","7","Poverty Situation Reporting and MDG Progress Reporting Mechanism","the JCMB Secretariat will be producing reports on poverty situation on three year basis to coincide with the completion of the NRVA surveys, which will continue to be most important instrument for collection of the poverty related data and produce annual MDG progress reports.",""],[1,"206","8","Public Expenditure Review and Sectoral Monitoring System","public expenditure reviews will be conducted and integrated into the ANDS monitoring process.",""],[1,"207","8","ANDS Monitoring and Evaluation System","In establishing an effective monitoring and evaluation systems for the ANDS, based on relevant national statistics (CSO/NRVA), the Government has already determined the fol- lowing: (i) goals, indicators and targets (ii) lev- els of data desegregation including by province and gender; (iii) appropriate targets, for exam- ple through the MDGs, Compact and ANDS sectoral levels; (iv) data requirements to meet the minimum standards of a PRSP; and (v) the frequency of data collection and monitoring.",""],[1,"207","9","Monitoring and Evaluation Indicator Framework","the Government has established a core set of monitoring and evaluation indicators for monitoring outcomes and impact for security, law and order and human rights, governance, social and economic development and poverty programs.",""],[1,"207","10","CMRS Data Requirements and Source Integration","Data requirements to feed into the input, out- put, outcome and impact assessment process are gradually being established.",""],[1,"207","12","Statistical Capacity Strengthening and Baseline Establishment","This is going to be an important priority for the first two years of implementation of the ANDS.",""],[1,"208","2","Sector Monitoring and Evaluation Frameworks","initial Sector Monitoring and Evaluation Frameworks have been prepared to identify needs with regard to existing and planned policies, and developing the programs/ projects and indicators.",""],[1,"208","3","ANDS Monitoring and Evaluation System","The ANDS monitoring and evaluation system being developed will track the progress of implementation of the ANDS towards the achievement of its objectives in poverty reduction and overall development in the country.",""]],"93":[[1,"36","6","Mineral Exploration and Market Delivery Programme","For mining and minerals, the emphasis is on the exploration, extraction and delivery to market; for hydrocarbons the emphasis is exploration and development.",""],[1,"36","6","Accelerated Mineral Resource Exploration and Development","The test will be in moving quickly from the success in attracting investment in the Aynak copper deposits to the development and exploration of the many other mineral resources of the country.",""]],"94":[[1,"39","4","Independent and Pluralistic Media Support","to ensure an independent and pluralistic media that contributes to an open and democratic so- ciety",""]],"95":[[1,"34","7","Religious Affairs Infrastructure Improvement","The Government will focus on the following priorities: (i) to improve infrastructure for reli- gious affairs, such as mosques, shrines, holy places, and religious schools;",""],[1,"34","7","Imam and Religious Educator Capacity Building","improve the training and capacity of Imams, preachers, reli- gious teachers and other scholars to raise pub- lic awareness and to teach;",""],[1,"34","7","Comprehensive Culture Curriculum Finalization","finalize a com- prehensive culture curriculum for primary and higher education;",""],[1,"34","7","Hajj Arrangement System Strengthening","strengthen Hajj arrange- ment systems for Afghan pilgrims;",""],[1,"34","7","Literacy, Dispute Resolution, and National Solidarity Support","support efforts of the other government agen- cies to improve literacy, dispute resolution and to contribute to strengthening of the national solidarity.",""],[1,"39","4","Cultural Heritage Documentation and Preservation Initiative","to document and pre- serve cultural artifacts and heritage sites",""]],"96":[[1,"25","4","Legal and Commercial Infrastructure Development for Market-Oriented Economy","The legal and commercial infrastructure is being put in place for a market oriented economy.",""],[1,"26","6","Comprehensive Economic Reform","The Government is pursuing comprehensive economic reform, including the introduction of new commercial laws and regulations, but the establishment of institutions needed for effective implementation and enforcement are largely lacking and will take years to develop.",""],[1,"35","5","Economy-Wide Review of Industry Protection Proposals","Any proposals to provide protec- tion to particular industries will be evaluated with a proper 'economy wide' perspective that fully accounts for the costs and benefits from such actions, including the negative impacts on other firms and on the consumers who must pay higher prices.",""]],"97":[[1,"40","5","Comprehensive Agriculture and Rural Development Strategy","plans for a series of programs that are designed to achieve an improved quality of life for rural citizens - one in which food security is assured, basic services are provided, incomes increase with households actively engaged in legal ac- tivities, employment opportunities expand and where people live in a safe and secure envi- ronment.",""],[1,"40","5","Agricultural and Rural Development Zone Initiative","Activities are grouped into two main components of the strategy: a Comprehensive Agriculture and Rural Development (CARD) and the Agricultural and Rural Development Zone (ARDZ) initiative.",""],[1,"40","6","Rural Poverty Reduction and Economic Regeneration Measures","Proposed interventions will provide a range of measures that will differ between groups and between regions, but all are de- signed to help diversify incomes, including income support, direct provision of assets, skills training and market opportunities.",""],[1,"63","8","Crop Diversification Support Programme","Programs to support crop diversification, targeted livestock, orchards, distribution and providing farming implements will contribute to poverty reduction among the rural poor.",""],[1,"63","8","Targeted Livestock Support Programme","Programs to support crop diversification, targeted livestock, orchards, distribution and providing farming implements will contribute to poverty reduction among the rural poor.",""],[1,"63","8","Orchard Development Support Programme","Programs to support crop diversification, targeted livestock, orchards, distribution and providing farming implements will contribute to poverty reduction among the rural poor.",""],[1,"63","8","Farm Input Distribution Programme","Programs to support crop diversification, targeted livestock, orchards, distribution and providing farming implements will contribute to poverty reduction among the rural poor.",""],[1,"63","8","Rural Employment Promotion Programme","As will improved access to rural all-weather roads, sanitation, electricity, job opportunities and promoting rural enterprises.",""],[1,"63","8","Rural Enterprise Promotion Programme","As will improved access to rural all-weather roads, sanitation, electricity, job opportunities and promoting rural enterprises.",""]],"98":[[1,"40","7","Agriculture and Rural Development Zones Program","The second main component of the strategy, the Agriculture and Rural Development Zones (ARDZ) program, is the Government's approach to expanding commercial activities and increasing agricultural productivity.",""],[1,"40","7","Public Land Release for Private Sector Investment","The Government will release publicly held land to increase private sector investment through a competitive bidding process.",""],[1,"40","7","Private Firm Financial and Technical Support Measures","the Government will continue to investigate and implement measures to increase financial and technical support that can be utilized by private firms to expand operations.",""],[1,"40","7","Commercial Agro-processing Enterprise Conversion Initiative","This will ensure the process of transforming underutilized state land into commercially viable agro-processing enterprises will be as fast and efficient as possible.",""]],"99":[[1,"43","2","Core Development Budget Implementation Capacity Enhancement","Efforts to increase capacity to implement the Core Development Budget more efficiently will result in higher donor contributions, aiding coordination.","MoF"],[1,"73","7","Budget Process Enhancement","Continuing to enhance the budget process and the role of the budget as the central instrument for policy and reforms;",""],[1,"74","8","Prudent Fiscal Policy and Budget Management","Prudent fiscal policy and effective budget planning and exe- cution will support sustained robust economic growth.",""],[1,"74","8","Sound Expenditure Management and Revenue Mobilization","the Government remains com- mitted to sound expenditure management and increased revenue mobilization, as well as en- suring fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"75","5","Public Finance Management Reform Package","The Government is taking measures to improve the overall absorption capacity and execution of projects in these sectors through more effec- tive public finance management and efficient project management methods.",""]],"100":[[1,"49","11","Provincial Priority Project Prioritization","Prioritization of the provincial priority projects, aligned with National Programs, forms the basis on which implementation of the ANDS will take place at the local level.",""],[1,"49","11","Provincial Budgeting Reform Pilot","Provincial budgeting, as a component of the National Program Budgeting Reform Progress, is also informed by the provincial prioritization process.",""],[1,"53","4","Integration of Provincial Planning and Budgeting into National Development Process","it is assumed that integration of the provincial planning, budgeting and implementation into the national development process will contribute to a relevant and accountable national development process.",""],[1,"91","13","Provincial Planning and Budgeting Institutionalization","Provincial planning and budgeting will be institutionalized.","Independent Directorate of Local Governance (IDLG)"]],"101":[[1,"61","8","Pro-Poor Growth Strategy","the Government will tackle poverty first and foremost through promoting strong equitable and broad based private sector led growth.",""],[1,"61","9","Pro-Poor Budgeting","Promoting pro-poor budgeting: the most important sectors impacting on poverty and poverty reduction, including security, education, health, and social protection, will see budget allocations maintained or increased over the medium term.",""],[1,"61","11","Balanced Support for Kuchis, Rural and Urban Poor","Future support to the Kuchis, rural and urban poor will need to be more balanced based on levels of poverty.",""],[1,"79","6","Expanded Social Sector Resource Allocation","In the coming years the Government will also devote progressively more resources on education, governance, health, and social protection.",""]],"102":[[1,"63","1","Labor Market Regulation and Pension Reform Improvement","Labor market regulation and the pension reforms will be improved to pro- vide protection from the employers, especially for workers engaged in the informal economy.",""]],"103":[[1,"63","6","Pro-Poor Urban Development Programs","the Ministry of Urban Development will include pro-poor urban development programs.","Ministry of Urban Development"]],"104":[[1,"63","8","Rural All-Weather Roads Improvement Programme","As will improved access to rural all-weather roads, sanitation, electricity, job opportunities and promoting rural enterprises.",""],[1,"63","8","Rural Sanitation Improvement Programme","As will improved access to rural all-weather roads, sanitation, electricity, job opportunities and promoting rural enterprises.",""],[1,"63","8","Rural Electrification Expansion Programme","As will improved access to rural all-weather roads, sanitation, electricity, job opportunities and promoting rural enterprises.",""]],"105":[[1,"64","1","Community-Based Crop Insurance Scheme","Further, the Government will initiate the establishment of community based crop insurance schemes to enable the poor to better mitigate the risks of losing harvest.",""]],"106":[[1,"64","7","Participatory Program Design for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","As the ANDS sector strategies are implemented, great effort is being made to use participatory and consultative processes to better understand the needs of the poorest and most vulnerable groups, to inform the design of appropriate programs to address those needs.",""],[1,"64","7","Special Programs for Women and Persons with Disabilities","Special programs are suggested to be put in place to target these groups so that they too share in the benefits from economic and social development programs.",""]],"107":[[1,"78","6","Security Sector Financing","security will remain the highest priority.",""]],"108":[[1,"73","20","Legal Framework Reform","Enacting an appropriate legal framework;",""],[1,"90","5","Legal Framework Reform for Investment and Trade","Laws have been enacted to promote investment and trade.",""],[1,"90","5","Legal Measures Against Illegal Drugs, Corruption, and Money Laundering","Measures to deal with illegal drugs, corruption and money laundering are under review and",""],[1,"90","6","Judicial Reform Legal Approval Package","As part of the judicial re- form program a number of other important laws will soon be approved.",""]],"109":[[1,"82","6","Disbandment of Illegal Armed Groups and DDR Continuation","The Disbandment of Illegal Armed Groups (DIAG) and the continuation of the Disarma- ment, Disintegration and Rehabilitation pro- gram (DDR), is the first step in disarming ille- gal armed groups.",""],[1,"82","6","Community Support for Removal of Arms Caches","The government -in coop- eration with international organizations - is trying to garner support from local communi- ties to get rid of these arms caches.",""],[1,"83","8","Disbandment of Illegal Armed Groups","All illegal armed groups will dis- banded by 20 March 2011 in all provinces.",""],[1,"83","9","Unexploded Ordnance Clearance and Ammunition Destruction Programme","Removing Unexploded Ordnance: By Jaddi 1389 (end-2010), in line with Afghanistan MDGs, the land area contaminated by mines and unexploded ordnance will be reduced by 70%; and by end-2010 all unsafe, unserviceable, and surplus ammunition will be destroyed.",""],[1,"84","15","Counter-Illegal Armed Groups and Terrorism Initiative","Fighting illegally armed groups and terror- ism, and help establish the rule of law;",""],[1,"85","12","DIAG Program for Arms Collection and Private Security Regulation","Implement the DIAG program: Collect un- registered arms in cooperation with other security departments and implement and enforce new regulations regarding private security companies.",""],[1,"88","11","DIAG and Mine/UXO Clearance Programme","Implement DIAG and mine/UXO clearance pro- grams to enhance security that would allow for extensive land to be taken back into use for farm- ing and devel- opment.",""]],"110":[[1,"88","3","Female Staffing and Gender Mainstreaming in the Security Sector","Increase the number of quali- fied female staff throughout the security sector.",""],[1,"88","3","Gender Balance Promotion Across the Security Sector","Promote gender mainstream- ing and gender-balance throughout the security sector.",""],[1,"88","15","Gender Equality in the Security Sector","Recognize in all policies and programs that men and women have equal rights and responsibilities through the security sector.",""],[1,"88","16","Public Complaints Mechanism","the Government will estab- lish and implement a pub- lic complaints mechanism.",""],[1,"88","17","Gender Equality Monitoring Mechanisms","Ensure that monitoring mechanisms are in place to realize goals for gender equal- ity.",""],[1,"88","17","Workplace Violence and Harassment Prevention Measures for Women","Ensure reduction of violence and harassment against women in the workplace, by implementing specific train- ing, units/ programs (e.g. re- ferral centers) and effective complaint and redress mecha- nisms.",""],[1,"88","21","Gender-Sensitive Security System Development","Special programs will be developed for developing gender sensitive security system internally as well for external interactions.",""]],"111":[[1,"89","5","Sustainable Election Administration Reform","The Government will also establish a fiscally and institutionally sustainable administration for future elections and prioritize the reform of the justice system to ensure equal, fair and trans- parent access to justice.",""],[1,"91","8","Independent Election Commission Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of the Independent Election Commission will be strengthened.","Independent Election Commission"],[1,"91","8","Permanent Voters' Registry Establishment","A permanent voters' registry will be established.",""],[1,"91","8","Regular National and Sub-national Elections","Regular national and sub-national elections will be held as mandated by the Constitution.",""]],"112":[[1,"93","8","Codes of Ethics and Oversight Mechanisms for Legal Professionals","Codes of Ethics and oversight mechanisms to be established for all legal professionals;",""],[1,"93","14","Systematic Justice Records System","sys- tematic records systems;",""],[1,"93","14","Anti-Corruption Measures in Justice Institutions","eradicating corruption;",""],[1,"93","14","Justice Sector Ethics Code Reform","promulgation of ethics codes,",""],[1,"93","14","Public Complaints System for Justice Services","engagement of public through complaints systems;",""]],"113":[[1,"93","14","Expansion of Justice Services Infrastructure","expansion of justice services through infra- structural development, procurement of transportation assets and equipment.",""],[1,"94","8","Justice Institutions Facilities Provision","Justice institutions, including the central prisons directorate, are provided with buildings necessary for fulfillment of their tasks.",""]],"114":[[1,"95","5","Religious Services and Public Awareness Strategy","The ANDS strategic objective for this sector is to provide competent and qualified religious services and increase the public awareness of Islamic religion and values in order to promote people's participation in the poverty reduction and development programs.",""],[1,"95","5","Religious Equality and Values Integration Policy","The Government's primary goal is to ensure that all Afghans have equal opportunities to exercise their Islamic and religious believes and that Islamic values will be embedded in the Afghan recovery and development.",""],[1,"95","5","Religious Affairs Policy Integration System","The religious affairs strategy intends to establish a system which ensures that religious values are reflected with every aspect to Government policy and contributes to the overall development of the country.",""],[1,"96","5","Hajj Services Improvement and Ministry Strengthening","Improved Hajj services and strengthening of Ministry of Hajj and Endowment;","Ministry of Hajj and Endowment"],[1,"96","24","Hajj Arrangement Systems Strengthening","Strengthen Hajj arrangement systems for pilgrims;",""],[1,"97","5","Administrative Reform Programme in the Ministry of Haj and Endowment","Implement administrative reform pro- grams in the Ministry of Haj and Endow- ment and its provincial offices;","Ministry of Haj and Endowment"],[1,"97","6","Hajj and Pilgrimage Services Reform","Reform the Hajj and pilgrimage services systems;",""],[1,"97","8","Religious Institutions Support Programme","Strengthen the support for building and maintaining mosques and other religious institutions;",""],[1,"97","10","Establishment of Ulama Councils for Local Dispute Settlement and Community Development Program Implementation","Establish Ulama Councils for settlement of local disputes and implementation of development programs in the community;",""]],"115":[[1,"95","6","Madrassa Development Programme","The Government will also develop religious schools (madrassas)",""],[1,"95","6","Imam and Religious Teacher Training Programme","will significantly strengthen the training of imams, preachers and religious teachers.",""],[1,"95","6","Islamic Teaching Training Opportunities","The Government will provide train- ing opportunities for Islamic teaching.",""],[1,"96","8","Inclusion of Islamic Subjects in the Curriculum","Inclusion of Islamic subjects in the new curriculum of primary, secondary and higher education systems;",""],[1,"96","9","Islamic Madrasas and Dar-Ul-Hefazs Establishment and Rehabilitation","Establishment and rehabilitation of the Is- lamic Madrasas and Dar-Ul-Hefazs;",""],[1,"96","10","Rehabilitation of the Department of Islamic Sciences","Rehabilitation of the Department of the Islamic Sciences of the Science Academy;",""],[1,"96","22","Religious Educator Training and Capacity-Building Programme","Improve the training and capacity of the Imams, preachers, religious teachers and other scholars to raise public awareness and to teach;",""],[1,"96","23","Cultural Curriculum Finalization","Finalize overall cultural curriculum for primary and higher education;",""],[1,"96","25","Religious Literacy Support Initiative","Support efforts of other government agen- cies to improve religious literacy.",""],[1,"96","29","Religious Education System Improvement","The religious education system will be im- proved;",""],[1,"97","4","Madrasa Education System and Teaching Methods Reform","Implement reforms in the education system and teaching methods in the public and private Madrasas;",""],[1,"97","7","Coordination Reform for Sharia Faculties","Reform and improve coordination of the Sharia faculties of Afghan Universities;",""]],"116":[[1,"95","6","Religious Infrastructure Improvement Programme","the Government will im- prove religious infrastructures including mosques, shrines and other holy places.",""],[1,"96","7","Restoration of Extorted Endowed Properties","Restoration of the endowed properties ex- torted by individuals;",""],[1,"96","21","Religious Affairs Infrastructure Improvement","Improve infrastructure for religious affairs: (mosques, shrines, holy places, religious schools);",""],[1,"97","9","Religious Institution Self-Sustainability Support","Improve self-sustainability of the religious institutions through building shops and business centers within the properties owned by mosques and other holy places and opening bank accounts for collecting donations;",""],[1,"97","12","Revenue Collection Mechanisms for Shrines and Holy Sites","Establish effective and transparent mecha- nisms for collecting revenues from shrines and holy sites.",""]],"117":[[1,"63","7","Zakat-Based Tax for Social Program Financing","The Government will con- sider introducing the Zakat-based tax to in- crease allocations for social programs to sup- port these programs.",""],[1,"95","8","Zakat Administration and Zakat-Based Tax Mechanism","With the establishment of the Zakat Administration within the government, as well as the possibility of a Zekat-based tax, donations can now be collected and redistributed in an organized manner among the most needy.",""],[1,"97","2","Strengthening Religious Institutions in Poverty Reduction Programs","Strengthening the role of the religious insti- tutions in programs for poverty reduction.",""],[1,"97","11","Establish Zakat Office within the Ministry of Hajj and Endowment","Establish Zakat related office within the ministry of Hajj and Endowment;","Ministry of Hajj and Endowment"]],"118":[[1,"89","2","Parliamentary and Legislative Process Strengthening","The main priorities for the governance sector are (iv) strengthen parliamentary and legislative processes including holding free and fair elections.",""],[1,"91","1","National Assembly Empowerment","National Assembly Empowerment: To enhance the capacity of the National Assembly in discharging legislative, oversight, transparency and accountability functions.",""]],"119":[[1,"98","9","Affirmative Action Legislation for Women's Seat Reservation","The Government will bring legislation on affirmative action providing a specific percent reservation of seats for women in the elected district, municipal and village councils as well as in the civil service.",""],[1,"98","9","Women's Education Reform Linkage to Political Participation","Affirmative action on allocating seats for women will be linked to education reforms for women.",""]],"120":[[1,"98","11","Environmental Information, Participation, and Justice Rights Framework","The right of everyone to receive environmental information that is held by public authorities (\"access to environmental information\"). 2. The right of both women and men to participate in environmental decision-making. (\"public participation in environmental decision-making\"); 3. The right to review procedures to challenge public decisions that have been made without respecting the two aforementioned rights or environmental law in general (\"access to environmental justice\").",""],[1,"98","11","Community-Based Natural Resource Management","Natural resources will be managed through community-based mechanisms and with the support of legitimate local governments.",""],[1,"98","11","Participatory Natural Resource Management Consultations","Natural Resource Management-related interventions will be based on broad consultations with local communities (that include marginalized groups like pastoralists or",""]],"121":[[1,"102","10","Supportive Financial Sector and Secured Transactions Reform","The growth of a supportive financial sector that is able to extend credit to viable firms will be supported through legal and regulatory reforms, including the implementation of secured transactions laws.",""],[1,"103","15","Private Sector Access to Finance Expansion Strategy","The Government will implement a well-defined strategy to expand the availability and range of financial products and services, especially targeting small and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"103","16","Financial Law Reform Package","Passage and enactment of four key financial laws: Secured Transactions, Mortgage, Leasing and Negotiable Instruments Laws.",""],[1,"103","17","Independent Banking and Business Training Institute","Establish an independent banking and business training institute as a joint commercial bank - DAB initiative.",""],[1,"103","18","Credit Information Bureau Establishment","A credit information bureau will be established to facilitate commercial and consumer lending.",""]],"122":[[1,"111","3","Agricultural Institutional and Regulatory Framework for Irrigation and Food Security","The necessary institutional, regulatory and incentive framework will be established for securing access to irrigation, water management systems and food security.",""],[1,"111","11","Water Infrastructure Feasibility Studies","Feasibility studies have been completed or are underway for small, medium and large water infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"111","11","Hydrological Station Rehabilitation and Modernization","The rehabilitation and modernization of hydrological stations have been started.",""],[1,"111","11","Safe Drinking Water Research and Modeling","Research and modeling of the availability of allocation of safe drinking water supplies in Kabul are being developed.",""],[1,"111","12","Kabul Groundwater Research and Assessment","Research and assessment of the underground water resources available to Kabul is on-going.",""],[1,"112","2","Irrigation Rehabilitation Programme","The Government will continue to work with the mirabs that manage these systems.",""],[1,"113","5","Project-by-Project Rehabilitation Investment Approach","Until the IWRM comes into effect, considerable reliance will have to be put on a project-by-project approach for continued investments in rehabilitation of existing systems.",""],[1,"113","5","New Project Appraisal Against Rehabilitation Returns","New projects need to be assessed relative to the returns from rehabilitation efforts and returns in other sectors",""],[1,"114","5","Emergency Irrigation Rehabilitation Program","Irrigation Rehabilitation Program: Several projects to address the immediate needs in irrigation infrastructure have been developed.",""],[1,"115","1","Emergency Water Infrastructure Rehabilitation","They consider short term emergency water infrastructure rehabilitation and income generation needs",""],[1,"115","1","Institutional Development and Multifunctional Infrastructure Creation","the long term goal of sustainable development of institutions and creation of new multifunctional infrastructure",""],[1,"119","3","Irrigation Infrastructure Expansion Program","The Irrigation Program will establish irrigation infrastructure on an additional 105,000 ha of new irrigated land by 2018 and improve on-farm water use efficiency.",""],[1,"121","2","Agricultural and Rural Irrigation Infrastructure Provision and Maintenance","Provision, and maintenance of Agricul- ture and Rural Infrastructure: Successful crop production requires: technical irriga- tion management (e.g., availability of irri- gation water supply, improving water effi- ciency and productivity, building effective and efficient irrigation and village based irrigation infrastructures, utilize modern ir- rigation technologies and human resource water management (e.g., organizing and strengthening mirabs, farmers associations, irrigation associations, decentralization of irrigation management at basin and sub- basin levels, water allocation. etc.).",""]],"123":[[1,"117","24","Comprehensive Agriculture Rural Development Program","Development of a comprehensive set of programs and projects - the Comprehen- sive Agriculture Rural Development pro- gram - designed to improve rural liveli- hoods and reduce rural poverty;",""],[1,"118","2","Comprehensive Agriculture and Rural Development Program","The Comprehensive Agriculture and Rural Development program (CARD) is a series of programs designed to support the poorest and most vulnerable seg- ments of rural society.",""],[1,"118","3","CARD Implementation with Private Sector Safeguards","In implementing the CARD, the Government will ensure that efforts to promote activity in the sector will stimulate and not displace spontaneous viable private sector development.",""],[1,"118","3","Gradual Devolution of Authority","The devolution of authority will be undertaken over a number of years to ensure the capacities at all levels of government exist.",""],[1,"118","3","Sub-national Governance Harmonization","The Government will work to reconcile the introduction of sub-national governance measures down to the village level with existing community organizations.",""],[1,"118","3","Clarification of Village Councils and Community Development Councils Roles","In particular, the role between proposed Village Councils and the existing Community Development Councils set up under the National Solidarity Program and which have been given legal status will be clarified.",""],[1,"118","3","Strengthening Sub-national Governance Structures","Strengthening sub-national governance structures in line with the newly-formed Independent Directorate for Local Governance will also be undertaken.",""],[1,"118","4","CARD Program Prioritization and Funding Framework","The Government will work with NGOs, civil society and the international community on the prioritization of the sub-components of the overall CARD program and to develop the funding requirements in some detail within a log frame matrix, identifying what will be done by when.",""],[1,"118","4","Ongoing Monitoring and Evaluation for CARD Programs","Ongoing monitoring and evaluation will be essential to address identified constraints and successes and alter the programs as necessary.",""],[1,"118","6","National Solidarity Programme","the Government's main community development program.",""],[1,"118","8","Local Governance Support in Villages","A key component of this program is the support to improve local governance in 38,000 villages.",""],[1,"118","9","National Area-Based Development Program","The National Area Based Development Program will support all District Develop- ment Assemblies to develop district level development plans which will support comprehensive rural development and re- generation.",""],[1,"119","10","Capacity Building Program","The Capacity Building Program will provide the institutional and organizational capacity at the national, provincial and dis-",""],[1,"123","10","Integrated Participatory Rural Development Approach","Use an integrated participatory regional development approach in rural areas, combining improved roads with agriculture, water, education, health, and counter-narcotics initiatives so that the poor derive the benefit from roads.",""]],"124":[[1,"118","8","National Food Security Program","The National Food Security Program will promote and implement food security opportunities at the household level, benefiting over 1.2 million households by 2010.",""],[1,"119","5","National Poverty, Vulnerability and Food Security Surveillance System","The National Surveillance System Project will assist MRRD and CSO in the development of a national poverty, vulnerability and food security surveillance system and enable the government to provide credible and timely information to all government and non-government agencies.","MRRD | CSO"],[1,"120","19","National Food Security Program","The National Food Security Program (NFSP) will increase household food security and nutritional status while contributing to national food security and economic growth in rural areas.",""]],"125":[[1,"116","2","Policy and Regulatory Framework for Rural MSMEs","creating the necessary policy and regula- tory framework to support the establish- ment of micro, small and medium-size ru- ral enterprises;",""],[1,"119","7","Rural Enterprise Development Program","The Rural Enterprise Program will provide training and finance to establish rural enterprises across 70 percent of all CDCs and create an estimated 2.1 million jobs, better integrate the rural economy with the national economy and reduce poppy cultivation.",""]],"126":[[1,"115","13","Refugee and Internally Displaced Persons Rehabilitation and Reintegration Support","assistance to and rehabilitation and integra- tion of refugees and internally displaced persons;",""],[1,"119","9","Emergency Response System","The Emergency Response System will provide a mechanism for humanitarian and disaster response that will provide emergency assistance, assure access to areas affected by snow and disasters and protect vulnerable people and assets.",""]],"127":[[1,"121","6","Regional Border Management and Transit Agreement Initiative","By end-2010 Afghanistan and its neighbors will achieve lower transit times through Afghanistan by means of cooperative border management and other multilateral or bilateral trade and transit agreements.",""],[1,"122","10","Transport Sector Inter-Ministerial Coordination Working Group","A Transport Sector Inter-Ministerial Working Group has been formed to coordinate the work of the ministries in the sector to as- sure that projects are properly designed to ob- tain the highest returns and greatest impact on",""],[1,"123","3","Transportation Services and Trade Facilitation Investment and Coordination","Improved transportation services, customs, and logistics management will require new investment and coordinated multilateral efforts, including work with the Economic Cooperation Trade Agreement (ECOTA), the Central Asian Region Economic Cooperation (CAREC), and the Shanghai Cooperation Organization.",""],[1,"123","5","Regional Transportation Investment Coordination Mechanism","Regional transportation investments will be coordinated by the Inter-ministerial Working Group for Transport to assure that investments are designed in such a way as to best serve the development goals of Afghanistan.",""]],"128":[[1,"123","1","Railway Program","The main programs of the strategy are (i) Regional, National Highways and Provincial Roads (ii) Rural Road (iii) Urban Transport (iv) Civil Aviation (v) Transport Sector Mainte- nance (vi) Pubic Transport (vii) Railway Pro- gram.",""],[1,"123","3","Railway Development Feasibility Studies","The Government will undertake feasibility studies to assess the economic viability of railway development within Afghanistan and links with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"123","8","Afghanistan Railway Project","The Government will pursue the Afghanistan Railway Project which will include 1,824 km rail links to connect Ka- bul, in the East with Islam Qala in the West through Kandahar and Hirat.",""],[1,"123","8","Railway Feasibility Studies for Neighboring Country Links","The Gov- ernment will also undertake feasibility studies to assess the economic viability of railway links with neighboring countries.",""]],"129":[[1,"126","5","ICT Sector Governance and Public Sector Capacity Study","A major study is currently being prepared that will provide guidance to the ICT Council, and the Government on improving governance and increasing public sector capacity for the industry.",""],[1,"126","7","ICT Law Drafting and Digital Regulatory Framework","drafting the ICT Law, which will address infra- structure and services, including issues such as legal recognition of electronic/digital signa- tures and formation of electronic contracts (af- fecting transactions both in public and private sectors), content regulation, competition regu- lation, electronic evidence, data privacy protec- tion, consumer protection and rights, domain name registration and regulation, intellectual property rights, encryption and security, finan- cial and banking sector law and regulation re- lating to electronic transfers and settlements, taxation of transfers, customs, jurisdiction, dis- pute resolution and civil and criminal offences, limitations of liability of internet service pro- viders, cyber piracy and digital rights man- agement, facilitation of e-government and cross border interoperability of e-commerce frame- works affecting trade.",""],[1,"126","8","ICT Legislation Development and Implementation","The sector priority policy is passage and im- plementation of ICT legislation that will create an appropriate environment for further devel- opment.","MoCIT"],[1,"127","1","ICT Legislation for E-Transactions and Cybercrime","MoCIT will submit draft ICT legislation governing e- transactions, electronic commerce, elec- tronic signatures and cyber crimes to the National Assembly.","MoCIT | National Assembly"],[1,"127","5","ICT Sector Tax Base Expansion and Regulatory Reform","By end-2010, the ICT sector will contribute five billion Afs ($100 million) annually to the treasury by broadening the tax base (at- tracting additional investors to the market, rather than over-burdening the existing ones).",""],[1,"127","5","Transparent ICT Legal and Regulatory Regime","ATRA will foster a transparent le- gal-regulatory regime that attracts a further",""],[1,"127","11","Afghan Telecom Privatization","Afghan Telecom is presently a corporation that is 100 percent owned by MoCIT however it is being privatized (an 80 percent share is to be sold), reflecting the Government's 2003 Tele- com and Internet Policy.","MoCIT"]],"130":[[1,"126","6","ICT Literacy Programme","The key programs of the ICT sector are (i) Ena- bling Environment (ii) Infrastructure Develop- ment (iii) E-Afghanistan (iv) ICT Literacy.",""],[1,"127","2","Unified Curriculum and Regulatory Framework for Private ICT Training Centers","A unified curriculum and regulatory framework for private ICT training centers will be drafted in cooperation with Ministry of Education.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"127","2","Provincial Capital IT Training Center Expansion","MoCIT will have established an IT Training center in all provincial capitals where security permits.","MoCIT"],[1,"127","4","ICT Village Establishment in Kabul","An ICT Village will be established in Kabul, this facility will attract foreign and local investments in ICT.",""],[1,"127","4","School Internet and Multimedia Access Expansion","Efforts will be made to ensure that all schools have access to internet and multimedia resources, together with a basic curriculum that includes browsing, searching and messaging.",""],[1,"127","12","Specialized Technical Training and ICT Bachelor's Programme","The Ministry's Information Communication Technology Institute (ICTI) provides specialized technical training and certification has launched a four year ICT bachelors program (the first class of 50 students have recently commenced studies).","The Ministry's Information Communication Technology Institute (ICTI)"]],"131":[[1,"105","2","Public Support for Private Education and Health Provision","It is reflected in innovative efforts to try and use public funding to support and improve private provision of education and health services.",""],[1,"128","1","Public-Private Partnership Curriculum Reform","the process of considering a transformation to public-private partnership in order to ensure that its curriculum meets the needs of the pri- vate sector (which has a huge demand for properly skilled workers).",""]],"132":[[1,"132","5","Solid Waste Management Improvement","Improve solid waste management through waste minimization (reduce, reuse, and recycle) and improved collection, transport and transfer, and disposal alternatives.",""]],"133":[[1,"132","7","Urban Development Monitoring and Information Systems","Key steps to improve and monitor progress with urban development will include the identification of indicators on which strategic, tactical, and operational decisions will be based; the establishment of GIS and databases to manage information; and the improvement of analytical routines and creation of the creation of web-based information systems.",""],[1,"132","7","Municipal Land Information and Registration Systems","The priority focus will be on the establishment of land information and registration systems in municipalities.",""]],"134":[[1,"134","4","Aynak Copper Mine Development Investment","The first major investment has recently been announced for developing the Aynak copper deposits in central Logar province, an almost $3 billion investment.",""],[1,"134","4","Aynak Mine Power Station Construction","The company will establish a power station with 400 mega watt capacity at a cost of over $400 million",""],[1,"134","4","Aynak Mine Workers' Town Construction","and will construct a town for the work-",""],[1,"135","3","Aynak Project Implementation","Planned actions include exploration and exploitation of mineral resources by the private sector or MoM; capacity building programs; successful implementation of the Aynak project; development of long term geo- science projects; and a reconstruction program including equipping the laboratory and techni- cal sections of the ministry.",""]],"135":[[1,"134","5","Hairatan-Torkham Railway Route Development","The company will also establish a railway route from Hairatan port in northern Afghanistan to Torkham in eastern Afghanistan.",""],[1,"134","5","Industrial Plant Development and Expansion","Ongoing and planned activities include the: (i) fertilizer and power plants at Balkh with capacity of 110,000 tons of urea each year, and 48 mega watt power per hour; (ii) Ghori cement factory with capacity of 100,000 tons per year; (iii) Jabal Seraj cement factory with maximum capacity of 30,000 tons per year; and (iv) Herat cement factory and Ghori 2 with capacity reaching 200,000 annu- ally.",""]],"136":[[1,"138","5","Comprehensive Hospital Referral Network and Service Standards","The MoPH will ensure the provision of a comprehensive referral network of secondary and tertiary hospitals that provide, as a minimum, the Essential Package of Hospital Services and do so within a framework of agreed upon, to set standards to improve clinical and managerial performance.","MoPH"],[1,"138","6","Central Drug Quality Control Laboratory","MoPH will also act to ensure the accessibility, availability, safety, efficiency, effectiveness and affordability of medicines, through several means, including establishment of a functional drug quality control laboratory at the central level.","MoPH"],[1,"138","6","Standard Medicines Procurement and Logistics System","Establish and use standard international level procurement, stocking and logistics systems to enable international contracting, bidding, stocking and transportation.",""],[1,"138","6","Affordable Health Communications Network","MoPH will also establish, maintain and further develop an affordable, useful and functioning communications network us-","MoPH"]],"137":[[1,"138","9","Environmental Health Awareness and Nutrition Security Programme","MoPH will also work to increase awareness and understanding of potential adverse health consequences of environmental factors, such as poor water supplies; lack of adequate sanitation facilities; inadequate rubbish disposal and collection; health facility waste; poor food handling and hygiene; and high levels of air pollution.","MoPH"],[1,"138","9","Integrated Malnutrition Reduction Programme","MoPH will also oversee programs to reduce malnutrition of all types, including reduction of micronutrient deficiency diseases, through integrated and coordinated programming and promotion of food and nutrition security for all by adopting a public nutrition approach involving multi-sectoral interventions that address the underlying causes of malnutrition, including food insecurity, poor social environment, and inadequate access to health care services.","MoPH"],[1,"138","10","Integrated Mental Health Support and Care Services","This program will also develop a flexible range of integrated mental health support and care services at all levels of the health system.",""],[1,"138","10","Post-Traumatic Counseling Workforce Expansion","Particular attention will be given to post-traumatic counseling through the training of more community health care workers and psychologists and their placement in accessible community health facilities;",""],[1,"139","1","Early Disability Detection and Specialized Health Services","temporary or permanent disabilities have access to both general health services and specialized services, and detect and treat disabilities early through more appropriate diagnosis of newborn and small children with disabilities.",""],[1,"139","2","Integrated Reproductive Health Service Delivery Package","High priority will be given to ensuring that development partners deliver the different components of reproductive health as an integrated package, and increase accessibility to, and utilization of, quality reproductive health care services, including antenatal care, intra-partum care, routine and emergency obstetric care and post partum care, counseling and modern family planning services.",""],[1,"139","2","Child Health and Development Improvement Measures","This will focus on reducing child mortality, morbidity and disabilities and improve child growth and development by promoting exclusive breast feeding, expanding implementation of integrated management of childhood illnesses, enhancing the control of vaccine preventable diseases and addressing adolescent health through school health programs.",""],[1,"140","5","Targeted Health and Nutrition Support for Vulnerable Groups","This strategy has been designed to specifically target the health and nutritional needs of the most vulnerable groups in Afghanistan.","MoPH"],[1,"155","11","Community-Based Rehabilitation Program for Drug Addicts","Develop programs for community-based rehabilitation of drug-addicts;",""]],"138":[[1,"145","8","Partnership Strengthening and Responsibility Clarification","Government will work towards strengthening partnerships, clarifying responsibility and",""],[1,"146","2","Education Financing and Administration Reform","A government-led education sector needs to be supported through building an accountable and transparent system of education financing and administration.",""],[1,"146","2","Education Management System Restructuring","The underpinning strategy that the government will employ to achieve its policy goals, therefore, is the reform and re- structuring of the management systems in place that facilitate the delivery of education services.",""],[1,"146","2","School-Level Devolution of Operating Authority","At the primary and secondary school level, a major policy shift seeks to devolve greater authority to the school level for minor operating expenses, planning and execution.",""],[1,"146","3","Public Administration Recruitment and Pay Reform for Teachers","Recruitment processes will be reviewed and be part of the overall public administration re- forms.",""],[1,"146","4","Five-Year Strategic Education Delivery Plan","A comprehensive five-year strategic plan for the delivery of education services has been developed by the Ministry of Education to meet the medium-term benchmarks for primary and secondary education set in the Afghanistan Compact by 2010.","Ministry of Education"]],"139":[[1,"148","5","Strengthening the Academy of Science","The Academy of Science will be strengthened and supported so as to use the resources and talents of the academy to assist with the restoration and development of Afghanistan society",""]],"140":[[1,"151","12","Disaster Preparedness and Response Coordination Strengthening","The capacity of ANDMA to coordinate disaster preparedness and response has improved as well.",""],[1,"153","5","Disaster Preparedness and Response System","By end-2010 an effective system of disaster preparedness will be in place; by end-2010 an effective system of disaster response will be in place.",""],[1,"153","10","Disaster Preparedness and Response Capacity Improvement","improve disaster preparedness and response capacity",""],[1,"156","11","Disaster Preparedness and Response Strategy","The main objectives of the sub-sector strategy for disaster preparedness will be to decrease risks from natural disasters and improve disaster preparedness and response with the aim of protecting human lives, assets, public infrastructure and the environment.",""],[1,"156","11","ANDMA Capacity Strengthening","(i) to strengthen the capacity of ANDMA, not only for coordination and policy making, but also for implementation of programs and projects;",""],[1,"156","11","Line Ministry Disaster Preparedness Capacity Building","(ii) to strengthen the capacity of line ministries for disaster preparedness and disaster response;",""],[1,"156","11","Provincial and Community Disaster Mechanisms","(iii) to enhance the provincial and community mechanisms for disaster preparedness and response;",""],[1,"156","11","Government Disaster Coordination Improvement","(iv) to improve coordination within the Government for disaster preparedness and response;",""],[1,"156","11","Humanitarian Aid Coordination Improvement","(v) to improve aid coordination in the area of delivering the humanitarian assistance, and (vi) to address long-term needs for rehabilitation.",""],[1,"157","1","Amend Disaster Management Legislation to Strengthen ANDMA Implementation Role","Therefore, the existing legislation will be amended to reflect the need to strengthen the ANDMA's role in implementing key projects.",""],[1,"157","2","National Disaster Preparedness Support Programme","Disaster preparedness will also be supported by the National Social Protection Sector Pro- gram and will include: (i) finalization of risk vulnerability assessments and disaster prepar- edness plans at the national and sub-national level; (ii) strengthening the capacity and the role of the ANDMA; (iii) establishing the emer- gency operation centers at the provincial level and regional warehouses; and (iv) moderniza- tion of equipment.",""],[1,"157","3","ANDMA Legislative Mandate Amendment","Amend the legislation to clearly reflect the leading role of the ANDMA in coordinat- ing the national efforts but also for imple- menting of key programs and projects;",""],[1,"157","4","Disaster Preparedness and Provincial Disaster Management Planning","Approve annual plans for disaster prepar- edness, finalize disaster risk analyses and guidelines for disaster response, and de- velop the provincial disaster management plans;",""],[1,"157","5","Standardized Emergency Response Procedures","Develop standardized operating proce- dures for quick assessment and response, reporting, and for rapid mobilization of in- ternational assistance;",""],[1,"157","6","Emergency Operations and Early Warning System Development","Establish Emergency Operation Centers at provincial level, response centers and teams at the regional level and effective early warning systems and develop the community emergency response system and develop back-up communication sys- tem based on Codan;",""],[1,"157","7","Regional Disaster Relief Storage Facilities and Public Awareness Campaign","Construct 12 regional storage facilities for aid assistance and equipment and improve public awareness activities and raise national awareness about disaster risks and vulnerabilities",""],[1,"157","8","ANDMA Capacity Strengthening and Coordination Improvement","Strengthening capacity and improving coordination: The ANDMA, and to a lesser",""],[1,"157","9","Disaster Preparedness Capacity Building and Equipment Modernization","the line ministries, require strong capacity building and equipment modernization.",""],[1,"157","9","Provincial Disaster Response Centers and Rescue Equipment","Having rescue equipment, management tools and operational centers at the provincial level will provide the necessary facilities to respond to disasters.",""],[1,"157","9","Community Disaster Preparedness through CDCs","Strengthening disaster preparedness and response at the community level through CDCs will be required.",""],[1,"157","9","Disaster Alarm Systems Deployment","Maintaining access to modern technology, such as with alarm systems, is important for reducing casualties and damages that occur during disasters.",""],[1,"157","9","ANDMA Disaster Preparedness Coordination Reform","the role of the ANDMA in leading and coordinat- ing the national efforts for disaster prepared- ness and response will need to be clearly de- fined and this will require adjustment of the current legislative framework.","ANDMA"]],"141":[[1,"153","1","Women’s Employment Quota in Public Administration","By end-2012/13 the Government will em- ploy 20 percent of women within its ad- ministration;",""],[1,"163","9","Female Participation Expansion in Transport Agencies","Government Trans- port agencies will increase female participation through additional training and new opportunities Greater consulta- tion with women.",""],[1,"163","9","National Action Plan for Women of Afghanistan Implementation","Also implement the National Action Plan for the Women of Afghanistan.",""],[1,"164","10","Mobile and Electronic Commerce Support for Women","Mobile and Elec- tronic commerce will make it possi- ble for women to work at home and be commercially viable without of- fending cultural sensitivities.",""],[1,"165","2","Enhancement of Female Professionals' Roles in Government","Roles and respon- sibilities of female professionals in government will be enhanced.",""]],"142":[[1,"155","3","International Agreements to Protect Migrant Workers","The Government will conclude international agreements with the neighboring and other countries to regulate the rights of the Afghanistan's migrant workers.",""],[1,"158","13","Cross-Border Movement and Economic Migration Management","strengthen the management of cross border movements and economic migration;",""],[1,"159","5","Implementation of Bilateral Temporary Labor Migration Agreements","make progress towards the implementation of the bilateral agreements on temporary labor migration;",""],[1,"159","9","Regional Labor Mobility and Remittance Facilitation Agreements","Afghanistan, its neighbors and countries in the region will reach agreements to enable Afghanistan to import skilled labor, and to enable Afghans to seek work in the region and send remittances home.",""],[1,"160","13","Tripartite Agreement and Tripartite Commission Implementation","The Government is committed to continue working with Iran, Pakistan and the UNHCR on the implementation of the Tripartite Agreement and the Tripartite Commission.",""],[1,"160","17","Cross-Border Movement and Economic Migration Management","· strengthen the management of cross border movements and economic migration; and",""],[1,"160","21","Neighbor Relations and Repatriation Solutions Initiative","The Government, with support from the inter- national community, will develop a range of political and practical solutions to work with and address the concerns of neighbors on the recent slowing of repatriation rates.",""],[1,"160","22","Retention of Tripartite Agreements for Refugee Return Coordination","The retention of the Tripartite Agreements is an important tool to ensure policy coordination and respect for refugee law and humanitarian principles.",""]],"143":[[1,"163","5","Energy Efficiency and Clean Cooking Transition","Emphasis on energy effi- ciency, renewable energy, and improved cooking fuels will have measur- able impact on improved environmental condi- tions;",""],[1,"163","7","Energy Sector Vocational Training Development","This strategy supports (1) the development of vocational train- ing for power and energy sector workers to become familiar with installation, health and safety and monitoring of op- erations;",""],[1,"163","7","Energy Sector Academic and Commercial Skills Training","improved university and other academic training to instill project finance, project management, legal skills and overall commercial capacity;",""],[1,"163","7","Regulatory and Oversight Capacity Building for Energy Officials","professional training for government offi- cials to implement important regulatory and oversight functions;",""],[1,"163","7","Energy Sector Commercial Management Skills Development","commercial skills to manage and operate the sector.",""]],"144":[[1,"166","1","Institutional Strengthening Programs Across Ministries","This issue has been addressed with institutional strengthening programs in all Ministries.",""],[1,"166","1","Improved Accounting and Procurement Support","There are also improved accounting procedures and support with procurement that will lower the probability of corruption.",""],[1,"166","7","Institutional Strengthening Program at the Ministry","There will be institutional strengthening program at the Ministry.",""],[1,"166","7","Internal Audit and Computing Department Establishment","As part of this, an internal audit department and a computing department will be established",""]],"145":[[1,"166","8","Gender Mainstreaming in State-Owned Media","Gender will be a core issue covered in all state owned media.",""],[1,"166","9","Anti-Drugs Media Messaging Initiative","The Ministry will work closely with the Ministry of Counter Narcotics and seek advice from them about the incorporation of an anti drugs message in all forms of media.","Ministry | Ministry of Counter Narcotics"],[1,"166","9","National Youth Program Drug-Free Society Promotion","The National Youth Program, through all its components will promote a drug-free society.",""]],"146":[[1,"166","10","Youth Environmental Engagement Program","Under the Youth Program, youth will be encouraged to become invoved in environmental pro- grams",""],[1,"179","2","Environmental Education and Awareness Programme","The strategy elaborates priority programs areas for environmental management based on thematic strategies in- cluding: environmental educa- tion and awareness.",""]],"147":[[1,"166","11","Regional Cooperation for Tourism, Culture, and Media Development","Tourism, culture and media can be further developed through an effective and fruitful cooperation with regional partners.",""]],"148":[[1,"167","13","Regional Food Security Reserve and Food Bank Operationalization","Afghanistan's membership in the South Asian Associa- tion for Regional Co- operation (SAARC) will operationalize a Regional Food Security Reserve and proposed Regional Food Bank",""]],"149":[[1,"168","6","Health and Nutrition Staff Capacity-Building Framework","The strategy provides a framework for increasing the capacity of staff in the sector to better deliver health and nutrition ser- vices.",""],[1,"168","8","Female Health Staff Deployment at Health Facilities","The MoPH has placed emphasis on having female health staff employed at every health facility.","MoPH"],[1,"168","15","Professional Standards Improvement in Key MoPH Entities","Raise professional standards in key MoPH entities",""]],"150":[[1,"168","7","Health Service Ombudsmen Unit Establishment","Establish Health Ser- vice Ombudsmen unit as a fully autonomous entity.",""],[1,"168","27","MoPH Transparency Working Group","Establish permanent MoPH transparency working group.","MoPH"]],"151":[[1,"168","11","HIV Prevention Programs","implementation of HIV prevention programs.",""],[1,"168","16","Women's Rights and Health Awareness Campaign","Increase awareness of gender and health and rights, raising women's",""]],"152":[[1,"168","26","Kabul Urban Development Implementation","Strategic actions include: implementing the Kabul",""],[1,"169","4","Public Works Greening Programme","to prepare and implement new public work pro- gram (Greening of",""],[1,"179","2","Urban Environmental Management Programme","The strategy elaborates priority programs areas for environmental management based on thematic strategies in- cluding: urban envi- ronmental management",""]],"153":[[1,"169","2","Benefits for Chronically Poor and At-Risk Women","to introduce benefits for chronically poor female headed households, victims of violence and other cate- gories of women \"at risk\"",""],[1,"169","2","Women's Inheritance Rights Legislation Reform","to improve legislation to ensure women's rights to inherit",""],[1,"169","15","Free Legal Aid for At-Risk Women","to introduce free legal ad- vise benefit for women \"at risk\" and improve women's access to justice",""]],"154":[[1,"169","2","Food for School Programme Expansion","to improve \"Food for Scholl\" programs to increase pri- mary school enrolment of girls",""]],"155":[[1,"170","2","Anti-Corruption Measures for Reintegration Program Components","In the design of reintegration program components such as land allocation, shelter and housing, attention will be paid to anti- corruption measures by providing full transparency on beneficiary selection processes.",""],[1,"170","7","Inter-Ministerial Cooperation Capacity Improvement","The capacity for Inter-ministerial cooperation will need to be im- proved.",""],[1,"170","7","Programme Preparation and Implementation Capacity Strengthening","Capacity for program preparation and implementation will also need to be improved, especially for im- mediate response to IDPs crisis.",""],[1,"170","7","Program and Project Implementation Unit","A program/project implementation unit (PIU) has been established within MORR to assist with the Land Allocation Scheme.",""]],"156":[[1,"170","3","Protection Measures for Returning Children, Women, and the Elderly","Special attention will be paid to protect children, women and the elderly during the return proc- ess.",""],[1,"170","4","Drug User Rehabilitation and Reintegration Programme","To improve re- habilitation and reintegration into society large number of drug users will be among the returnees.",""]],"157":[[1,"171","9","Trade Barrier Reduction and Market Liberalization","The removal of trade impediments and lower trade barriers will create a freer market and enhance the flow of goods, services, investment, and technology and support Afghan economic development.",""],[1,"172","8","WTO Accession and Regional Trade Agreement Expansion","In addition to the Government's ongoing efforts to accede to the World Trade Organization (WTO), it is also actively pursuing the expansion of bilateral and regional trade agreements with the countries of the region.",""]],"158":[[1,"171","11","Regional Border Management and Customs Cooperation","Improved border management and cus- toms cooperation at regional level increases security and helps to fight organized cross- border crime such as trafficking in arms and drugs.",""]],"159":[[1,"172","7","Intelligence Sharing and Counterterrorism Cooperation","the Government will seek better intelligence sharing and cooperation in counter terrorism measures.",""]],"160":[[1,"176","6","Gender Capacity Strengthening for Sector Professionals","Gender capacities of sector professionals will be strengthened and Gender Studies Institutes will be established in selected universities beginning with Kabul University.",""]],"161":[[1,"176","7","Strengthening the NGO Coordination Council","The NGO Coordination Coun- cil will be strengthened as a major link of gov- ernment to the NGO community in promoting gender equity.",""],[1,"176","7","Women-Focused NGO Participation Measures","NGOs will be encouraged to target women as project participants and bene- ficiaries and to increase the participation of women in the management of their organiza- tions.",""],[1,"176","7","National Advocacy and Public Communication Strategy on Gender Equality","An advocacy and public communication strategy that will transform negative percep- tions and attitudes toward women will be im- plemented nationwide, with particular atten- tion to women, men, media, religious leaders, and institutions and influential decision makers in society.",""],[1,"176","7","Culturally Sensitive Mass Communication for Remote and Tribal Communities","Non-traditional, culturally-sensitive forms of mass communication will be explored for remote and tribal communities to address cultural obstacles to women's education, lead- ership and participation in public life, repro- ductive rights, property ownership and inheri- tance.",""]],"162":[[1,"177","1","Gender Equity Monitoring Scorecard","The Government will also adopt a monitoring scorecard that ministries will use to track their own performance on gender equity.",""],[1,"177","1","Sex-Disaggregated Data and Gender-Sensitive Reporting Requirement","All sectors will be required to collect and use sex disaggregated data, adopt gender sensitive indicators, and include gender related performance in their regular reports.",""],[1,"177","1","Gender Performance Oversight and Evaluation System","Performance of sectors on gender will be monitored by the Oversight Committee and the JCMB.",""],[1,"177","1","MoWA Gender Indicators and Statistical Framework Enhancement","The gender indicators and statistical framework of MoWA will be elaborated to contain indicators on the performance of government on the promotion of women's status.","MoWA"],[1,"177","2","Gender Mainstreaming in Monitoring and Evaluation Unit","Include gender in the terms of reference of the monitoring and evaluation unit and job description of its chiefs;",""],[1,"177","3","Gender-Sensitive Monitoring and Reporting Training","Provide training on gender sensitive moni- toring and reporting;",""],[1,"177","5","Sex-Disaggregated Data Collection and Processing","Collect and process sex disaggregated data; and,",""],[1,"177","6","Gender Achievement Reporting and Baseline Survey Monitoring","Highlight gender achievements in ministry and sector reports.",""],[1,"177","7","Annual Gender Statistics Update and Dissemination","The baseline statistics on women and men in Afghanistan will be updated annually and dis- seminated to strategic users, and NRVA data collection process will be further strengthened to support greater gender desegregation.",""],[1,"177","7","Periodic Evaluation and Strategy Adjustment","Evaluation will be undertaken periodically to take stock of achievements, correct gaps and adjust strategies as necessary.",""],[1,"177","7","Mid-Term and Final Evaluation of the Plan","A mid-term evaluation will be conducted in 2008 and an- other on 2011.",""],[1,"177","7","Evaluation-Informed Future Planning for the National Action Plan for the Women of Afghanistan","Insights from the evaluation will be used to inform future planning, including the updating of the National Action Plan for the Women of Afghanistan.",""]],"163":[[1,"184","3","Support for Donor-Led Economic Reform Programs and Projects","The Government will continue to provide strong political backing for economic reforms through support to the conditions attached to programs and projects undertaken by donors.",""],[1,"184","3","Capacity-Building and Knowledge Transfer in Program and Project Design","The Government encourages program and project designs that focus on creating and transmitting knowledge and building capacity.",""],[1,"184","3","Post-Evaluation of Development Projects","Over the ANDS period, post evaluation of all development projects will be undertaken which will provide valuable information on the lessons learned and improve the future design of development programs and projects.",""],[1,"206","4","Ad Hoc Impact Evaluation Reporting","the JCMB Secretariat will provide ad hoc, periodic impact evaluation reports to the Government, the public and international partners.",""]],"164":[[1,"184","5","Macroeconomic Framework Reform","continue to improve its overall macroeco- nomic framework by identifying and re- moving structural rigidities and market distortions to permit higher levels of eco- nomic growth.",""],[1,"188","3","Resource Mobilization and Fiscal Sustainability Reforms","the Government needs to mobilize significant additional resources.",""],[1,"188","3","Domestic Revenue Mobilization Reforms","the Government will implement reforms that will lead to higher mobilization of domestic revenues in order to ensure fiscal sustainability in the long run and decrease aid dependence.",""],[1,"198","2","Aggregate Fiscal Discipline Strengthening","Government will aim to (i) increase the revenue to GDP ratio; (ii) reduce the ratio of operating expenditures to revenues, and (iii) make progress according to fiscal tar- gets established through the MTFF.",""],[1,"199","1","Medium-Term Fiscal Framework Continuation","The three year Medium Term Fiscal Frame- work (MTFF) will continue to provide the re- source framework.",""],[1,"199","5","Medium-Term Fiscal Framework and Sector-Wide Programming","The Medium Term Fiscal Framework and sec- tor wide programming and costing will (i) strengthen realistic resource projections; (ii) sectoral prioritization; (iii) support fiscal sus- tainability, and (iv) develop budget ceilings for all budget entities.",""],[1,"199","6","Government Expenditure Prioritization Framework","The Government expenditure prioritization frame- work will ensure that proper resource alloca- tion will be made to support implementation of these commitments and if necessary appro- priate adjustments will be done.",""]],"165":[[1,"185","7","Merit-Based Civil Service Reform","Major public administration reforms being implemented or planned -such as the introduction of a merit-based civil service system, and professional management of government min- istries and departments, or the creation of a more formalized budget, procurement, and audit processes and agencies-had their roots in the desire of the Government to avoid earlier abuses of graft and political patronage.",""],[1,"185","7","Formalized Budget, Procurement, and Audit Processes","Major public administration reforms being im- plemented or planned -such as the introduction of a merit-based civil service system, and professional management of government min- istries and departments, or the creation of a more formalized budget, procurement, and audit processes and agencies-had their roots in the desire of the Government to avoid earlier abuses of graft and political patronage.",""],[1,"185","7","Public Expenditure Financial Accountability Framework Development","Equally important will be the Government's accountability to the Afghan people with re- gard to the expenditure of aid money, which will be supported by the ongoing efforts of the MoF to develop the Public Expenditure Finan- cial Accountability (PEFA) framework.","MoF"],[1,"186","2","Public Finance Management, Procurement, and Auditing and Accounting Law Enforcement","The Government has also passed the Public Finance Management, Procurement, and Auditing and Accounting Laws and will ensure that these laws and regulations are implemented and enforced diligently.",""],[1,"199","3","Strengthening of the Control and Audit Office Oversight Role","The role of the Control and Audit Office (CAO) will be strengthened to provide oversight of the","Control and Audit Office (CAO)"]],"166":[[1,"185","8","Budget Process Transparency and Citizen Engagement Strengthening","This process will be strengthened by: (i) deep- ening the linkages between the ANDS, MTFF, MTB and in the future with the MTEF; (ii) en- hancing the 'budget literacy' of citizens and civil society organizations through engagement in budget processes; (iii) support to civil society organizations and downward accountability in the context of decentralized service delivery; (v) regular reporting to National As- sembly and other public entities in how budg- etary resources (core and external) are being spent; (vi) better communication with the pub- lic using the ANDS framework on plans, aid received, disbursed, outcomes and impact and (vi) supporting civil society organizations and non-governmental organizations to ensure that local governments are held accountable on how aid money is being spent to improve the peo- ple's welfare.",""]],"167":[[1,"186","7","Integration of Pooled Donor Funds into National Planning and Accountability Systems","Funds channeled through the Core Budget, by means of pooled funding modalities, including the Afghanistan Reconstruction Trust Fund (ARTF), Law and Order Trust Fund for Afghanistan (LOTFA) and Counter Narcotics Trust Fund (CNFT) will be fully integrated into national planning and resource accountability systems across the different layers of Government.",""],[1,"186","9","Reporting Requirement for Parallel-Funded Activities","the Government will require that information on all activities financed under parallel funding mechanisms is communicated to the MoF in a timely manner.","MoF"],[1,"186","9","Alignment of Parallel-Funded Projects with Sector Strategies","Donors who are implementing parallel funds are encouraged to show flexibility in aligning their projects with sector strategies of ANDS and having definite time-lines for eventually bringing such assistance on-budget.",""],[1,"187","1","Promotion of Untied Aid and Local Procurement","The Government would like to encourage donors to use more locally produced goods as well as local implementing agencies so as to promote greater private sector development and employment.",""],[1,"189","2","Core Budget Support Mechanism","The Government prefers core budget support (direct budget support).",""],[1,"189","3","Shift Donor-Funded Program and Project Financing to the Core Budget","it will seek to the transfer of more funds to the Core Budget.",""],[1,"189","4","Aid Channeling Through Established Trust Funds","Channeling aid through already established trust funds (ARTF, LOFTA, CNTF) would be the second preferred option as this would mean that the Government would be able to access these funds on an as-needed basis.",""],[1,"189","4","Pooled Donor Funding Mechanism","Finally, the Government prefers that donor funds be pooled rather than ear- marked for individual projects.",""],[1,"189","5","Government-Led Aid Project Approval Framework","The Government will not support provision of assistance in the form of donor preferred and designed projects based on needs assessment done solely by donors with little or no consul- tation with the Government.",""],[1,"195","3","Core Budget Support for National Program Implementation","The medium term budget expenditures of the Core Budget will support implementation of the national programs that will be aligned with the ANDS priorities.",""],[1,"195","3","Donor Implementation of External and PRT Budget Programs","Based on the Paris Declaration, the donors will be asked to implement programs and projects from the External and the PRT's budgets in line with the ANDS.",""],[1,"195","3","JCMB Coordination Mechanism","The existing JCMB coordination mechanism will be used to ensure this.",""],[1,"197","1","Aligned Funding for National Programs","By committing themselves to funding national programs according to ANDS priorities, international community will ensure that their assistance is leveraged to bring stability to the government planning cycle.",""]],"168":[[1,"189","7","Supportive Civil Society Organization Engagement Policy","The Government will ensure that it adopts a supportive approach vis-à-vis the work of the CSOs.",""],[1,"189","7","Civil Society Alignment and Compliance Framework","The Government however, will encourage the CSOs to align their assistance with ANDS priorities and conduct their business according to the NGO Law and other relevant legislation covering CSOs.",""],[1,"189","8","Harmonized NGO and CSO Reporting Mechanism","The NGOs and the CSOs will be required to improve their reporting systems and provide accurate and timely information on their development activities through the Harmonized Reporting Form.",""],[1,"189","8","Simplified NGO and CSO Reporting Reform","However, the Government remains committed to improving the reporting mechanism by introducing more simplicity and increasing compliance as well as removing unnecessary barriers to their effective operation.",""]],"169":[[1,"189","9","PRT Support for Priority Project Implementation through Provincial Development Plans","the Government would encourage the PRTs to assist in the implementation of priority projects through the Provincial Development Plans (PDPs) in line with national priorities (ANDS).",""],[1,"189","9","Harmonized Reporting Form for PRT Activity Reporting","all PRTs will need to report their activities to the Government through the Harmonized Reporting Form.",""]],"170":[[1,"193","9","Integrated Conflict Management in Sector Strategies","This chapter out- lines: (i) lessons learned; (ii) the principles of an integrated approach; (iii) budget management; (iv) the necessary institutional framework ar- rangements; (iv) the coordination framework; and (v) integrating Conflict Management into Sector Strategies.",""],[1,"194","7","Conflict Sensitivity Mainstreaming System","It is essential that a system be put in place to ensure that conflict sensitivity is mainstreamed into all development programs.",""],[1,"194","14","Kabul-Province Linkage Strengthening and Conflict Resolution Support","Strengthen links between Kabul and the provinces and support the resolution of conflicts;",""],[1,"201","5","Conflict Evaluation Mechanism","The conflict evaluation mechanism will be established within the existing monitoring structures",""],[1,"201","7","Conflict-Sensitive Development Assistance Mainstreaming","The Central Monitoring and Reporting System (CMRS)62 will conduct specific assessment and analysis which will subsequently mainstream and integrate conflict awareness and sensitivity into all areas of development assistance (based on criteria to be developed in cooperation with the donors) to ensure that development pro- grams will not erode stability or increase con- flict.",""],[1,"201","7","Peace-Promoting Reconstruction and Development Assistance","Finally, conflict awareness and peace- promoting initiatives will be incorporated into reconstruction and development assistance and special attention will be paid to ensure that de- velopment programs do not upset cultural val- ues or beliefs.",""]],"171":[[1,"194","13","Medium-Term Budget Framework Enhancement","Enhance the Medium Term Budget Framework, maintain fiscal sustainability, adopt sector-wide approaches and build upon Provincial Development Planning;",""],[1,"194","13","Sector-Wide Planning Approach","Enhance the Medium Term Budget Framework, maintain fiscal sustainability, adopt sector-wide approaches and build upon Provincial Development Planning;",""],[1,"194","13","Provincial Development Planning Strengthening","Enhance the Medium Term Budget Framework, maintain fiscal sustainability, adopt sector-wide approaches and build upon Provincial Development Planning;",""],[1,"196","1","Public Investment Program Preparation","the Public Investment Program (PIP) will be prepared to enable (i) full integration of the ANDS into the Medium-Term Fiscal Framework and the Budget; and (ii) presentation to the National Assembly.",""],[1,"196","4","ANDS Review and Update","Based on the progress and evaluation reports the ANDS Review/Update will be completed by mid-1389 (September 2010).",""],[1,"196","12","Integration of ANDS and PIP into the Budget","Integrate the ANDS and the PIP into Budget",""],[1,"196","14","National Budget Implementation Mechanism","The Budget is the funding mechanism through which ANDS policy will be implemented.",""],[1,"196","15","Budget as a National Policy-Making Instrument","Strengthening the role of the Budget as the in- strument of national policy making is critical to the implementation of the ANDS.",""],[1,"196","17","Core Budget Self-Sufficiency and Budget Integration Reform","The Government is committed to getting to the stage where the total Budget is Core, and is funded from nationally generated revenues, but acknowledges that it will take some time to accom- plish this goal.",""],[1,"197","15","Programmatic Budgeting Reform","The Government's current approach is based on programmatic budgeting.",""],[1,"197","16","On-Budget Resource Control Reform","Control of on-budget resources is being strengthened through fundamental reforms of",""],[1,"198","3","Expansion of Program Budgeting Across All Ministries","Currently, the Ministry of Finance uses program budgeting in key sectors and ministries. This activity will expand to include all ministries, which will significantly support the integrated approach.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"198","3","Alignment Review of Budgetary Proposals with ANDS Policies","Budgetary proposals will be examined on the basis of their alignment to the ANDS policies.",""],[1,"198","10","Integration of Trust Funds into the Budgetary Process","Efforts will continue to incorporate the Afghan Reconstruction Trust Fund (ARTF), Law and Order Trust Fund (LOTFA) and the Counter Narcotics Trust Fund (CNTF) into the budgetary process.",""],[1,"198","11","Integrated Budgeting and Policy-Making Reform","Integrate budgetary processes with cabinet- level policy-making and legislative planning: The linkages among policy-making, planning and budgeting will be strengthened to promote more results-based performance management.",""],[1,"198","12","Poverty-Related Spending Tracking System","Evalu- ating the effects of public spending on poverty reduction will be enhanced by introducing the system of tracking of poverty related spending within the framework of the future monitoring mechanism.",""],[1,"199","2","Medium-Term Expenditure Framework Development","Based on this the MoF plans to embark on the process of developing the Medium-Term Ex- penditure Framework (MTEF) to strengthen the Governments capacity for expenditure planning.","MoF"],[1,"200","8","Programme and Project Costing and Budget Integration Mechanism","MoF will be responsible to ensure that the pro- grams and projects of the line ministries will be costed, prioritized against the fiscal framework, sequenced and integrated into the MTFF and the Budget.","MoF | line ministries"],[1,"205","8","Medium-Term Budget Framework for Sectoral Priorities","The close day-to-day working relationship between the MoF (AFMIS), the various budget entities, the CMRS and CSO will provide vital information in setting and costing sectoral priorities and targets to be funded through the medium term budget framework.","MoF (AFMIS) | CMRS | CSO"],[1,"205","8","Annual Sectoral Target Reporting and Budget Hearings","Annual targets will be reported against the agreed sectoral baselines and the budget hearing sessions will increasingly move",""],[1,"208","1","Budget Alignment with Indicators and Costing Priorities","the JCMB Secretariat will ensure that the budgets will be aligned with the indicators and costing priorities.",""],[1,"214","6","Priority Public Investment in Infrastructure and Social Sectors","penditure programs for investments in energy, water and irrigation, transportation infrastruc- ture, agriculture, agro-based industry, and ru- ral development will remain high priorities",""]],"172":[[1,"215","3","Public Infrastructure Investment and PPP Support","The Government intends to under- take public investment in infrastructure in ways that complement private investment in these areas or using public-private partnership arrangements whenever feasible.",""],[1,"215","3","Essential Infrastructure Investment Programme","With donor assistance, considerable investment in essential infrastructure is currently being undertaken, particularly in roads, power, commercial agri- culture, healthcare, and education and voca- tional skills.",""]],"173":[[1,"219","3","Security Coordination Centers Establishment","Monitor and coordinate security issues between ministries and departments and establish 13 coordination centers",""]],"174":[[1,"193","1","Equal Access to Basic Services Expansion","It will require equal access to the delivery of basic services, in particular education, road infrastructure and health throughout the country.",""]],"175":[[1,"220","3","Fire Brigade Department Establishment and Equipment","Establish/Equip Fire Brigade Departments",""]],"176":[[1,"220","4","Traffic Signal Infrastructure Restoration","Restore Traffic signals structure in Urban areas and highways",""],[1,"242","10","Road Safety Capacity Building Program","Institute a substantial capacity building program, including a road safety pro- gram.",""],[1,"242","11","Traffic Management Bureau Decentralization","Develop the Traffic Management Bureau form the MoI to the Provinces and Municipalities through the new Independent Directorate of Local Governance","MoI | Independent Directorate of Local Governance"]],"177":[[1,"219","17","Conflict Prevention Programs in High-Risk Areas","Focus on conflict prevention programs in areas where anti government activities are ripe",""],[1,"220","20","Ammunition Destruction Programme","All unsafe unserviceable and surplus ammunition will be destroyed",""],[1,"220","21","DIAG Plan Implementation","DIAG plans need to be instated and properly implemented",""],[1,"220","24","Coordinated Poppy Eradication Campaign","Coordinate and target poppy eradication, in particluar where the beneficiaries are supporting anti government activities",""],[1,"220","25","Afghan Security Forces Capacity-Building for Drug Law Enforcement","Conduct training to increase the capacity of Afghan Security forces to enforce the law against poppy cultivation and drug trafficking",""],[1,"221","2","Cross-Border Intelligence Sharing on Drug Smuggling","Cooperate and coordinate with neighboring countries with intelligence sharing, particular with regard to drug smuggling across borders.",""],[1,"221","3","Anti-Poppy and Drug Trafficking Information Campaigns","Conduct effective information campaigns against poppy production and drug trad- ing.",""],[1,"243","18","Checks and Balances for Illicit Trafficking Control","Introduce and checks and balances for illicit transpiration of human and com- modities like precursors, drugs, etc.",""]],"178":[[1,"222","31","Disaster Preparedness and Response System","Establish an effective system of disaster preparedness and response",""],[1,"242","2","Sector Vulnerability and Mitigation Planning","Conducting VCA and developing mitigation plans in the sector;",""],[1,"246","4","Hydrological Station Rehabilitation and Expansion","Rehabilitation and establishment of new Hydrological Stations for collection of the necessary information and figures",""],[1,"246","18","Environmental Safeguards Measures","Introduction of measures to ensure environmental concerns taken care of.",""],[1,"247","6","Hydrometric Network Institutional Establishment","Establishment of institutions for hydrometric network in the country",""],[1,"248","11","National Hydro-meteorological Network Rehabilitation","Rehabilitation of National Hydro-meteorological network",""],[1,"248","15","Riverbank Protection and Erosion Control Works","Undertake riverbank protection and erosion control works and implement long-term flood control program",""],[1,"248","15","Long-Term Flood Control Program","Undertake riverbank protection and erosion control works and implement long-term flood control program",""]],"179":[[1,"226","11","Taqnin Needs Assessment and Capacity-Building Recommendations","Perform comprehensive needs assessment of Taqnin and make recommendations for technical assistance and capac- ity building",""],[1,"226","12","Taqnin Technical Assistance and Capacity Building","Provide technical assistance and capacity building for Taqnin in line with recommendations.",""],[1,"226","13","Legislative Drafting Cooperation and Efficiency Working Body","Establish a working body to promote greater cooperation and enhance the efficiency of the legislative drafting proc- ess.",""],[1,"226","15","Constitutionality Review of Laws","Taqnin conducts a review of the constitutionality of all laws in force, and recommends amendments to ensure constitu- tionality.",""],[1,"226","16","Unconstitutional Law Amendment Reform","Unconstitutional laws are amended to ensure constitutional- ity",""],[1,"227","2","Legislative Drafting Capacity Enhancement in Justice Institutions","Implement recommendations for enhancing legislative drafting capacity in justice institutions.",""],[1,"227","3","Taqnin Working Group for Civil Society Inclusion in Legislative Deliberations","Establish a Taqnin working group to make recommenda- tions for inclusion of civil society stakeholders in legislative deliberations.",""],[1,"231","12","National Assembly Capacity Building for Legislative Support","Invest in capacity building for National Assembly so that MPs are better in- formed and supported in their role and understanding of the rationale, use and content of proposed laws.",""],[1,"232","2","Legal Publication and Gazette Notification Requirement","Establish the principle that no law can be implemented unless it has been ga- zetted, published in the newspapers, and made available electronically and in hard copies at no cost.",""],[1,"232","2","Interim Online Law Publication via ANDS Website","Explore the option of using the Afghanistan National Development Strategy (ANDS) website as an interim solution for publishing laws after their enactment.",""],[1,"232","2","Online Publication of Tariff Structures","Publish the tariff structures on the Ministry of Fi- nance website.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"249","10","Government Document Publication Rules and Regulations","Develop rules and regulations to require all government institutions to publish documents on their official websites (as a supplement to the Official Gazette)",""]],"180":[[1,"225","7","Sexual Harassment and Grievance Handling Law and Policy Enactment","Public demands Sexual Harassment and grievance handling laws/policy to be enacted",""],[1,"229","12","Institutional Response to Stop Violence Against Women","strengthened institutional response to stop violence against women",""],[1,"229","16","Sexual Harassment and Grievance Handling Law and Policy Enactment","Public demands Sexual Harassment and grievance handling laws/policy to be enacted",""],[1,"229","19","Juvenile Justice Legal Framework Reform","Strengthen the legal framework so as to improve responsiveness to the needs of juvenile offenders and children in conflict with the law",""],[1,"229","20","Legal and Institutional Framework for Children Accompanying Incarcerated Parents","Strengthen the legal and institutional framework for children accompanying their parents in prison.",""],[1,"230","3","Family Response Units","Family Response Units, staffed by all female police offi- cers, are functional in all provinces, and are effectively linked with Special Victims Units in the AGO.",""],[1,"230","8","Procedural Code Amendment for Witness Protection","Procedural code is amended to address specific needs of witnesses, including women and other vulnerable groups",""]],"181":[[1,"225","4","Judges Safety Security Measures","Implement security measure for Judges safety",""],[1,"229","21","Sentencing and Prison Conditions Reform","Develop and implement policy recommendations for im- proving sentencing, detention, and conditions of prisoners.",""],[1,"230","2","Justice Institutions Rights Protection Practices","Promote practices within the justice institutions that are supportive of the rights of victims, witnesses, the accused, and those convicted of crimes",""],[1,"230","4","Corrections Officials Training Programme","Develop and implement training programs for corrections officials incorporating recommendations based on analysis.",""],[1,"230","9","Human Rights Abuses Recording and Victim Rights Preservation System","Establish a system to record past human rights abuses and to preserve the rights of victims",""],[1,"230","16","Justice Sector Codes of Ethics Development and Dissemination","Develop, finalize and disseminate codes of ethics for professionals in justice institutions.",""],[1,"230","18","Justice Professionals Ethics Code Training","Train justice professionals on ethics code.",""],[1,"231","2","Ethics Code Advisory and Enforcement Units","Design and establish dedicated and effective institutional units and procedures to advice on and enforce codes of ethics.",""],[1,"231","3","Independent Bar Association for Attorney Standards","Improve the professional and ethic standards of attorneys at law through an Independent Bar Association.",""],[1,"231","7","Justice Sector Anti-Corruption Operations Implementation","Implement the activities related to operations of the justice sector contained in the National Anti Corruption Strategy.",""]],"182":[[1,"234","26","Civil Society Legal Framework Revision","Revise, clarify and update the legal framework governing civil society organizations, including the NGO Law and Social Organizations Law, to cover civil",""],[1,"235","3","Civil Society Organization Registration and Oversight Reform","easing the establishment / registration of CSOs and ensuring adequate (not burdensome) oversight.",""],[1,"235","4","Civil Society Self-Regulation and Code of Conduct Framework","Develop self-regulatory mechanisms with clearly defined quality standards or a \"code of conduct\" to ensure that civil society organizations are well man- aged, accountable and their activities are well conceived, effective and attuned to the needs of Afghans, with governance models drawn from international best practice.",""],[1,"235","6","Independent Certification Bodies for Civil Society Organizations","Establish independent certification bodies for civil society organizations that are recognized by Government, the private sector, donor agencies and civil society while introducing the associated capacity building services required to achieve certification.",""],[1,"236","14","Public-Private Partnership Development Mechanism","Public-Private Partnerships are used to aid social and economic development",""],[1,"236","15","Pilot Projects for New Infrastructure and Social Development Approaches","Identify and implement three pilot projects to test new approaches in areas such as power, water supply, transportation infrastructure and social develop- ment.",""],[1,"236","16","Catalogue Best Practices for Public-Private Partnerships","Catalogue best practices drawn from across ministries (especially of Ministry of Health) of genuine partnerships between public and private sectors.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"236","17","Public-Private Partnership Programs for Social Services","Develop programs of public-private partnership that would improve health, education, drug demand reduction",""],[1,"236","31","Legal and Fiscal Incentive Framework for Private Support to Development","Create the necessary legal and fiscal incentives that actively encourage indi- vidual and corporate support for social and economic development.",""],[1,"237","2","Corporate Social Responsibility and Philanthropy Legal Reform","Improve the legal framework governing corporate social responsibility (CSR) and philanthropy including creating a Foundation law; revising NGO law to allow CSOs to generate (non-commercial) revenue to ensure self- sustainability; creating tax deductions for giving; and developing new mecha- nisms for private giving such as Zakat funds, a Diaspora fund and community foundations.",""],[1,"237","4","Business Donor Group for Corporate Social Responsibility and Philanthropy","Form a business donor's group to share best practices in corporate social responsibility and philanthropy to create more flexibility, risk-taking and imaginative practices in approaches to corporate giving, including lending good business practices to civil society.",""],[1,"237","5","CSO Vetting and CSR Awareness System","Increase trust and credibility of the civil society sector by establishing a system to vet CSOs through standards that the businesses would work with, publicizing CSO successes, and educating businesses to increase understanding of the concept of CSR.",""]],"183":[[1,"241","12","Environmental Law Enforcement Regulations","Pass enabling legislation so that the environmental law has regulations that can be enforced",""],[1,"245","12","Protected Areas and National Parks Management Plan Implementation","Management Plans and Implementation of management plans initiated for protected areas and national parks, including game reserves, wetlands and bird sanctuaries",""]],"184":[[1,"251","6","Drug Treatment and Rehabilitation Centers","Establishing centers for treatment and rehabilitation of Drugs users.",""]],"185":[[1,"256","3","Academic Journal Publication Initiative","Consider publication of an academic journal edited by the academy",""],[1,"256","4","Academy Building Construction","Construct a 7-story building for use by the academy (note: this building could also be used for higher education teaching and seminars)",""],[1,"256","5","Centre for Literature and Language Rehabilitation","Rehabilitate the Centre for Literature and Language at the academy",""],[1,"256","6","Academy Laboratory Facilities Provision","Provide laboratory facilities for the academy",""]],"186":[[1,"256","18","Editorially Independent Public Service Broadcasting Development","Development of a truly editorially independent public service broadcasting of a high standard educational radio-TV production centre",""],[1,"256","19","National Radio Studio Equipment Renovation","Renovation of the existing Radio Studios (National) equipments",""],[1,"281","19","Media Law Adoption and Implementation","Media Law to be passed and implemented by 2008",""]],"187":[[1,"258","13","Infrastructure Investment and Maintenance Policy","Develop and implement policy on infrastructure investment and maintenance",""],[1,"258","14","Rural Sub-Sector Policy Development and Implementation","Develop and implement sub-sector policies on rural roads, water, irrigation and rural energy",""],[1,"258","15","Labor-Intensive Infrastructure Investment and Maintenance Approach","Devise and implement appropriate labor-intensive approach and technologies for investment and maintenance of infrastructure",""],[1,"258","17","Social and Environmental Safeguards Standards","Establish standards including social and environmental safeguards",""],[1,"258","18","Infrastructure Program Management Capacity Enhancement","Enhance public and private sectors capacities to effectively and efficiently manage and deliver infrastructure programs",""]],"188":[[1,"260","4","National Law on Rights and Privileges of Persons with Disability","Approve the new National Law on Rights and Privileges of the Persons with Disability",""],[1,"260","7","National Disability Terms Book Development and Dissemination","Develop and circulate the National Disability Terms Book",""],[1,"260","8","National Disability Referral Guide Development and Dissemination","Develop and circulate National Disability Referral Guide",""],[1,"262","14","Alignment of the National Action Plan on Disability with the Social Protection Sector Strategy","Adjust the National Action Plan on Disability with the ANDS Social Protection Sector Strategy",""],[1,"262","15","Survey on Poor Persons with Disabilities","Conduct the survey to collect data on poor persons with disability",""],[1,"262","16","Direct Cash Entitlements for Poor Disabled Individuals","Develop the criteria and mechanisms for distributing direct cash entitlements to the poor disabled individuals with the non-war related disability",""],[1,"262","17","Community-Based Rehabilitation Center Policy and Standards","Develop and approve the policy and standards for establishing the community based rehabilitation centers by the NGOs to support integration of disabled, drug users and other vulnerable groups",""],[1,"262","18","Rehabilitation of Disabled Persons in the BHP","Include rehabilitation of disabled in the BHP in all provinces",""],[1,"285","2","Disability Assistance and Social Integration Programme","By end-2010 increased assistance will be provided to meet the special needs of all disabled people, including their integration into society through opportunities for education, skill develop- ment and gainful employment",""],[1,"285","16","Public Sector Employment Quotas for Disabled People and Women","By end-2012/13 the Government will employ at least 3 percent of disabled and 30 percent of women within its administration",""]],"189":[[1,"260","9","Labor Market Regulation Reform","Improve labor market regulations to eliminate employer's abuses and to de- crease informal economy",""],[1,"261","1","Priority Access for Vulnerable Groups in Public Works Programs","Ensure that the most vulnerable groups will be priority for participation in the public work programs",""],[1,"261","3","Financial Market Literacy and Anti-Corruption Awareness Campaigns","Implement awareness campaigns to increase the financial market literacy of the poor and issues, laws and regulations against corruption",""],[1,"261","10","International Agreements for Migrant Worker Rights","Conclude international agreements with the neighboring and other countries to regulate the rights of the Afghanistan's migrant workers",""]],"190":[[1,"261","22","Redesign of the National Solidarity Programme and National Rural Access Programme","Redesign the NSP and the NRAP to ensure their presence in remote and poor- est provinces",""],[1,"262","4","Functional Review of the MoLSAMD","Conduct the functional review of the MoLSAMD","MoLSAMD"],[1,"262","5","MoLSAMD Capacity Building and Restructuring Plan","Prepare the Plan for capacity building and restructuring of the MoLSAMD","MoLSAMD"],[1,"262","7","Social Protection HRM and Project Information Database Computerization","Establish the data base and computerize all HRM and project information for the beneficiaries of the social protection",""],[1,"263","14","NGO Standards and Referral System for Social Protection Projects","Develop the standards for the NGOs involvement in implementation of the social protection projects and set up recognized and publish referral system",""],[1,"263","15","Alignment of Social Protection Programs with the SAARC Social Chapter","Ensure that social protection programs of line ministries will be in line with the SAARC Social Chapter",""],[1,"263","16","Social Protection Sector Strategy Monitoring Baseline Indicators","Establish the qualitative baseline indicators for monitoring of the Social Protec- tion Sector Strategy",""],[1,"263","17","Social Protection Sector Strategy Progress and Evaluation Reporting","Prepare and disseminate regular progress and evaluation report on implementation of the Social Protection Sector Strategy",""],[1,"263","21","Social Protection Project Database Development","Develop the database of all Government and donor-funded projects in the area of social protection.",""],[1,"266","9","Human Resource and Project Management Computerization","Computerize all HRM and project activities to strengthen Human Resource and Project Management",""]],"191":[[1,"269","20","Legal Framework for Constitutional Right Implementation","By Jaddi 1389 (end-2010), the legal framework required for exercise of this right provided under the constitution will be put in place, distributed to all judicial and legislative institutions, and made available to the public and, implemented.",""],[1,"269","23","Affirmative Action Law for Women's Political Participation","female participation in all Afghan governance institutions, including elected and appointed bodies and the civil service, will be strengthened by providing a specific per cent reservation of seats by enacting a law of affirmative action.",""],[1,"270","3","Electoral Commission Capacity and Fiscal Sustainability Support","The Afghanistan Independent Electoral Commission will have the high integrity, capacity and resources to undertake elections in an increasingly fiscally sustainable manner by Jaddi 1388 (end-2009), with the Government of Afghanistan contributing to the extent possible to the cost of future elections from its own resources.",""],[1,"270","6","National Civil Registry and Single Identity Document System","By Jaddi 1392 (end-2013), civil registry with a single national identity docu- ment will be established",""],[1,"270","12","Statistical Baseline and Capacity-Building Initiative","Reliable statistical baselines will be established for all quantitative benchmarks and statistical capacity built to track progress against them.",""],[1,"270","15","Political and Administrative Mapping of the Country","Government will carry out political and administrative mapping of the country with villages and gozars as basic units and, the political and administrative maps will be made available at all levels for the purpose of elections, socio- economic planning and implementation of sub-national governance policy.",""],[1,"271","6","Human Rights Treaty Compliance and Reporting Capacity Strengthening","By Jaddi 1389 (end-2010), the Government's capacity to comply with and report on its human rights treaty obligations will be strengthened",""]],"192":[[1,"278","26","Shaberghan Gas Network Renovation and Mazar-e-Sharif Gas Pipeline Extension","Renovation of Shaberghan gas network and extension of Mazar-e-sharif gas pipeline and its network",""]],"193":[[1,"267","5","Reintegration Process Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Monitoring and evaluation mechanisms for tracking the reintegration process are established",""],[1,"286","5","Return and Reintegration Program Capacity Strengthening","Government's capacity to manage and support return and reintegra- tion programs is strengthened",""],[1,"286","8","Ministry of Refugees and Repatriation Reform","By 2010, the first phase of reform within the Ministry of Refugees and Re- patriation should have been completed and inter-ministerial mechanisms for reintegration assistance should have been established and operating","Ministry of Refugees and Re- patriation"]]}});